window.FWN_PRODIGIOUSLY_AMAZING_WEAPONSMITH_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_PRODIGIOUSLY_AMAZING_WEAPONSMITH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1601,"title":"Chapter 1601 - A debt to settle (7)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","There was a time limit to the Master Servant Contract that she had with Yuan Zeyu, and furthermore it was only effective when she was alive.","If she died accidentally, then Yuan Zeyu would regain his freedom.","Hence from the angle of the greatest benefit, Yuan Zeyu should have chosen to leave the mystic region himself. However, he chose to take the risk of not being able to leave the dangerous place and to remain right here.","This friendship, Huang Yueli would not forget about it.","It was her principle to repay kindness rendered upon her and take revenge back on her foes!","She took another look deeply at Yuan Zeyu and turned around to walk towards Li Moying as she hooked her arm around his and swung, “Alright, now we can finally leave!”","Li Moying allowed the young lady to act like a spoilt child while hanging his arm as his expression seemed a little arrogantly pampered while his cool peach blossomed eyes grazed past her face, without saying a single word.","Huang Yueli felt a little strange as she turned her head to take a look at him.","“Moying, we can leave now! What’s the matter with you? Why are you in a daze?”","Li Moying’s lips curled up slightly as he gave a cold snort, “Young Miss Huang is finally all done? I see that you’re rather happy talking to other men, so much that you’ve forgotten that your own fiancée is standing right next to you!”","“Ah?” Huang Yeuli went into a blank and following that she immediately burst out into laughter, “You..... what’s the matter with you? Why are you being jealous? These are all your subordinates! I’m merely helping you to beguile them otherwise why would I spend so much effort talking to them? You’re a little too petty!”","Li Moying gave a slight hmph as he lowered his voice, seeming as though he was muttering to himself.","“Really? But there’s one here who isn’t my subordinate!”","The look which Yuan Zeyu looked towards Huang Yueli was something which he understood very clearly as a man! That fellow obviously has a crush on Huang Yueli, but he probably knew that he wasn’t worthy of her hence he used the excuse of being a Shadow Guard to stay beside Huang Yueli.","That fellow had stayed in Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region not because of his loyalty only. Only his Li’er was so retarded in this aspect which was why she had not detected the other party’s feelings.","“What?” Huang Yueli didn’t hear what he was saying as she raised her head up to question closely with purity in her crystal clear big eyes.","Li Moying gave a sigh as he caressed her delicate face and switched the topic.","“Nothing, we.... Should be going!”","When they spoke about leaving, Mo Yi and the rest all frowned.","Mo Yi said, “Master, the agreed date to reactivate the mystic region by both Sects had already passed by for more than a month and I’m assuming that no one had stayed outside to look for us. If we want to leave, then we have to try to open the entrance ourselves and that requires a huge amount of Profound Energy to support it....”","Li Moying opened his mouth calmly and cut off his words, “No matter, I have a way! Everyone just crowd around me will do.”","Under normal circumstances, Mo Yi’s would naturally not be wrong. Reactivating the mystic region required twelve ninth stage realm practitioners to work together and it wasn’t something which they were capable of.","But for Li Moying, this wasn’t the case.","As Cloudy Qilin Clan’s first even god grade genius to have passed the Qilin tablet refinement successfully, not only had he received all the inheritances in the Qilin tablet, he had also received the authority to control Violet Sun Valley fully and special privilege to enter or leave Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region as he wished.","With him around, leaving this place didn’t take any effort at all.","Indeed, with a change in Li Moying’s thoughts, Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region’s sky activated a brand new pathway.","“Let’s go!”","Li Moying held Huang Yueli’s slender waist as he led her to pass through the path first while the rest of them followed up one after another."]},{"number":1602,"title":"Chapter 1602 - A dumbass who thinks too highly of himself (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","At the present moment in the Celestial Light Sect.","The entire Sect’s entrance was filled with lights as it was bustling with excitement.","Li Lingchuan and Murong Fei each wore a set of official court dress as they stood at the front of Celestial Light Sect’s main entrance, welcoming various guests who came over to visit from many different large Sects.","Today, to Celestial Light Sect, was an extremely important day, and was the start of a brand new beginning.","Because today was the day where Li Lingchuan would be officially designated as Celestial Light Sect’s new Young Sect Master, and also the day when he got officially engaged to Murong Fei!","This was the day when Li Lingchuan felt flushed with success.","He dressed up in his best attire and he was high spirited as he stood at the front of the mountain entrance, filled with great aspiration.","Almost all those large powerhouses within South Sky Region had all received Celestial Light Sect’s invitation card, inviting them to witness the birth of their new Young Sect Master.","Those guests were headed over as spectators were full of praises and congratulations when they saw Li Lingchuan, almost sending him to heaven!","“Mister Li... aiyoh, wrong, it’s Young Sect Master Li! Congratulations, congratulations! I knew long ago that you have a fortunate life ahead and your innate talent is the top within South Sky Region so you’d definitely come out with big achievements in future! Within such a short time, you’ve already become the Young Sect Master!”","“Isn’t that so? Mister Li is South Sky Region’s first class super genius and what’s rarer is that his moral standing, courage and insight are all first rated too. I’ve always felt that it’s a waste of talent for Young Sect Master Li to only be a direct disciple. Only the position of Young Sect Master is worthy of you! Indeed, you’ve finally become Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master eventually!”","“Sect Master Murong has great insight, to be able to tell that Young Sect Master Li’s ability and character are excellent, and he’s able to take on huge responsibility! Not only had he passed on the position of Young Sect Master to you, he’s also married his eldest daughter to you as well! Eldest Miss Murong is the number one beauty among our South Sky Region, the number one talented young lady! Even she fancies Young Sect Master Li, it’s obvious what kind of potential and person Young Sect Master is!”","“Congratulations to Young Sect Master Li for the double happiness!”","“That’s right, double happiness! Congratulations!”","Peals of praise kept on coming, making Li Lingchuan extremely comfortable as he was elated.","Especially when he recalled the first time when Li Moying had been designated to be the Young Sect Master, although the guests were much more than now, but most of them had a gloomy look as they came and went by quickly, totally not flattering Li Moying at all.","Li Lingchuan naturally assumed that under this comparison, of course he Li Lingchuan’s character had gained the approval of everyone! His potential... apparently wasn’t any worse off than Li Moying!","Of course, there was no way that he would find out that the reason as to why those guests didn’t flatter Li Moying, one of it was because Li Moying’s character was just too cold and no one dared to be rash in front of him.","Another reason was because Li Moying’s innate talent was just too abnormal! The minute many presidents from those powerhouses thought of the fact that for the next several hundreds or even thousands of years, they would be suppressed by that demonic grade genius over their heads and that their own Sects would never be able to be known to the world, how would their feelings.... Possibly get lifted up! Some of them couldn’t even be bothered to come out with polite words.","In comparison, Li Lingchuan wasn’t much of a threat in various powerhouses’ eyes.","To the extent that, in front of a gem like Li Moying only made him especially useless, no different from a dumbass.","But unfortunately, this dumbass was still immensely pleased with himself.","As everyone found him laughable, so they wouldn’t be stingy with a few words of flattering.","Since nice words don’t require any money so they could ridicule him all they wanted behind his back and Li Lingchuan would never find out!"]},{"number":1603,"title":"Chapter 1603 - A dumbass who thinks too highly of himself (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Right after the bunch of Sect Masters and Elders from other large Sects had exchanged polite greetings with Li Lingchuan, the minute they walked into the door, their faces indeed took a change immediately.","They took a quick glance around and couldn’t help but gathered together to ridicule him.","“Look at the conceited and arrogant look from that vile character, all of us are the Elders from large Sects but he doesn’t even bother to look at us in the eye, how could he do that? Did he really think that having the position of Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master meant that he was really Li Moying?”","“Isn’t that so? Li Lingchuan didn’t think that he is Li Moying, he just feels that he’s much more incredible than Li Moying! I really wonder where his confidence came from!”","“But this is a great thing! Originally I thought that the Sects in South Sky Region could only continue breathing under Celestial Light Sect but whoever knew that Li Moying actually got into an accident while on an experience learning trip in the mystic region! Now that this dumbass Li Lingchuan is taking over the position, it’s really a great help from the heavens!”","“Haha, you’re right! Only Li Moying has such excellent innate talent. Although he’s not my Sect’s disciple but his demise still made some people sigh.....”","“If I had a say in it, it’s you who’s too naïve! I heard the rumors around the world that Li Moying’s death has something to do with Li Lingchuan! It was said that Li Lingchuan had plotted against his own Senior Brother, causing him to die in the mystic region!”","“What? There’s actually such a thing?? How could that be possible?? Where did you hear that from?”","“There’s quite a number of people who heard of this! It’s rumoured that this time it was Celestial Light Sect and West Sky Region’s Green Clouds Sect entering the mystic region for experience learning together and Green Clouds Sect’s disciples went around spreading these. Even West Sky Region’s large Sects all know about this rumour...”","“Heavens! If it’s really true, that would be too scary! Even plotting against his own Senior Brother, that’s an intolerable behaviour! Is Murong De getting foolish as he grows old? How could he allow such a thing that is worse than a beast to take on the position of Young Sect Master and even marry his own eldest daughter to him!”","“So that’s why they say Celestial Light Sect is finished.... It really matches the saying that ‘Fortune rests in the east of the river for thirty years but turns to the west after thirty years pass’ 1 ...”","Similar rumours were heard around every corner of Celestial Light Sect.","The guests from other Sects who were spreading the rumours mostly avoided Li Lingchuan himself, but in front of other Celestial Light Sect’s ordinary disciples, they had nothing to fear.","Because Li Lingchuan wasn’t Li Moying!","When Li Moying was Young Sect Master, he had absolute prestige in Celestial Light Sect. If anyone were to talk bad about him in the Sect, it would immediately cause an uproar by the masses of the disciples, invoking a group fight.","But now that there were so many guests from other sects who gossiped about Li Lingchuan’s unpleasant talk unbridledly, yet no one was upset over this.","On the contrary, Celestial Light Sect’s disciples secretly gazed towards Li Lingchuan’s direction as a sliver of hatred flashed past their eyes.","Regarding the rumour of Li Lingchuan causing Li Moying’s death, they naturally had heard of it.","Because there were quite a number of direct disciples present and they had heard the truth when Luo Jiyun said it out.","Although they didn’t dare to offend Li Lingchuan, and they didn’t debate the truth with him in front of the mystic region’s entrance but they had spread the rumour under the tables by quite a bit.","Although none of them were the witness, but compared to Luo Jiyun and Li Lingchuan’s usual character, everyone felt that Luo Jiyun’s words were apparently more convincing.","Moreover speaking, Li Moying’s potential was clear for all to see. Just how powerful he was, was something which Celestial Light Sect’s disciples had all experienced. Even his fiancée Bai Ruoli was also a first class talented lady."]},{"number":1604,"title":"Chapter 1604 - A dumbass who thinks too highly of himself (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The two of them joined hands and easily allowed Leng Yi Feng to kill him so easily? Wasn’t that a comedy? It’s just an unbelievable story!","Li Lingchuan on the other hand, because he was a disciple of their Sect, so there were many ways which he could come out with to hoodwink Li Moying, thereby successfully plotting against him!","Li Lingchuan’s character was originally arrogant and cold blooded, with a look of hatred to exact revenge hence he wasn’t exactly able to capture the hearts of those in Celestial Light Sect. Now with such a rumour, there was a ninety nine percent of the masses of disciples going against him!","But no one could do anything about him at all.","Right after Li Moying’s death, Murong De knew that the possibility of Celestial Light Sect becoming Soaring Heavens Continent’s first class powerhouse no longer existed hence he had no heart to manage the Sect’s affairs therefore he passed the authority over to Li Lingchuan.","With absolute authority in Li Lingchuan’s hands, he started to suppress those people who dared to oppose him. He also had Murong Fei to stand up for him, so if any disciple dared to say anything bad about him, they would suffer from an insane level of revenge!","“Sigh, today is Young Sect Master’s coronation day, it really makes me feel that there’s nothing left to live for! Are we going to let such a despicable villain reign over our heads forever?!” Someone shot a furious look towards Li Lingchuan’s back as he couldn’t help but grumbled angrily.","“Hush... are you mad! How dare you even say such things! Guests from other sects can comment.... Young Sect Master, but we can’t! Have you forgotten about what happened to those people like Su Qingyue and the others who had once followed Bai Ruoli, what has happened to them now? Don’t tell me you want to end up like them?”","The former had a shock as he recalled something and his expression turned steely green and immediately shut his mouth, not daring to speak a single word more.","A vile character like Li Lingchuan didn’t have abilities like Li Moying and he couldn’t even be compared to Li Moying when handling the Sect’s affairs. But when he exacted revenge, his had many different ways of doing so.","Like those people who came from Celestial Light Academy, they were merely Celestial Light Sect’s ordinary disciples and didn’t dare to discuss about Li Lingchuan’s matter. But only because they had once stayed in the same academy as Li Moying and were acquainted to Huang Yueli, hence they suffered the most severe revenge.","Especially for Su Qingyue and the others, they were directly sent to the most dangerous Demonic Ore Cave for mining.","Demonic Ore Cave had abundant Fantasy Eye Demonic Rock and each piece of it was priceless. But these kinds of rocks itself had its own spiritual nature and would form a special kind of demonic tone in the cave, to cause confusion onto those practitioners’ soul trace and consciousness who entered the Demonic Ore Cave.","In the past, those practitioners who entered the Demonic Ore Cave to mine had willingly accepted the missions and most of them were inner or even direct disciples who thought that under the provocation of the demonic tone, it might lead to a better method of cultivation. In order to seek a breakthrough in their bottlenecks, they proactively went ahead with this.","But now, Li Lingchuan had coerced Su Qingyue and the others to mine in the Demonic Ore Cave from day to night.","These people originally had ordinary innate talents and their cultivation base was the lowest in the entire Celestial Light Sect. They had been shut in the Demonic Ore Cave for a long time hence quite a number of them had already gone insane.","There were often other Celestial Light Sect’s disciples who passed by the Demonic Ore Cave and hearing those peals of miserable shrieks, it sounded extremely horrifying.","For a moment, Li Lingchuan’s method of killing the chickens to warn the monkey was effective and in an instant, it lessened the number of people who went against him.","All of Celestial Light Sect’s disciples didn’t dare to voice out their displeasures and could only watch Li Lingchuan hugging Murong Fei with an extremely conceited and complacent look. They were suffocated by this so much that they were almost going to sustain an internal injury!","Everyone’s inner hearts were sighing with sorrow, why had Li Moying been harmed by this kind of despicable and shameless thing!","Could it be true that good men could not live for long whereas scourges reigned for a millennium?","Heaven was really unjust!"]},{"number":1605,"title":"Chapter 1605 - A dumbass who thinks too highly of himself (4)","paragraphs":["The process of welcoming guests lasted for an entire morning","At midday, the coronation of Young Sect Master and engagement ceremony was held right in front of the public square in front of Celestial Light Sect’s main door, as it was about to start.","With the support of Murong Fei, Murong De walked up the stage slowly.","The entire public square quietened down.","“Distinguished guests from various powerhouses in South Sky Region and disciples of Celestial Light Sect, it’s an honour to have invited all of you here. I believe that everyone knows that today is an extremely important date to us Celestial Light Sect. From today onwards, our Sect will have a successor and my daughter Murong Fei, has a man who she can entrust her life to.”","Murong De’s gaze brushed past Li Lingchuan and Murong Fei who were standing beside him as he opened his mouth to speak ruefully.","He had naturally valued Li Moying much more, no matter if it was for Young Sect Master or his son-in-law, it was Li Moying who was much more dependable. But now he had no other choices.","Li Lingchuan seemed to have seen through his thoughts as he took a step upwards and said, “Master please be assured. This disciple will never let down your hopes and valuation, and will lead Celestial Light Sect to new heights! I will also let Fei’er become the most fortunate and glorious lady in the entire South Sky Region!”","Murong Fei’s lips immediately surfaced a smile.","To receive a confession so openly, naturally was a very glamorous matter.","Especially before this, it had always been her to stick to Li Moying. Not to mention being affectionate to openly, he simply just treated her as air.","Now that Li Lingchuan had been so attentive towards her, it had satisfied her vanity and adding on to the considerations of reality benefits, she immediately casted Li Moying behind her.","When Murong De heard that, he nodded as a praiseful look appeared in his eyes, “En, not bad, this Master naturally believes in you! But in terms of cultivation, you need to put more effort into it, to get closer to your Eldest Senior Brother who had already passed on.”","When Li Lingchuan heard these words, his expression stiffened a little and he nodded his head a little while later, “Yes, I will obey Master’s teachings!”","He had thought that he had already successfully brainwashed this old man completely! But he had not imagined that his heart was still longing for Li Moying! He even dared to compare him against Li Moying!","Could it be that he was so incomparable to Li Moying, even if that fellow was already dead but yet he could only live under his shadow?","But no matter how much Murong De longed for Li Moying was totally useless!","Just like those ordinary disciples, there was no meaning in opposing him becoming Young Sect Master!","Because there was no way a dead person.... could possibly be revived!","There were many practitioners from other Sects who heard the conversation on the stage and they exchanged glances as they started applauding together.","But secretly, they started to engage in commentaries softly.","“What’s going on? What do you guys say.... Does Sect Master Murong know or not, about Li Lingchuan causing Li Moying’s death?”","“I think, he probably doesn’t know much. Li Lingchuan is not an idiot so he definitely wouldn’t let this news emit to his ears! But for Murong De to not know about this completely without a single doubt, I don’t believe it at all! After all, he had been a Sect Master for several hundreds of years so how could he be that silly!”","“Then why did he still.....”","“That’s easy to understand! If you were in his position, you probably could only do this as well! Li Lingchuan’s innate talent, although compared to Li Moying, he’s a complete trash but among the talents in South Sky Region, he is still one of the top few. He has the highest innate talent and ability in the current Celestial Light Sect! What else could Old Man Murong do? Just act as if you don’t know a thing, as long as you don’t expose him directly, that will do!"]},{"number":1606,"title":"Chapter 1606 - Extreme joy turns to sorrow (1)","paragraphs":["“Tsk tsk, listen to what you said, I really feel indignant for Li Moying! When he was Young Sect Master, just how much benefits had he obtained for Celestial Light Sect? How many tournaments had he won? In the end?”","“Don’t say Old Man Murong don’t remember him, just look at that Eldest Miss Murong! In the past, she was so smitten towards Li Moying until even outsiders like us were touched by it. But now he had just died for how long? She can’t wait to remarry!”","“Sigh, this kind of woman... no wonder Li Moying doesn’t fancy her!”","While everyone was chipping it, the coronation ceremony had officially begun.","Murong De stood in the middle of the stage as he recited an entire page of incantation, the rough meaning was to report Celestial Light Sect’s situation to those ancestors and seniors who had already passed on.","After he finished reciting, he beckoned towards Li Lingchuan.","Li Lingchuan immediately showed a look of joy as he hurriedly took quick steps towards Murong De and knelt down.","Murong De was looking at him intently as he opened his mouth slowly, Lingchuan, Celestial Light Sect’s future is now entrusted into your hands so you must cultivate hard, regulating yourself strictly without any laziness.”","“Yes, Master please be assured!” Li Lingchuan replied.","His heart was beating fast as he had reached the limit of excitement.","For the past ten over years, he had schemed various times and even doing many despicable things, even colluding with other Sect’s practitioners to murder his own Senior Brother. All these were just for this moment!","His motive was finally going to be accomplished!","Murong De’s voice rang from above his head, “This Sect Master announce that direct disciple Li Lingchuan is now officially Celestial Light Sect’s two hundred and fifty third....”","“Wait! I don’t agree!”","An icy cold voice suddenly rang from the direction of the mountain entrance, interrupting Murong De’s words.","Everyone present was all dazed as they didn’t expect anyone to open their mouths to talk at this moment!","Don’t think that they were in an intense discussion privately earlier. The minute Murong De started off the ceremony officially, everyone immediately shut their mouths.","The coronation ceremony officially started and for such a solemn occasion like that, who dared to casually butt in? This was an impolite action and that was simply a clear provocation towards the Celestial Light Sect! Anyone with a bit of brains would never do such a thing.","Murong De’s face revealed an unpleasant look and the movements of his hand paused as he turned back towards the entrance and spoke out sharply, “Who dares to interrupt Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master’s coronation ceremony? How dare you! What audacity!”","The others also started to bustle as they all looked out towards the entrance.","Only Li Lingchuan who was kneeling on the ground, upon hearing this voice, made his brain went “buzz”!","This voice.... this voice.....was just.. was just too alike!","Could it be that, that man had suddenly came back to life??","Li Lingchuan’s heart pounded wildly but he immediately convinced himself, “Impossible, this is just impossible! It must be my misperception! It must be because I’m usually too afraid of Li Moying so I’m having this hallucination! Dead people cannot come back to life, how could I even scare myself like that?”","Thinking of this, he too turned his head back as he cried out sharply towards the direction of the entrance, “Who is that? How dare you play punk at Celestial Light Sect! And even dare to deceive us! Still not showing yourself quickly!”","“Li Lingchuan, who gave you the guts... to talk to yours truly like that?”","A frigidly cold but magnetic voice rang once again as it slowly floated in from the entrance."]},{"number":1607,"title":"Chapter 1607 - Extreme joy turns to sorrow (2)","paragraphs":["Earlier when that person spoke for the first time, it was a few mere words and many of them had not reacted.","But now he had spoken, a strange familiarity rang among everyone’s ears.","Momentarily, everyone was stunned as they exchanged glances and all they could see were shock and surprise in one another’s eyes!","Everyone had the same thoughts in their minds: What the, this is just too.... too ridiculous? Could it be that Li Moying’s departed spirit is back to Celestial Light Sect to demand vengeance for his grievances?? This was simply seeing a ghost alive!","Whereas at this moment, a powerful thunder attributed Profound Energy expanded from the mountain entrance’s position. This Profound Energy came in the form of a lofty scale as it caused surging waves with an unequalled overbearing might, as though a heavy hammer knocking on to everyone’s chests!","Those disciples with slightly weaker cultivations immediately turned green as their chests felt a surging turbulence.","Everyone present had a change of expression as they had an unbelievable guess in their minds! They subconsciously split up in the middle to leave out a path from the mountain entrance.","A tall lanky figure walked in slowly from the entrance.","His speed wasn’t very fast but every step was steady and firm, emitting a powerful Profound Energy aura, making him appear as though he was a majestic tall mountain in everyone’s eyes.","Everyone’s gazes fell upon his face.","Following that, everyone’s mouth opened wide as their eyes popped out from their eye sockets in a dazed look, totally unable to say a word.","“Li.... Li Moying??”","Murong De was the first to regain his senses as he opened his mouth in disbelief.","That outstanding, handsome look on that perfectly featured face had no flaw on it. His imposing manner was strong and he was a man with excellent abilities which no one present could even recognise wrongly!","Li Moying... South Sky Region’s first genius in the long history, Li Moying!","Celestial Light Sect’s once Young Sect Master Li Moying!","Only he had such peerless handsome looks, and only he had such unparalleled aura! It was enough to make everyone present, bow down and submit to him uncontrollably!","This was the genuine persona Li Moying himself! Not some grieved spirit, but a living man!","As the Profound Energy fluctuations emitting from him was too strong, even those who stood very far away from him could sense that pressurizing suffocation which was not something that an incomplete spirit could achieve?","Murong De looked blankly at his own eldest disciple walking nearer and he didn’t manage to regain his senses in time.","“You.... you... how did you.....”","Li Moying had not appeared alone. By his side stood Huang Yueli who was dressed in a white dress with delicate embroidered flowers and when the two of them stood next to each other, the impeccable image of a talented man and a beautiful lady made them look like the perfect couple.","As for those Shadow Guards who had disappeared in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region, all of them reappeared as they followed behind him.","Li Moying clutched Huang Yueli’s hand as he looked straight and walked towards Murong De. After he stopped, he opened his mouth and spoke out coldly.","“Master, how have you been.... I know that you’re anxious to find a new successor for the Sect but unfortunately, I’m not dead yet! So this so-called coronation ceremony, is merely a joke!”","Murong De stared at him as his mouth opened wide, “But, but... aren’t you already... haven’t you already fallen in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region.... No, gone missing! I personally led men to search for you around the surroundings for a few days but we didn’t even catch a glimpse of your shadow! Now that the mystic region has already closed for such a long time... how is it possible for you to leave that place by yourself?”"]},{"number":1608,"title":"Chapter 1608 - Extreme joy turns to sorrow (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Li Moying’s lips curled up which seemed like a smile but not exactly one.","However, beneath his eyes was a chilly murderous intent which made anyone who saw him born fear in their hearts!","Even an established ninth stage realm practitioner like Murong De, when meeting against his sight, couldn’t help but have his hair stood up on its ends.","Li Moying said coldly, “What’s the matter? Could it be that Master had assumed that since the mystic region is shut, then there’s really no way to come out? As long as I want to, I’d naturally have a way to do so!”","“But... that’s the ancient mystic region! Our two Sects with so many ninth stage realm Elders, spending so much Profound Energy together before we could barely activate the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region’s entrance. Moreover it can only be opened at a special designated timing.. how could you possibly.....”","Li Moying didn’t reply, merely casting his gaze towards Li Lingchuan who was by the side.","At this present moment, Li Lingchuan was already frightened out of his wits as his face turned as white as paper. Sweat kept dripping down from his forehead and his body kept on trembling uncontrollably.","Never in his wildest dreams had he expected that Li Moying had actually... actually left the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region alive!","But how was this possible?","He had personally witnessed Li Moying pursuing Huang Yueli and had directly jumped down that cliff! The bottom of the cliff was filled with high levelled magical beasts so no matter how strong Li Moying was, he absolutely could not have survived under the attack of so many high levelled magical beasts!","Moreover speaking, even if Li Moying’s luck was really good and had not been eaten alive by those magical beasts, but it wasn’t possible for him to use his own strength to activate the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region by himself?","No matter how Li Lingchuan thought, there was no way he could understand what on earth was going on.","But this fascinating thing had already happened right now!","“Li Lingchuan.....” Li Moying swept an indifferent glance at him as he slowly spoke out, “You don’t seem very happy to see me come back? What are you afraid of? Have you not thought of the possibility... that I could still return alive?”","Li Lingchuan’s face turned deadly white but he said, “El... Eldest Senior Brother, what joke... are you cracking? How could I possibly not be happy? You’re able to come back peacefully so this is something which we Celestial Light Sect should celebrate about, I... of course I’m happy.”","He forcibly curled up his lips as he braced himself to say these words.","At the same time, his thoughts swiftly turned in his mind, continuing to think if there was any way to whitewash himself, or some method which would allow him to escape from Li Moying’s hands.","However, he was in a fluster and couldn’t think of any ideas at all.","Li Moying’s immense Profound Energy aura had securely locked onto him and under such a strong imposing presence enveloping him, as long as he moved an inch, he would definitely suffer from Li Moying’s Profound Energy’s restraint.","Li Moying laughed coldly, “Really? Junior Brother Li really knows how to play dumb! Did you think I’ve got amnesia? That day in Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region’s core region, you made a move towards me and my fiancée and attempted to push me down the cliff, these are things which had barely happened just slightly over a month ago!”","“No, it’s not like that.... Eldest Senior Brother, you’ve mistaken. Things are not what you think it is, listen to my explanation.....”","Li Lingchuan’s face was deadly pale as he kept on shaking his head vigorously.","Although he was anxious, but he instinctively knew that if he absolutely could not admit to doing such things, to verify that he had done such a crime!","Otherwise there was no doubt that he would end up dead today! Li Moying was never soft handed when he killed someone.","If he could find a reason to get over this and refuted Li Moying’s accusation, even if Li Moying wanted to kill him, Murong De would absolutely not ignore this."]},{"number":1609,"title":"Chapter 1609 - Extreme joy turns to sorrow (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Li Lingchuan’s thoughts flew swiftly about in his mind when a light suddenly lit up.","“Eldest Senior Brother, you’ve really mistaken! That day by the side of the cliff, I absolutely wasn’t trying to harm you, but to aid you! While I was in the mystic region going on my experience learning, I accidentally heard that Leng Yi Feng was going to deal you with a deadly move so in order to save you, I rushed over! Just as we were crossing hands at the cliff, Eldest Senior Brother you suddenly appeared hence you’ve misunderstood.....”","His words sounded apparently right but were actually wrong. He thought that since no one actually saw the true scenario and Leng Yi Feng had already died, Murong Fei was just like a grasshopper like him hanging on the same thread, so as long as he denied it all the way, who could expose him?","His words had just fallen when Li Moying’s murderous intent became even fiercer, apparently angered by his shameless agitation as his fingers moved and he had the intent to kill him immediately!","However right at this moment, from his back, a figure suddenly scurried out as he pointed at Li Lingchuan’s nose, swearing and cursing at him.","“You.. simply turning black into white, I’ve never seen such a shameless scum like you before!”","After seeing that suddenly popped out figure clearly, everyone went into a commotion yet again.","“Hmmm... this is Sect Master Murong’s other direct disciple, called Luo what again?”","“He’s Luo Jiyun!”","“Right, right, right, that’s him! Didn’t they say that he had also died in that mystic region’s experience learning trip? How did he also come back to life?”","“Looks like there’s indeed something suspicious in this matter. Celestial Light Sect’s water.... Is really deep!”","Luo Jiyun originally didn’t wanted to interrupt his Eldest Senior Brother but on seeing Li Moying almost wanting to murder someone, he couldn’t hold himself back.","It wasn’t that his ill-timed saintliness was acting up to stop Li Moying from killing him, but he was afraid that if Li Moying had a disagreement and made a move, then it would really make Li Lingchuan’s lie become the truth.","He knew that Li Moying couldn’t be bothered to talk with this kind of scum and didn’t bother about his reputation among the ordinary practitioners but he, Luo Jiyun, minded that very much! His own Senior Brother was so suave and awesome, how could he possibly allow this kind of villain to splash dirty water onto him? He must expose Li Lingchuan’s shameless filthy mouth!","Luo Jiyun suddenly popped out and Li Moying was worried that he might injure him so his action took a pause.","“What are you doing out here for?”","Luo Jiyun said loudly, “Eldest Senior Brother, I’ve had enough of Li Lingchuan that hypocritical villain so just let me finish my words!”","He turned towards Li Lingchuan, “Li Lingchuan, in the past I have still treated you as my senior brother. Occasionally those small little tricks which you plotted to scheme Eldest Senior Brother, I’d only treated those as you were acting in a moment of folly hence I didn’t complain about you in front of Master. But you actually colluded with outside people and almost got Eldest Senior Brother killed, you’re simply shameless to the extreme!”","“That day’s matters, did you really think that it’s done real secretively? There’s no witness? Unfortunately, I am not dead and is still alive and kicking and I’ve witnessed everything that had happened that day! Let’s put aside that fact that you and Leng Yi Feng colluded together to harm Eldest Senior Brother, you even used me to threaten Sister-in-law and coerced her to be together with Leng Yi Feng!”","Luo Jiyun spoke frankly with assurance, explaining in detail what had happened.","Following his description, the public square’s discussion got louder and louder.","There was a huge disparity between both their sayings and evidently, Li Lingchuan had just tried to brushed past this by giving vague descriptions without any elaboration whereas Luo Jiyun was able to speak out each single detail clearly, explaining the cause and effect clearly. So anyone with a bit of judgement would be able to tell who had a higher possibility of speaking the truth.","“Heavens, so the rumour is actually true! Li Lingchuan had really dealt his own Senior Brother a deadly blow, just because of the position of Young Sect Master?”"]},{"number":1610,"title":"Chapter 1610 - Extreme joy turns to sorrow (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“This is really the greatest gossip ever! Li Lingchuan actually did something so disgraceful, even daring to scheme his own Senior Brother. It seems that Celestial Light Sect is absolutely going to have their reputation going down the drain this time round!”","“Isn’t that so? Celestial Light Sect had always been South Sky Region’s major powerhouses’ leader and is usually almighty, but whoever knew that this time round they created such a scandal like this. Both parties actually had a confrontation in front of so many strongholds. Tsk tsk, I think it won’t take a few days before this scandal is going to revolve around the entire Soaring Heavens Continent!”","“This is really going to be bustling!”","Various guests from those major Sects were roaring with excitement as they pricked up their ears while gloating over the misfortune.","Murong De was shaking all over from this piece of news!","Even though he had subconsciously considered this possibility, but he still wasn’t willing to believe that such a thing could really happen!","“Jiyun.... You.. what you said, is it the truth? You must report the truth and not take any sides! Is it really your Second Senior Brother who harmed Eldest Senior Brother?”","Luo Jiyun replied bitterly, “Master, I’m not siding anyone! What I said is the entire truth! I can swear to heaven that if I’ve lied in any way, may I be struck by lightning!”","Murong De turned his vision towards Li Lingchuan.","Li Lingchuan’s heart thumped hard and he clenched his teeth and continued denying, “You still dare to say you’re not taking any sides? You and Li Moying are on good terms and had always excluded me. This is an open secret within Celestial Light Sect, which disciple doesn’t know about this? Why are you putting up an act? According to what you say, I’m the one who harmed Eldest Senior Brother then will everyone please judge this reasonably. Based on my cultivation, how could I possibly harm Eldest Senior Brother? Even if it was a sneak attack, there’s no way I could do anything to him!”","Usually, Li Lingchuan would never admit that Li Moying’s ability was much stronger than his!","But now in front of so many people trying to whitewash himself, he could only admit to this fact through his clenched teeth.","When he said these words out, he sensed that he seemed to have been slapped by someone, which made him feel extremely embarrassed.","What made him even more embarrassed was that when he said that, no one actually casted any doubts towards his ability as everyone deeply felt that what he said was reasonable as they all started to nod their heads.","“Isn’t that so? The disparity between the two of their abilities are just too far apart! Li Lingchuan probably can’t even take one move from Li Moying!”","“A genius like Li Moying, even if it was Li Lingchuan and Leng Yi Feng added together, could not possibly harm him! This matter indeed sounds a little too ridiculous!”","“Could Luo Jiyun really have exaggerated the entire matter?”","A small portion of people expressed the doubts in their minds and when these discussions entered everyone’s ears, not only did Li Lingchuan not feel the joy of escaping death, instead he felt his face turning fiery red!","So which he had thought highly of himself during this period of time, the others were actually treating him like a joke!","In other people’s minds, he could not even be compared to one finger of Li Moying’s!","When Luo Jiyun heard the doubts, he pursed his lips and seemed as though he hesitated for a moment, but eventually, he still opened his mouth.","“Eldest Senior Brother fell for it, of course isn’t because his ability didn’t match up to you, but because.... because Murong Fei was one of his accomplices! She was the one who personally pushed Lil Sister-in-law down the cliff and Eldest Senior Brother jumped down the cliff in order to save Sister-in-law! Otherwise just based on you and Leng Yi Feng, how could you possibly have harmed Eldest Senior Brother?”","He originally wanted to leave some face for his Master Murong De, thinking of exposing Murong Fei’s crimes in private later.","But now seeing that Li Lingchuan had shamelessly continued to whitewash himself, he could only say this out."]},{"number":1611,"title":"Chapter 1611 - Extreme joy turns to sorrow (6)","paragraphs":["Chapter 1611: Extreme joy turns to sorrow (6)","When this was told, it immediately caused a brand new commotion among the crowd.","Celestial Light Sect’s scandal was getting bigger and bigger. Not only did it have to do with the fight over Young Sect Master’s authority, it even implicated the Sect Master’s daughter!","Li Lingchuan’s lies had been exposed on the spot and his expression turned extremely embarrassed.","But he quickly stabilised himself as he gritted his teeth and hissed, “You weaved your lie as though it was real! Of course there’s no such thing! This is also something that you made up! How could Third Junior Sister possibly do such a thing? Master, don’t tell me you don’t believe in me and Third Junior Sister’s character?”","Murong De was originally convinced by what Luo Jiyun said, but upon hearing such words, he started to become hesitant again.","Murong Fei was after her his most pampered eldest daughter but now she had been accused of murdering Li Moying’s fiancée in public!","Sending the gazes from the guests of various major powerhouses, Murong De’s face was almost about to fall off!","However, he wasn’t willing to accept the fact that his own daughter would do such a thing like this.","He looked at Murong Fei, “Fei’er, what exactly is going on? You really.... really didn’t do such a thing.... Right?”","“I.... Eldest Senior Brother...”","Murong Fei opened her mouth but it wasn’t to answer her father’s question, but to call out for Li Moying.","In reality, the minute Li Moying appeared in front of everyone, Murong Fei’s gaze had been fixated on him!","Not knowing if it was her misperception or what, Murong Fei felt that Li Moying’s appearance this time round seemed to be even more handsome and suave, and even more powerful and charming.... As though he had shed his mortal body and changed wholly as an unexcelled top expert’s aura appeared to be even grander and condensed than before.","To any woman, this overbearing might which belonged to the strong, when paired to that handsome looking face, was a fatal attraction.","Li Lingchuan turned his head back and upon seeing her gaze, his face turned green immediately!","There was nothing more face slapping than this!","His own fiancée had actually ignored himself by her side as she used that star studded gaze to stare at another man! Wasn’t this obviously putting on a green hat for him? Moreover, it was under the situation when so many people were around!","Indeed, the public square started to emit some jeering sounds on and off.","Li Lingchuan got even more flabbergasted as his tone was tinged with unpleasantry, Fei’er, what’s wrong with you? Haven’t you heard Master asking you a question? Quickly answer him! You’re such a kind hearted person so how could you possibly have harmed Bai Ruoli!”","Murong Fei then regained her senses, “Ughh, this... right Father, how could you possibly not even believe in me? I absolutely have not pushed Bai... Miss Bai. She had lost her footing and fell down herself and I happened to be nearby but I wasn’t able to pull her up in time... speaking of this, I indeed have some responsibility as well because I had not noticed Miss Bai’s situation then. But this is really an accident. Such a matter happening isn’t something that anyone wanted to see....”","When Li Lingchuan heard that what she said wasn’t quite bad as it was the same saying as what they had discussed. The expression on his face then smoothened a little.","Luckily, although this woman was quick to change sides and was a wanton woman but at least she still knew what was important.....","In actual fact, how could he possibly have known that Murong Fei’s soul had flown towards Li Moying once again.","The reason why she had remembered to say this was not to help Li Lingchuan whitewash himself, but was so that she could use this opportunity to get close to Li Moying once again, hence she put on this act.","After Murong De obtained the answer that he wanted to hear, he muttered softly, “Jiyun, this matter is probably a mistake.....”"]},{"number":1612,"title":"Chapter 1612 - Reputation completely ruined (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 1612: Reputation completely ruined (1)","“To say that Fei’er they all had harmed someone but there’s no evidence. And as this is a huge matter, we shouldn’t come to a conclusion so easily. If there’s really a mistake somewhere, it’s not good if we wrongly accused anyone right?”","Murong De fiddled with his beard and hesitated for a moment, “You have just come back from the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region and have all been tired out. I see quite a number of you still have injuries on you, so it’s better to hurry back and rest! Your Master I will investigate the truth in this matter to return you justice!”","Although Murong De indistinctively felt that there wasn’t something quite right with this matter, but he still chose to stand by his biological daughter’s side.","His beloved wife had passed on early, leaving just these two daughters for him.","Murong Ni had already became the Sect’s traitor and despised by everyone, so surely he could not bear to see Murong Ni becoming a murderer, right?","Luo Jiyun was so infuriated that he was shaking with anger. He had not expected that even his Master who he had always respected, had actually abused the fact to flip things around!","“This is totally not a misunderstanding! The truth is exactly as what I’ve said, what other evidence do you need?”","Murong De frowned as he felt that this disciple of his was really.... to put it in a nice way he was called frank and honest, if it was put in a bad way, it was called dense!","With so many outsider Sect’s guests around, exposing Celestial Light Sect’s internal scandal, even if what he said was the truth, what use was it to him? The entire Celestial Light Sect would have its reputation completely ruined because of this!","“Jiyun, you’re really tired, it’s better for you to go take a rest!”","Luo Jiyun was agitated and wanted to continue speaking when he heard a sweet voice coming from his back.","“Junior Brother Luo, stop arguing with Sect Master Murong, perhaps.... you might have really seen it wrongly!”","Huang Yueli had been standing right beside Li Moying listening to their argument silently, as though she was one of the audience watching the show. But now, she suddenly opened her mouth.","When Luo Jiyun heard that, he turned out abruptly as he looked at her in shock, “Lil Sister-in-law, you.....”","He wanted to say: Have you taken the wrong medicine? How could you tell a blatant lie about this kind of thing!","But his gaze shifted towards Li Moying’s icy cold face and he immediately shut his mouth.","Huang Yueli casted a glance at him and suddenly stretched out her arm to hug Li Moying’s arm and leaned against her own fiancée, giving off a sweet smile.","“I feel that Eldest Miss Murong couldn’t have possibly pushed me on purpose, after all she has no reason to do so! In the past, we thought that it was because she liked my Moying hence she went against me but today, I discovered that it was really all a misunderstanding! The one who Eldest Miss Murong really liked is Master Li!”","“Speaking of that, I haven’t congratulated Master Li and Miss Murong. Today the two of you are getting engaged and the lovers finally got married, it’s really a heavenly joyous occasion! Moying, we’ve come empty handed and haven’t prepared any gift, is it not nice of us to do this?”","Huang Yueli’s eyes were really large as she put on an obedient look while clinging next to Li Moying’s side.","Li Moying saw her innocent look and knew that she was up to no good. This young lass.... the more she looked obedient, the more ill-intentions she had.","He just switched a train of thoughts and knew exactly what Huang Yueli was planning as his eyes flashed a smile filled with adoration as he stretched his hand out to bring her into his embrace, lowering his head as he gave a light peck on her fair forehead.","“No matter, things were unexpected so it’s understandable that we didn’t bring along any gifts. At most when we get married later on, we’ll just not accept their red packet!”","Murong Fei saw their intimate gestures and her face instantly turned green with anger!"]},{"number":1613,"title":"Chapter 1613 - Reputation completely ruined (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Bai Ruoli this wretched lass... wasn’t she a little too smug!","She was actually acting so intimately in public with Eldest Senior Brother. It was simply.... too improper!","What was so great about this wretched lass, why did Eldest Senior Brother take a fancy to her?","Murong Fei was feeling stuffed, especially when she heard Li Moying say to get “married” to this wretched lass, which poked into her sensitive senses as she blurted out, “You two... you two are really going to get married??”","Huang Yueli looked at her puzzledly as she asked, “What’s so strange about that? We are originally fiancé and fiancée so it’s just a matter of time before we get married! Speaking of that, it’s all thanks to you that you didn’t manage to hold on to me at the cliff. When I fell down the cliff, I saw Moying risking his own life to jump down to save me, that made me feel really touched hence we’ve decided to hold our wedding in the near future. This is all thanks to Eldest Miss Murong’s freak accidental matchmaking so we should really thank you properly!”","When she said that, she was entirely leaning in Li Moying’s arms, putting on a cute and helpless look.","Murong Fei saw that and it simply angered her so much that it almost made her die of anger!","Why did that wretched lass not seem to die? She was even displaying the deep affection which Eldest Senior Brother had towards her!","Recalling back on how cold and distant Eldest Senior Brother treated her usually, Murong Fei felt that Huang Yueli was simply just ridiculing her!","Furthermore, Huang Yueli seemed to have guessed what she was thinking about. When Murong Fei looked towards her, she coincidentally curled up her lips, revealing a smile which was filled with provocation and ridicule.","Murong Fei originally could still barely remember her own stand and identity but after being despised so clearly, she finally lost her rationality.","She stared at Huang Yueli angrily as she clenched her teeth and said, “You... who is trying to matchmake you? I wanted you to die! Why are you still not dead yet? Don’t be too complacent and think that you can monopolise Eldest Senior Brother, sooner or later, I’ll let you die in front of me!”","When Murong Fei blurted out such words, Huang Yueli immediately opened her eyes wide with a shocked look.","“You.... what are you saying? You want me to die? Why? Don’t you like Master Li? You’re immediately going to become Mrs Li!”","Huang Yueli used all her might to step on Murong Fei’s sore spot, the words “Mrs Li” was like a sharp knife, stabbing right into Murong Fei’s chest.","She recalled just how dumb she was, why did she agree to marry Li Lingchuan! Now that Li Moying had returned, she had conveniently allowed this wretched lass to gain an advantage for nothing, and she was so angry that she had nowhere to vent her anger!","Unfortunately, Huang Yueli just had to show off right in front of her!","Murong Fei was both angry and anxious!","She stared at Huang Yueli furiously and was just about to open her mouth but in the same instance when their eyes met, Murong Fei’s mind suddenly went buzz!","For a moment, she seemed to have seen a strange glint in Huang Yueli’s eyes and it instantly looted her consciousness.","“Pei! What thing is Li Lingchuan? If it wasn’t for the fact that he has a handle onto me, would I have taken a fancy on him? Only Eldest Senior Brother is compatible with me! I’m warning you, you’d better scram from Eldest Senior Brother’s side otherwise there will be plenty of times when you will “accidentally lose your footing” from cliffs, so don’t blame me for not reminding you!”","Murong Fei had lost all her rationality as she spoke incoherently, voicing out all the malicious swearing right from the bottom of her heart!","Huang Yueli’s lips curled into a smile which wasn’t like a smile as she said in a meaningful tone, “Oh.... So that’s the case! In this way, my falling down the cliff isn’t an.... accident?”","Murong Fei then realised that she had said the wrong words as a deadly pale colour filled her entire face."]},{"number":1614,"title":"Chapter 1614 - Reputation completely ruined (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“No.. that’s not true, you’ve heard it wrongly, no... I said it wrongly.....”","She tried her best to explain but there was already no way to explain!","Earlier when she spoke out accidentally, it had already clearly explained everything!","Murong Fei’s jealousy towards Huang Yueli had already been exhibited in her speech, furthermore she kept repeatedly cursing her to go and die!","Including the fact that in her words, she had clearly mentioned letting Huang Yueli suffer from multiple “lost footing and falling down the cliff”!","If she said now that she had not intentionally pushed Huang Yueli down, no one would believe her!","Murong Fei kept on shaking her head, simply not believing that these words came out right from her own mouth! She had actually lost her own rationality to such a step!","Earlier for a moment, she only felt that she was so upset to the limit that a burst of flame was about to explode in her chest and immediately following that, her mind went blank as though she had lost her senses. By the time she regained her senses, those malicious truthful thinking had already come right out of her mouth!","This.... why did she do that?","Even though she had been trying to find ways to make that little slut die, but she had never lost herself so much to have taken such a step before?","Furthermore, it was under this kind of occasion so wasn’t this simply seeking death’s path for herself!","Murong Fei would have never thought in her wildest dream that she had been struck with Huang Yueli’s Piercing Sky Eye Technique hence losing her senses.","The public square’s guests and disciples had totally disregarded all formalities as they all couldn’t hold themselves back from talking about this matter.","“Did you all hear what Eldest Young Miss Murong said! So, she really wanted to send Young Sect Master Li’s fiancée to her death!”","“Not only thinking about it, I think she had already done it! From the meaning of her words, Mister Luo’s accusations are totally true, she’s the one who pushed Miss Bai down the cliff!”","“This woman’s heart is really too malicious, how could there be such a venomous woman? To think that I had once liked her so much, thinking that she was a talented lady with both outstanding looks and innate talent, my Senior Brother had even been secretly admiring her! Whoever knew that she’s such a hypocrite right down into her bones! It’s all an act!”","“Which way is this malicious? She’s just dumb! She actually retardedly spoke out the entire truthful thinking in her mind upon seeing Young Sect Master Li and his fiancée getting intimate! Not only had she admitted her crime, she had also indirectly proved that what Mister Luo said was the entire truth. Li Lingchuan and the others had really colluded together to work against Young Sect Master Li.....”","“Tsk tsk, speaking of this, she’s really a wanton woman. One moment she said she liked Young Sect Master Li, the next moment, she’s getting engaged to Li Ligchuan. Now that she saw Young Sect Master Li leaving the mystic region safely, she wanted to stick back to him? Hei, did she really thought all men are idiots, who can be fooled within her palms?”","Everyone’s words were filled with despise towards Murong Fei!","After all, Murong Fei’s sculpted cold and saintly image was simply too successful. She was a first class talented young lady in South Sky Region. No matter if it was in terms of background, innate talent, looks or talent, she was the first choice in every aspect. Usually she put on an almighty cool look which attracted admiration from many young talents from various Sects.","Even though everyone knew she liked Li Moying, but she held herself very well and rarely displayed actions which were too much in front of others, hence she didn’t give anyone the chance to look down on her as well.","After all, what kind of genius grade was Li Moying? A man so powerful to this extent made all people from the same gender helplessly felt jealous of him."]},{"number":1615,"title":"Chapter 1615 - Reputation completely ruined (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","A talented lady admiring him wasn’t some devaluing matter as others would only feel that it was very common!","But now, she had changed faces overnight which made her image which she had pain-stakingly built up over the years collapsed instantly!","So, Murong Fei wasn’t some aloof fairy but such a sinister and treacherous woman on the inside!","Never mind that she was so malicious, but she was still that dumb to admit whatever bad things she had done, simply retarded to the stage where no one could bear to look at her straight!","Moreover, she assumed that Li Moying was dead and was just about to marry Li Lingchuan but now that she saw Li Moying appearing once again, she immediately tried to turn back, without any aspect of a woman’s virtuousness.","This action made anyone who saw it, wanted to berate her as shameless!","Henceforth, Murong Fei’s image was completely ruined!","Murong Fei actually realised that swiftly but since she could rescind the words which she had said, and upon hearing the crowd’s whispering in the public square, sensing the disdainful gazes from the audience, her eyes blacked out and she almost fainted on the spot!","She could not understand why was it that she could be so retarded to such an extent for that instant!","Li Moying however was very clear what his own fiancée had been up to.","Earlier when Huang Yueli extended her Piercing Sky Eye Technique, he clearly sensed her Profound Energy fluctuations hence he clearly understood her plan right from the start.","His Li’er had intentionally agitated Murong Fei and after she had infuriated her to the max limit, she chose a suitable timing to use her eye technique to mess up her rationality, making her say out the words in her mind! She had dug a hole to bury herself in it!","Li Moying lowered his head and looked at Huang Yueli and coincidentally Huang Yueli also turned over to look at him.","The two of them exchanged glances and Huang Yueli smiled sweetly. That crafty and black-bellied look made Li Moying feel emotionally affected.","If it wasn’t for the fact that the occasion wasn’t suitable, he really wanted to hug and kiss her.","These two were full of tender feelings for each other as it blinded Luo Jiyun and the bunch of Shadow Guard’s dog eyes, as they all started to cough lightly while they turned their heads away.","Everything was good about following these two Masters but the only thing was the minute they had a disagreement they would torture the dogs, simply had no consideration for others at all! This made them singles feel so embarrassed!","On one hand, while this side was engaged in uninterrupted affection, on the other hand, Murong Fei’s matter wasn’t considered completed yet.","She had blurted out the words in her heart, damaging not only the fall of her own image, but it was equivalent to confessing to everyone about herself, Li Lingchuan and the others colluding together which also caused Murong De, who had been taking her side, to ruin his reputation totally.","Li Lingchuan was so angry that his face turned green while he cried out sharply, “Murong Fei, you’re simply spouting nonsense! Do you know what you’re saying? I really didn’t expect that you’re such a shameless, vicious and wanton woman, I’ve really seen you wrongly! I thought that you had unintentionally seen Sister-in-law falling down the cliff and wasn’t able to pull on to her in time! I’d not expected that it was really you who pushed her down! You’ve even deceived me! You... you’re simply too venomous!”","Li Lingchuan was simply going to cry dumb by this woman!","On seeing her reputation completely ruined in a quarter of an hour, Li Lingchuan made a decisive decision to push all the blame onto Murong Fei immediately as he tried his best to pull himself out of it.","It was impossible for him to be dragged down by this kind of brainless woman!","However Li Lingchuan was hasty in choosing a way out, only remembering to whitewash himself but he had forgotten that he and Murong Fei were on the same boat. Murong Fei had a handle on him!"]},{"number":1616,"title":"Chapter 1616 - Reputation completely ruined (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","When Murong Fei heard his words, she first went into a blank, apparently not expecting that Li Lingchuan had a change of face that quickly!","One should know that during this period of time, Li Lingchuan had been placing all his attention on her as he pampered and fawned on her, he could be regarded as a Love Sage!","If it wasn’t for this, she wouldn’t have agreed to getting engaged to Li Lingchuan in such a short span of time after assuming that Li Moying had died.","Murong Fei had thought that she had found another sentimental man who could be used by her but she had not expected that Li Lingchuan was actually making use of her instead! The minute the truth was exposed, he didn’t even hesitate to offer any deficiencies as he immediately casted her aside!","Murong Fei’s expression turned menacing, “Li Lingchuan! What do you mean by that? Are you trying to throw all the responsibilities onto me? Do you think that you are able to cast it all aside? It’s you and Leng Yi Feng, the both of you who had started planning even before we entered the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region on how to harm Eldest Senior Brother! You’d still been lying to me that you only want to murder Bai Ruoli! Did you really think that I didn’t know about that? If it wasn’t for the fact that you had seen me pushing Bai Ruoli, in order to stop you from threatening me to keep this secret, I wouldn’t marry a cruel and unscrupulous thing like you!”","Murong Fei had really pressed all her luck out!","Anyway her reputation was already at rock bottom and the matter where she harmed someone could no longer be hidden, hence she had nothing more to fear!","Li Lingchuan actually tried to hit her while she was down? Then she wouldn’t mind entering a life and death struggle with him as well!","Li Lingchuan’s expression turned uglier. He had always known that Murong Fei totally wasn’t into him. Every single time she merely ordered him around, completely different from when she acted affectionately, to the extent of offering herself to Li Moying.","But today, Murong Fei had once and again bore it all, making this “future fiancé’s” face unable to hang on any further!","In this way, there was no way that they wouldn’t tore their faces apart!","Li Lingchuan couldn’t stop himself from retorting out, “Murong Fei, who are you calling cruel and unscrupulous? It’s you who’s wanton alright? I’m threatening you? It’s plainly yourself who couldn’t wait to find another man on seeing that Li Moying might possibly be dead! I’m threatening you? Did I force you to push Bai Ruoli down the cliff? I’m telling you, if not for the fact that you’re the Eldest Young Miss of Celestial Light Sect, for such a venomous and fickle woman like you, you’re not even fit to lift my shoes for me! Would I even get engaged with you?”","Murong Fei was originally abused by him badly as her face had turned into a pig liver colour.","She had always been pursued after by numerous men so since when had she ever been scolded that directly by anyone?","Her anger got the better of her and this time round, she totally didn’t care about anything else as she stretched out her finger and pointed her trembling fingers towards Li Lingchuan.","“Li Lingchuan... don’t you take things too far! I’m telling you, the dirty things which you’ve done, I’m very clear of it all! Don’t force me to spill the beans right here!”","When Li Lingchuan heard that, his heart constricted as he was slightly scared stiff.","But changing his frame of thoughts, the handle which Murong Fei knew wasn’t that he had schemed Li Moying? Earlier he had decided not to admit it even if he was beaten to death and he had already thrown the pot over to Murong Fei so what else was he still afraid of?","He gauged that Murong Fei was merely trying to put on a bluff so he shouldn’t fall for her trick!","Li Lingchuan laughed coldly, “Don’t think that just sprouting some casual specious words and you will be able to splash dirty water onto me! I stayed upright and did righteous things! So could I possibly be scared of your nonsensical words?”","Murong Fei gritted her teeth as she looked at him and hissed a sentence out from the slits of her teeth.","“Don’t think I don’t know, Leng Yi Feng.... was stabbed to death by you!”"]},{"number":1617,"title":"Chapter 1617 - Reputation completely ruined (6)","paragraphs":["Murong Fei’s words was like a bomb, incinerating the entire public square!","“What? Leng Yi Feng?? Have I heard wrongly, the Leng Yi Feng whom Eldest Miss Murong was talking about, is the eldest disciple from Green Clouds Sect?”","“That’s right, but earlier wasn’t Luo Jiyun and the rest saying that Leng Yi Feng had colluded with Li Lingchuan and was in a cooperative relationship? Why is it that now she’s saying that Li Lingchuan had killed Leng Yi Feng??”","“I remembered that at the entrance of Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region, Li Lingchuan mentioned that Leng Yi Feng was struck dead by Li Moying when they were engaged in a battle! But now Murong Fei said this, could it be that.... there’s really something suspicious about this matter?”","“Heavens, if this is true, then something big is going to happen! Sect Master Cui from Green Clouds Sect is right here today to attend the coronation ceremony!”","Right at this moment, Green Clouds Sect’s Sect Master Cui Yuan Shan was seated in the VIP seating.","Originally after Leng Yi Feng’s death, he had also turned tables with Murong De.","Today he had appeared at this place was not because the two sects had reached a peace treaty but because Murong Ni had an affair with Fang Shaoning in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region and she actually gotten pregnant. Both Sects were reputable and since such a farce had occurred between their direct disciples, Murong Ni could only marry over to Green Clouds Sect.","Cui Yuan Shan most unwillingly headed over to discuss this matter and coincidentally he had come in time for the coronation ceremony hence he tugged his utmost displeasure to attend this event.","Whoever knew that this event gave him a shocking piece of truth!","When Cui Yuan Shan heard Murong Fei’s words, he was so agitated that he stood right up and overturned the teacups right next to him.","“Murong Fei, what did you say? Leng Yi Feng was killed by Li Lingchuan? Wasn’t it said that.... Li Moying had accidentally killed him when they were crossing hands? Speak clearly!”","Originally Cui Yuan Shan had already believed Li Lingchuan’s words because Leng Yi Feng had tried to plot against Li Moying first. Plus the fact that he was killed during a battle so no matter what, it was Leng Yi Feng at fault. Later on everyone thought that Li Moying was already dead and there was no way to seek revenge hence this matter just settled by leaving it unsettled.","But now, things had taken an unexpected turn and there was a totally new saying?","Could it be that.... he was tricked by Li Lingchuan?","Li Lingchuan had a huge change of expression as the sweat on his forehead kept on sprouting. His hands and feet were chilly as he was anxious to the maximum limit.","He had assumed that he had done it so discreetly that no one knew about it. Even if it was Li Moying himself, he wasn’t sure that when he injured Leng Yi Feng heavily, did he really kill that person!","Whoever knew that today his lies were all exposed by Murong Fei!","What was going on? How did Murong Fei find out... that he was the one who killed Leng Yi Feng?","Li Lingchuan’s heart started palpitating but he forced himself to maintain his composure. He knew that he could not reveal any flaws otherwise he would really be dead meat this time!","From his point of view, Leng family was much stickier than Li Moying by at least a hundred times!","Such an influential family strength, killing him was as easy as crushing an ant wasn’t it?","“Murong Fei don’t you go slandering me venomously! The situation then wasn’t only seen by you! Leng Yi Feng had tried to assassinate Eldest Senior Brother but in the end he was heavily struck down in one move! Later on, Leng Yi Feng used the Profound Artifact which his family had left for him but it was still decoded by Eldest Senior Brother as he was struck flying off and spitting out blood at the same time, later on losing his consciousness! Later on as there wasn’t anyone who could save him, hence he had died due to a prolonged lapse of time from excessive bleeding!”","Saying that, he turned towards Luo Jiyun, “Luo Jiyun, you were one of the witnesses then!”"]},{"number":1618,"title":"Chapter 1618 - Reputation completely ruined (7)","paragraphs":["Everyone’s gazes fell onto Luo Jiyun once again.","Luo Jiyun frowned slightly as he replied hesitantly, “This...”","Actually when he was by the side of the cliff, after Li Moying and Huang Yueli had both fallen and jumped off the cliff sequentially, he lost consciousness after that and he didn’t know when Li Lingchuan and Murong Fei left. But right before he lost consciousness, what he had seen was exactly as what Li Lingchuan had described.","His character was upright and just, and he had never lied before.","But in this case, wouldn’t it be equivalent to testifying for Li Lingchuan, to accuse that his Eldest Senior Brother had killed Leng Yi Feng?","However, not waiting for his reply, Li Lingchuan had already continued speaking, “See, Junior Brother Luo can’t say anything else right? If I’m the one who killed him, then would Luo Jiyun be so hesitant in reply? Apparently he was killed by Li Moying, that’s why he doesn’t have the cheek to say it out! Honestly speaking, as a large family’s descendant, Leng Yi Feng has many Profound Artifacts on him and just based on my cultivation.... Sect Master Cui, do you feel that I am able to kill him?”","Being asked in such a manner, Cui Yuan Shan frowned, feeling that he might possibly have gotten it wrong.","Back then in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region, the only person who had the ability to kill Leng Yi Feng was only Li Moying. Furthermore he had the motive and chance to do so!","He turned his head towards Li Moying, “Li Moying, this matter concerning my disciple Leng...”","“Wait! Sect Master Cui, don’t you believe in Li Lingchuan’s nonsense!”","When Murong Fei saw that, she couldn’t help but cried out loudly, “Li Lingchuan, did you really think that I haven’t seen anything at all? That time, you were the first to get up and Leng Yi Feng begged you for help but you saw riches which provoked evil designs hence you stabbed him to death with your dagger! You even stole his realm ring and Profound Weapons and Profound Artifacts, this is something which I’ve seen with my own eyes!”","Li Lingchuan instantly turned chilly, “You... what nonsense are you sprouting?? Don’t think that by weaving a lie like that, you’re able to divert away everyone’s attention! And that you’re able to whitewash yourself!”","Murong Fei stared at him furiously, “Why? Dare to do it but no guts to admit? Did you really think that both I and Junior Brother Luo were unconscious so no one would know about it hence you dared to kill Leng Yi Feng? In actual fact, I had regained consciousness long ago but on seeing you killing him, I could only pretend to lose consciousness! I was afraid that you would eliminate me! Actually I’ve seen every single thing that you’ve done!”","Li Lingchuan stopped her sharply, “Shut up! What nonsense are you sprouting, I don’t understand a single word of it!”","His mind went blank and his legs turned into jelly as he almost fell onto the ground!","Never in his wildest dream had he thought that his seamless plans had actually.... actually been exposed!","Furthermore, at this juncture, to be exposed by Murong Fei in front of Cui Yuan Shan!","Murong Fei had actually seen this but she actually pretended to have fainted! How was that possible?","If he had long knew that Murong Fei had grasped this handle of his, then he would absolutely not tear faces with Murong Fei so easily earlier!","But now, it was too late to say anything!","No matter how menacing Li Lingchuan’s appearance was, insisting that it was Murong Fei who was creating rumours.","But everyone present were not idiots and Cui Yuan Shan was an astute and circumspect Sect Master from a large sect so how could he possibly be cheated by this performance?","Anyone with a bit of brains was able to tell that Murong Fei had spoken so frankly and straightforwardly hence she definitely had something to support her!","“Good, very good! Extremely good!” Cui Yuan Shan’s face as deep as water as his gloomy cold gaze was fixated onto Li Lingchuan."]},{"number":1619,"title":"Chapter 1619 - Reputation completely ruined (8)","paragraphs":["Li Lingchuan shuddered as he furiously shook his head to deny the allegations.","“Cui... Sect Master Cui, you... you cannot just listen to Murong Fei’s one sided story! I didn’t... I really didn’t! That day when I regained consciousness, Leng Yi Feng was already dead! He had died due to serious injuries which he sustained from Li Moying and had nothing to do with me at all! Don’t listen to Murong Fei’s nonsense, she’s just a woman who is full of lies!”","“Hmph, I think you’re the loser who is full of lies!” Murong Fei immediately rebutted, “Weren’t you just greedy for Leng Yi Feng’s treasures on him hence you killed him so that you can take his treasures for your own? Sect Master Cui, in order to verify that what I said was correct, it’s very simple. You just need to catch him and search his realm ring, then you’d be able to see if there’s any of Leng Yi Feng’s belongings inside!”","“You.... You.....”","Li Lingchuan had an abrupt change of colours as he really didn’t expect Murong Fei to scam him in such a way!","As he was afraid of being exposed, he didn’t dare to use the treasures which Leng Yi Feng left behind but he had been carrying it around with him, preparing to find a chance to head towards Sky Emperor City to exchange for money.","If he was seriously captured and searched, then he would be exposed for sure!","Cui Yuan Shan apparently felt that it was a good idea as he nodded his head immediately, “That’s right, this Sect Master has the same sentiments!”","He was already at the verge of blowing his top and if what Murong Fei said was true, then Li Lingchuan was truly a despicable and utterly shameless villain!","After all, all practitioners held in contempt on the action of suddenly changing faces while their companions were heavily injured, then to retain the other party’s treasures for their own. No one wished for their own companions to betray and murder them while they were in the middle of experience training. Hence the minute anyone did that, that person would be condemned by all the practitioners in the whole world.","Momentarily, the audience in the public square were all furious beyond words and some even started swearing loudly.","“Li Lingchuan is just too cheap! He dared to even do such a thing like this??”","“He still has the cheek to claim Murong Fei is a wanton woman? Heh, I think the both of them, one a scum while the other one is cheap, they’re really a match made in heaven!”","“Heavens, it’s simply too shameless! He’s even a large Sect’s direct disciple and he actually did such a thing, is there any difference from being a robber?”","“Celestial Light Sect actually wants to promote such a person to become Young Sect Master, is Murong De blind or what?”","Li Lingchuan plopped down on his knees and started pleading for mercy, “Sect Master Cui, spare me... please spare my life! I really didn’t kill anyone! Yes I admit that I have taken Mister Leng’s realm ring but I absolutely didn’t kill him! I merely... merely felt that those treasures left behind in the mystic region was a huge waste, so.... so I helped him to retrieve it out...”","Cui Yuan Shan’s face had turned deep like water as his gaze was fixated onto Li Lingchuan while he spoke out coldly, “Whether it’s real or fake... after you reach Sky Emperor City, go explain to the Leng family yourself! Don’t blame this Sect Master for not reminding you that Leng family has an exclusive soul searching skill. So no matter if what you said is the truth or not, there’s absolutely no way to conceal the facts!”","Hearing that, Li Lingchuan had an abrupt change of colour as he started shaking all over!","Soul searching skill!","This ancient secret arts was something which an established powerhouse in Sky Emperor City could grasp and he had also heard rumours on it.","It required a practitioner with extremely powerful mental power to forcibly inject in his Profound Energy to read the memories of the person whose soul was being searched! Any lies under this secret arts had no way to hide!","What was most terrifying of all was that this secret arts caused a destructive damage to the practitioner’s primordial spirit."]},{"number":1620,"title":"Chapter 1620 - Ninth stage realm’s might (1)","paragraphs":["The minute Leng family’s top exponents used the soul searching skill on him, the lightest injury would be damage to his primordial spirit causing his cultivation to take drastic drop or the worse was that he could completely lose his senses, turning into a living dead! There was also the possibility of losing his life on the spot!","No matter which outcome it was, it wasn’t something which he could handle!","Moreover the minute his soul was searched, the matter where he had murdered Leng Yi Feng would be exposed and what awaited him was absolutely all kinds of cruel tortures which was worse than dying!","Li Lingchuan’s soul almost flew out as he tried his best to explain, “Sect Master Cui, I really didn’t... please let me off!”","Cui Yuan Shan’s face was icy cold as he remained unmoved.","As Leng Yi Feng had died in Green Cloud Sect’s organized experience learning, he had been under tremendous pressure from the Leng family for this period of time and the entire Sect was affected by this!","Now he had finally found the main culprit to answer to Leng family so no matter what, he would never give up on this chance!","Li Lingchuan looked at him with a staunch look so he could only turn towards Murong De and plead for mercy. He kept on kowtowing on the ground as he pleaded pitifully.","“Master, please save me! I cannot go to the Leng family, I cannot let them search my soul! The Sect had used so much effort to nurture me so surely you won’t want to see me lose my cultivation like that, right? Master, on account that we are Master-disciple, I beg you to please save me!”","Murong De lowered his head and looked at his second disciple who knelt on the ground.","Towards this disciple, he had some feelings since he had also been under him since young and he watched him growing up little by little.","However, the matter which was caused by Li Lingchuan had largely surpassed his bottom line!","He had first been exposed that because of Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master’s position, he disregarded everything and caused harm to his own Senior Brother. Immediately following that, he turned tables against Murong De’s biological daughter turning into foes to mutually frame and entrap the other. Lastly he was exposed of his greed turning into murder, killing Leng family’s descendant!","Any of these three items were enough to make any practitioner being disdained by everyone, consigned to eternal damnation!","Li Lingchuan..... today he had completely reduced Celestial Light Sect into the entire pugilist world’s laughing stock!","Celestial Light Sect had been passed on from generation to generation and had finally managed to establish some prestige, had totally been ruined today!","No matter if it was in terms of public or private, Murong De was totally unable to accept this matter.","What’s more, if he defended Li Lingchuan today, Leng family might just come over to seek revenge another day. This kind of strong powerhouse in Soaring Heavens Continents was not something that a small little Sect like them could afford to offend.","Murong De looked deeply at Li Lingchuan and he already came to an understanding in his heart.","He gave a deep sigh, “Lingchuan ah, This Master had been guiding you for so many years, that one’s character is more important than cultivation! If you can’t even become a righteous person, then what’s the point of it all no matter how high your cultivation gets? You’ve really made this Master too disappointed!”","Li Lingchuan’s heart thumped wildly, “Mas... Master... you... you can’t do this to me.....”","Murong De frowned, “You’ve created this sin yourself so you naturally need to bear the consequences. No matter what happens, you deserve it! Committing such a huge offence, This Master could only choose to place righteousness before family!”","His devotion to righteousness which inspired reverence made Li Lingchuan’s heart turn ashen.","He knew that this Master of his had always been timid and at this juncture, he would absolutely not save him!","But could it be that he was just waiting for death like that?","No, he absolutely could not accept this result! Why... Why did things turn out this way?","Today was obviously the day where he was most proud of his success!"]},{"number":1621,"title":"Chapter 1621 - Ninth stage realm’s might (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","All that he ever wanted, status, authority, beauty, were all right in front of him, but why had it just been a blink of an eye and everything had turned into bubbles popping into illusions, even pulling him into the abyss of the bottomless hell.....","Li Lingchuan’s face was utterly defeated as he sat despondently on the ground in a kneeling position.","Cui Yuan Shan gave a cold humpf and said, “What’s the matter? Done with your rubbish talk? Sect Master Murong has finally dealt with this reasonably. Not that I want to say, this kind of scum of the Sect who had dragged down the entire Sect should have been driven out long ago! Today, this Sect Master shall help you clean up your place!”","Saying that he stretched out his hand and the Profound Energy injected within viciously struck towards Li Lingchuan’s chest.","This move was tumultuous.","Anyone could tell that if Li Lingchuan was hit, he would absolutely have all his meridians shattered causing him to lay limp on the ground, just waiting to be slaughtered!","Li Lingchuan himself knew this clearer than anyone else. But a ninth stage realm practitioner’s might was not something which he could go against.","He didn’t even have the possibility to struggle and escape as his entire body was suppressed by Cui Yuan Shan’s aura, rendering him totally immovable as he could only watch with his eyes open to wait for himself to become crippled!","Just as everything thought the same thought, Li Lingchuan would be injured and brought away by Cui Yuan Shan.","Suddenly Cui Yuan Shan gave off a “Yi” sound.","Immediately following that, a burst of Profound Energy flew out from the side as it collided ferociously with Cui Yuan Shan’s Profound Energy!","A “Boom” sound reverberated and shooting sparks was seen in mid sky.","Cui Yuan Shan couldn’t help but gave a dull moan as he felt that that gust of Profound Energy was not only rich, it was also abnormally solid. It could instantly crush his own Profound Energy as his feet was pushed back by half a step before he managed to steady himself with his breathing slightly unstable.","“Sect Master Murong, what’s the meaning in this? Haven’t you agreed not to dabble in this matter? Don’t tell me you’re regretting it??”","Cui Yuan Shan hollered out exasperatedly as he gave Murong De a furious stare.","However when the two of them exchanged glances, he then discovered that Murong De’s expression was even more astonished than his.","“What’s going on?” Cui Yuan Shan frowned.","Murong De turned his indeterminate bewildered gaze onto Li Moying, “Moying, you.....”","Not only Murong de, everyone below the stage had seen it clearly. The person who obstructed Cui Yuan Shan was not Murong De, but..... Li Moying!","Cui Yuan Shan followed his gaze as he looked towards Li Moying.","“What’s the meaning? Don’t tell me the person who struck earlier.... is Li Moying?”","Cui Yuan Shan’s eyes turned wild like full moons as he deeply felt that Murong De was playing tricks on him!","After all, when he struck earlier, although he had used only twenty to thirty percent of his Profound Energy, but that was still a ninth stage realm practitioner’s strike! Ninth stage realm practitioners who advanced would all enter a stage of shedding their mortal bones. As compared to practitioners who were under ninth stage realm, there was a huge difference in their abilities. Even if it was an eighth stage realm peak practitioner, that person would not be able to take on twenty percent of his Profound Energy!","Moreover speaking, in order for him to cripple Li Lingchuan in one move, he used a heaven grade Profound Skill.","Who exactly was Li Moying?","He as South Sky Region’s, or perhaps Soaring Heavens Continent’s number one genius but he was merely a junior! Moreover his cultivation was only at the seventh stage realm.","He was invincible among the younger generation but in front of a ninth stage realm practitioner, he could barely take on a strike!","How could Li Moying possibly block a move from Cui Yuan Shan?","Cui Yuan Shan wanted to laugh loudly to express his disdainful feelings but when he turned his gaze towards the public square, he discovered that everyone’s face was filled with astonishment."]},{"number":1622,"title":"Chapter 1622 - Ninth stage realm’s might (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Cui Yuan Shan was stunned.","From the looks of it..... could it be that Murong De was not deliberately mystifying but.... he was telling the truth?","Before he could even react, Li Moying’s icy cold gaze swept past him as he opened his mouth indifferently.","“Sect Master Cui, you cannot take him away!”","Cui Yuan Shan’s face flashed past a furious look. He was an established practitioner for quite a number of years and he had never been commanded in such a way by a junior.","Unfortunately, Li Moying did it and furthermore, in such a just and forceful way.","Cui Yuan Shan replied, “Young Sect Master Li, please be clear of who you are speaking to! Li Lingchuan caused harm to my Green Clouds Sect’s eldest disciple and this is of utmost concern hence this Sect Master has the authority to take him away! Furthermore, Leng family had been investigating Leng Yi Feng’s cause of death, so this Sect Master must definitely hand this person over to them!”","Cui Yuan Shan forcibly suppressed the anger in his heart as he made an exception to explain a little more.","The main thing was because he didn’t bring along any ninth stage realm Elders and was there alone on Celestial Light Sect’s turf so he didn’t want to create any trouble.","When Li Moying heard that, there was still no expression on his face as he continued speaking, “Li Lingchuan plotted against me and my fiancée in Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region and this debt.... Cannot be forgotten! He can only be dealt with by me. Sect Master Cui.... Please return him!”","Cui Yuan Shan was shoved back by a similar reason as his face was so stuffed that it turned red.","From what he saw, the explanation that he gave earlier was already lowering his own status, giving this young junior enough face so Li Moying should just be tactful and leave the stage , respectfully allowing him to take the person away!","Whoever knew that Li Moying was actually unmoved and he even obstructed right in front of him.","He couldn’t help but flew into a rage, “Li Moying! Who do you think you’re talking to? Move aside for This Sect Master! Otherwise, I’ll capture both of you and send you over to the Leng family! Don’t forget, Leng Yi Feng’s death is connected to you as well!”","Cui Yuan Shan berated him while unhesitatingly releasing his Profound Energy from within.","A ninth stage realm top exponent’s suppression enveloped the entire public square and many practitioners present weren’t able to take it as they started shuffling backwards.","But Li Moying who was facing Cui Yuan Shan stood high and mighty as he was motionless, as though Cui Yuan Shan’s Profound Energy suppression had no effect on him at all.","Cui Yuan Shan had never met with such a thing and on seeing Li Moying behaving in an opposite reaction as what he had expected, he immediately threw up blood and retreated a little, feeling that he had lost face further he continued to unleash his Profound Energy.","This time round, even a top exponent like Murong De started feeling uncomfortable.","Li Lingchuan who knelt on the ground was throwing up blood as he bent over and curled up.","Even so, Li Moying still didn’t show any signs of discomfort. On the contrary, his lips curled upwards slightly and signs of ridicule started appearing on his face.","This expression completely infuriated Cui Yuan Shan.","“You little fellow, did you really think that you have outstanding innate talent and you can go up against an established senior? You’re simply too conceited! If you don’t move aside, then This Sect Master will not continue being polite!”","He was just about to give his fullest and seriously deal out his move to show Li Moying some colours.","But at this moment, Murong De stood in the middle to stop him as he cried out, “Sect Master Cui, misunderstanding, this is all a misunderstanding! Don’t be rash! Moying he almost died under his own junior brother’s hand and is still feeling upset over it which is inevitable hence he’s acting a little out of control not knowing what’s more important. He’s young and still ignorant so I’ll speak to him then he’d start to get over it! Sect Master Cui please don’t hold it against a junior!”"]},{"number":1623,"title":"Chapter 1623 - Ninth stage realm’s might (4)","paragraphs":["Murong De stood by the side as he looked at Li Moying, winking at him.","“Moying, aren’t you coming over to apologize to Sect Master Cui?”","Murong De now understood that Li Lingchuan could not be saved but there wasn’t much influence if he gave up on this hopeless second disciple. Now the greatest news was Li Moying had came back to life!","As long as Li Moying was around, Celestial Light Sect’s future would be boundless so even if one thousand Li Lingchuans died, there wasn’t any influence at all.","Hence when Cui Yuan Shan dabbled in the situation based on his reason to capture Li Lingchuan to hand over to Leng family, he didn’t object too violently.","But now that Li Moying was going up against Cui Yuan Shan, things were not good.","If Cui Yuan Shan exploded and heavily injured Li Moying, then that would be Celestial Light Sect’s irrevocable damage!","That was why Murong De hurriedly jumped out to ease the situation.","Cui Yuan Shan saw Murong De jumping out and thinking that he had not brought any men along, hence he could only let things go. He placed his hands behind his back and gave a cold humpf as he said, “Alright, since Sect Master Murong put it in this way, how could this Sect Master haggle with a junior? As long as Young Sect Master Li apologizes sincerely, then I can let this matter rest!”","When Murong De heard that, he winked even harder at Li Moying, so much that his eyeballs were about to drop out.","Alas, Li Moying totally ignored him as the ridicule beneath his eyes was even stronger.","“This is not a misunderstanding! This Seat has already made it clearly, Li Lingchuan.... Must die under my hands!”","Cui Yuan Shan simply did not believe what he had heard!","Under his coercive suppression, Li Moying actually remained so resolute, without any sense of wanting to step back.","“You.... must you go against this Sect Master??” Cui Yuan Shan’s face turned green.","The Profound Energy in his body had started to gather and his aura kept on increasing as the air started to be charged with an intense wind attribute Profound Energy!","If it was an ordinary seventh stage realm practitioner, he would have been lying limp on the ground. No matter how much determination he had, there was no way that he could control his own actions under such a powerful suppression.","But Li Moying merely replied indifferently, “Talking so much rubbish, either you scram or strike!”","The public square turned completely silent.","No one had expected that Li Moying actually dared to provoke the long established ninth stage realm practitioner, Cui Yuan Shan in such a way!","He... did he really want to die? Or had he gone insane?","No matter how excellent his innate talent was, there was no possibility of him being able to block a move from Cui Yuan Shan!","Now he had even incited Cui Yuan Shan to make a move, was he... in a hurry to reincarnate??","Cui Yuan Shan stared intently at Li Moying’s eyes, “Good, good, you’re very good! This Sect Master shall let you experience what is known as a genuine ninth stage realm practitioner! You must know what kind of price you must pay for provoking the strong!”","Murong De’s expression changed abruptly as he cried out sharply, “Li Moying, what nonsense are you sprouting?? Quickly shut your mouth!!”","But saying anything now was just too late.","Right after Cui Yuan Shan said three “good” words, the Profound Energy within his body started pouring out in torrents as it gathered into a wind blade striking towards Li Moying’s head!","He had been completely angered and no matter what, he was a Sect Master. To be provoked by a junior in such a way, his face had been completely lost!"]},{"number":1624,"title":"Chapter 1624 - Ninth stage realm’s might (5)","paragraphs":["If he didn’t make Li Moying pay a painful price, then where would his face be placed?","Towards Wind attributed practitioners, wind blade was an extremely ordinary Profound Skill but under the drive of a ninth stage realm’s torrential Profound Energy, the air gathered in mid-air into blade images but was extraordinarily strong as though it could tear the entire heaven and earth apart. Wind attributed energy revolved around the sharp blade bearing a devastating stance in everyone’s heart!","Wind attributed practitioners’ speed were extremely swift and it only took a flash before it was just inches away from Li Moying.","“Heavens! Li Moying is a goner!”","“Too terrifying, so this is a ninth stage realm practitioner’s potential! He could simply call upon the wind and summon rain, totally not something that ordinary people like us could imagine!”","“Finished, Li Moying he.....”","Amidst the cries, many of them were so afraid that they covered their eyes, especially for those young ladies who secretly admired Li Moying, they didn’t dare to see him being cut into half by the wind blade!","Murong De hurriedly struck out in an attempt to save him.","But his potential was originally much weaker than Cui Yuan Shan and adding on to the speed which a Wind attributed practitioner had, not to mention that Cui Yuan Shan had suddenly struck.","Under various elements, Murong De’s Profound Energy missed the wind blade and he could only watch with his eyes open at the blade which had sliced open the space as it landed onto the top of Li Moying’s head.","He drew in a breath of cold air!","However, the image which was in his mind did not appear.","Li Moying was facing an abruptly descended wind blade but he totally made no signs of attempting to evade it. In fact, he didn’t even bother to put out a defensive stance.","It was until the wind blade was right on top of his head when he moved slightly as he raised his hand up.","A blue purplish streak of lightning violently flashed, instantly attracting thunder.","A loud “BOOM” sound reverberated and the explosive sound rang above Celestial Light Sect as a bolt of lightning split opened heaven and earth, forming a line with the thunder light in Li Moying’s palm!","This bolt of lightning was simply too bright and many practitioners of weaker cultivation were blinded the moment that lightning lit up as their eyes started tearing, totally unable to see anything.","Whereas for practitioners with higher cultivations, they could only barely see that bolt of lightning which suddenly released a powerful amount of energy, clashing fiercely against Cui Yuan Shan’s wind blade.","An intense explosion sounded!","Raging wind and electric currents started to land on the public square, causing torrents of miserable shrieks.","After a moment later, the explosive repercussions then slowly subsides as those practitioners who had gone dizzy from the effect could barely pick themselves up, raising their heads to look at the situation on the stage.","Celestial Light Sect’s VIP seats had been blown away.","Amid the mayhem, Li Moying and Cui Yuan Shan were at a distance of ten meters away from each other.","Cui Yuan Shan’s condition was far from good. His face was pale and his entire face was filled with dust and ash and the protection armour which he wore was blasted into shreds with multiple wounds on his body as it kept on seeping out blood.","His eyes were wide open as he displayed an expression of disbelief as he used his finger and pointed towards Li Moying’s direction. As he did that, his entire body started trembling uncontrollably.","“You..... you, you.... how is it possible? How is this possible???”","Li Moying shot a glance at him coldly, “Why is it not possible?”","Cui Yuan Shan seemed as though he had suffered a huge blow as he started to talk incoherently, “How could you... possibly..... I am.... In ninth stage realm! How could you possibly block it... impossible!”","Li Moying’s icy cold voice was heard, “Haven’t you seen it for yourself? This is of course because.... my cultivation is also in the ninth stage realm!”"]},{"number":1625,"title":"Chapter 1625 - Ninth stage realm’s might (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Ninth stage realm??”","“What is Young Sect Master Li talking about?”","“Have I heard wrongly? Pinch me quickly!”","Hearing what Li Moying said, those practitioners who had finally started to quieten down all started to shriek as all of them felt that they had developed hallucination.","However, when they turned their gazes towards Li Moying, all of their questions were all stuffed back at their faces.","Li Moying stood there firmly as his gaze was cold and penetrating with his tall statue standing upright like a mountain as it was impenetrable.","His aura kept on increasing as his Profound Energy fluctuation which was emitted started to become stronger and stronger.....","Overbearing Profound Energy suppression enveloped the entire public square, even pushing Cui Yuan Shan’s unleashed Profound Energy back, totally suppressing him until it couldn’t be felt.","This kind of powerful and pure Profound Energy clearly answered the question, which was.... Li Moying had genuinely crossed into the line of the ninth stage realm!","Cui Yuan Shan’s pupils slightly contracted as his gaze which was fixed onto Li Moying was as though he had seen a ghost in broad daylight!","“Ninth stage realm.... it really is the ninth stage realm.....”","“Heavens! Young Sect Master Li had actually advanced into the ninth stage realm! This, this, this..... isn’t this a little too ridiculous! If I hadn’t recalled wrongly, he’s only twenty one years old this year! A twenty one year old ninth stage realm...”","“Terrifying, too terrifying! The number one top expert, Mu Chengying, in Soaring Heavens Continent then was over thirty years old when he advanced into ninth stage realm, and that was Soaring Heavens Continent’s fastest record of advancing into ninth stage realm! Looks like this record is broken by Young Sect Master Li!”","“It’s far more than broken! It has totally been shrunk by a huge chunk! How on earth did he do it??”","Public square exploded into a bustle as everyone used a mixed gaze of shock, fear and adoration as they looked at Li Moying!","Since the moment he stepped into ninth stage realm, he was no longer the so-called “genius”, but a genuine peerless top exponent! All the people present were no longer in a possibility of being put on the same level to be compared!","Not only the disciples from other Sects, even everyone in Celestial Light Sect were dazed beyond words.","“Eldest Senior Brother... Eldest Senior Brother is too..... too powerful...”","“This simply is.... too ridiculous!”","“I thought that I had already gained enough understanding on Eldest Senior Brother’s powerfulness but it’s only until now that I realised that all I’ve seen were just a tip of the iceberg.....”","“Is he still a human??”","Even Murong De was completely dazed.","As Li Moying’s Master, he should be clearest towards his own disciple’s innate talent but now he realised that this Li Moying right in front of him was someone whom he totally didn’t recognise!","He had merely just entered the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region once and only for slightly over two months but he had actually broken through two large realms consecutively! This was not using just a simple word “genius” to describe him!","Under everyone’s dumbstruck look, Li Moying inclined his head to the side as he told Mo Yi, “Go get Li Lingchuan, we should get going!”","Mo Yi hurriedly responded as he and Mo Er went up to grab hold of Li Lingchuan.","Mo Yi and Mo Er were merely at sixth stage realm cultivation and were slightly weaker than Li Lingchuan. Originally if they went up to capture him, Li Lingchuan would absolutely not wait to be captured.","But earlier after witnessing Li Moying’s astonishing ability, Li Lingchuan was so shocked that he laid limp on the ground as a smelly stench of urine flowed out from his pants, stinking the entire place!","Facing the icy cold expressionless Shadow Guards, he didn’t dare to resist against them."]},{"number":1626,"title":"Chapter 1626 - Ninth stage realm’s might (7)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Mo Yi and Mo Er didn’t use much effort as they used the Immortal Binding Rope to tie him up.","But just as they were about to drag him away, Cui Yuan Shan suddenly regained his senses.","He shot upwards like an arrow and cried out sharply towards the both of them, “Move aside! Who allowed you to snatch this person away from This Sect Master!”","Mo Yi and Mo Er were intimidated by a ninth stage realm practitioner’s Profound Energy and instantly the blood in their chest started churning, causing them to almost throw up blood but they didn’t even take a step back!","Cui Yuan Shan was exasperated and was about to strike out at them to teach them a lesson but Li Moying waved his sleeve at a suitable timing as a burst of Profound Energy shot across silently to dispel Cui Yuan Shan’s intentional suppression.","“Sect Master Cui, the outcome is already clear and if you continue to tangle in this way, does that mean that you don’t even want your face anymore?”","Li Moying’s cold voice was heard at a speed which was not too fast nor too slow.","But every single word which he said was thought to infuriate anyone to death alive!","Cui Yuan Shan’s face was flushed as he shouted out loudly, “Wh... What outcome is already clear? Stop plastering gold onto your face! Earlier it was because This Sect Master had underestimated you thinking that you’ve just in the seventh stage realm hence I didn’t put in any actual power! Did you think that you could win this Sect Master?”","In actual fact, if it was just based on that move earlier, the winner and loser was already extremely obvious.","Both parties had a face to face Profound Energy clash and in the end, Cui Yuan Shan was thrown ten over feet away, even sustaining a moderate internal injury whereas Li Moying was totally unharmed as he still had surplus energy. Anyone with eyes knew just who had a stronger ability!","However Cui Yuan Shan could not accept this reality or rather, any established ninth stage realm practitioner who thought themselves as extraordinary were all unable to accept that they were actually defeated so easily by a twenty over year old junior in just one move!","This was his lifetime’s goal in cultivation which he was pursuing after and his arrogance and pride as an established top exponent was completely shattered!","So Cui Yuan Shan kept on hypnotising himself that Li Moying was able to defeat himself was all because he had underestimated him!","That move earlier used at most sixty percent of his Profound Energy and he had not even used any Profound Skill so it did not represent his genuine strength!","Hence he was defeated was just a coincidence.....","But Cui Yuan Shan had not thought that as an established old-timer top exponent, yet all he was thinking of was to use his full strength and resorted to all methods to fight with Li Moying before he could even obtain a sliver of “possible” victory. This itself had already shown clearly the difference between both parties’ ability!","Li Moying heard Cui Yuan Shan boasting shamelessly as his lips curled up slightly and sneered, “Since you’re in a hurry to die, then why not let This Seat take a look, at how much ability..... do you really have!”","When he said this, everyone was all dishevelled in the wind.","Li Moying’s sentence and that tone, no matter what it should be a senior saying such words to a junior right?","Why did it feel as though the situation was reversed? He and Cui Yuan Shan’s position... seemed to have turned topsy turvy?","The bystanders who heard that were astonished whereas Cui Yuan Shan was so angry that his seven orifices were fuming with smoke.","“You.... Li Moying, you’re simply seeking.... Death!”","Before his last word left his mouth, Cui Yuan Shan’s face suddenly turned pale as his mouth opened wide in shock.","Li Moying’s feet moved and took a step forward.","Just a small step and his surrounding aura had once again ascended as it instantly expanded rapidly by one fold!","Thunder attributed energy in the surrounding ten miles were all wildly gushing towards him as the air was filled with electric currents, giving off crackling noises."]},{"number":1627,"title":"Chapter 1627 - Ninth stage realm’s might (8)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“You.....” Cui Yuan Shan’s eyes widened.","At this moment, right in front of him, he absolutely wasn’t some talented junior who had just stepped into the ninth stage realm’s door. On the contrary, the peerless strong exponent in front of him had easily controlled the electric currents power and his surrounding’s Heaven & Earth energy, which was extremely complex and hard to handle but he made it seem so easy and simply done as he wished...","This was absolutely something which an established strong exponent who had genuinely combat experience could achieve!","“Who on earth.....” are you?","Cui Yuan Shan’s question was raised but before he could finish asking, Li Moying’s brows rose and he moved in an instance!","Overbearing thunder attributed Profound Energy gathered into bursts of thin electric currents and following a lift of his finger, it struck towards Cui Yuan Shan’s chest!","This bolt of lightning was extremely minute and as compared to the last time the both of them crossed hands, that terrifying lightning which tore the sky apart became an obvious comparison.","However, Cui Yuan Shan sensed that this bolt of non-exceptional lightning contained even more powerful energy which was even more than that lightning which blinded their eyes!","This bolt of lightning came extremely quickly!","Even if Cui Yuan Shan was a wind attributed practitioner, in terms of this speed, he was still too late.","It took merely a thought and the lightning had already reached him and Cui Yuan Shan exhausted everything he could to take precaution as he expedited all the Profound Energy he had to protect his physical body.","However, it was all in vain.","A soft “pffff” was heard!","Li Moying’s electric currents easily tore apart Cui Yuan Shan’s Protection Profound Qi, directly entering his body!","Cui Yuan Shan cried out miserably as his entire body was sent flying out towards the public square’s direction!","He flew for a couple of hundred meters before crashing heavily into the crown, causing a bustle of chaos.","By the time Green Cloud Sect’s disciples hastily passed through the crowd to render aid, they only saw a charred body on the ground. If it wasn’t for the fact that he was still twitching occasionally, they really thought that he had already become a charred corpse!","Whereas on Li Moying’s face, he still bore the biting cold expression, without even a crease in his brow.","It was as though defeating Cui Yuan Shan who was considered a rather strong practitioner who was in the ninth stage realm with one move wasn’t something extraordinary and couldn’t even stir any emotions within his heart.","He couldn’t even be bothered to say a word more as he raised his hand and waved.","Mo Yi and Mo Er who were behind him immediately reciprocated as they went up to drag Li Lingchuan.","This time round, no one else dared to jump out to object.","Li Lingchuan was already foaming at his mouth as he laid limp on the ground totally unconscious, just short of being scared to death alive!","Murong De, on the other hand, had his eyes opened wide as he stared fixedly on Li Moying.","No one was clearer than Murong De on just how strong was Cui Yuan Shan’s ability. In the recent years, he and Cui Yuan Shan had been paring against each other and out of so many times, Murong De had never gained victory at all!","But such a powerful top exponent wasn’t even able to take a strike from his disciple??","This.... really was reality?","After Mo Yi trussed Li Lingchuan up, he returned back to standing behind Li Moying.","Li Moying frowned as he said impatiently, “Murong Fei as well.... Bring them away together!”","Mo Yi shuddered as he hurriedly headed up to capture her.","When Murong Fei heard that, she immediately shrieked, “El.... Eldest Senior Brother, mer... mercy! Don’t catch me, don’t kill me! I really.... really had not thought about harming you at all! It’s Li Lingchuan and Leng Yi Feng they... they forced me! I know my mistake, I’m begging you to take account of my father and spare me, please!”"]},{"number":1628,"title":"Chapter 1628 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","On seeing Li Moying’s cold expression with an unwavering emotion, she hurriedly looked towards Murong De.","“Father, Father.... Quick save me, save me! As long as you say a word, Eldest Senior Brother will definitely listen to you! I.... I really have never harmed Eldest Senior Brother before!”","Murong Fei had never felt such terror before.","In actual fact, it wasn’t only just her. When everyone present took a look at Li Moying, their gazes were mixed in between shock and terror.","Even a top exponent like Cui Yuan Shan had been defeated by him in just one move, not knowing if he was still alive or dead, just what.... What kind of ability was that? And how conceited and overbearing he was!","No matter how Murong Fei had offended Li Moying in the past, she knew that she had a backing behind her, knowing that he felt grateful towards Murong De for saving him and he wouldn’t really kill her. But today, not knowing why, Murong Fei had an unspeakable fear in her heart, somehow feeling that.... Li Moying seemed to have changed into someone else.","Murong De was originally in a daze from the shock and upon hearing his eldest daughter screeching loudly, he regained his senses.","He hurriedly blocked Mo Yi and turned his head towards Li Moying, “Moying, you... your abilities have advanced by leaps and bounds so suddenly, you must had some fortuitous meeting in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region right, which is also considered as a blessing in disguise. Your Junior Sister... she absolutely wouldn’t intentionally do anything to harm you. You should know that for so many years, she had always had feelings for you.... if she had offended you in any way, it definitely must be unintentional so on account of This Master, please let her off this time!”","“That’s right, Eldest Senior Brother, I’m wrong.....” Murong Fei apologised profusely.","When Murong De opened his mouth, Murong Fei then somewhat felt assured.","No matter what, for so many years, Li Moying had basically never rejected any of Murong De’s requests and every time Murong Fei or Murong Ni had caused any trouble, he had also not bothered to haggle with them.","But, this time.....","Li Moying’s icy cold gaze swept past Murong Fei’s face, “Let her off? Impossible! Mo Yi, Mo Er, what are you still waiting for?”","Murong De’s face turned white!","He had not expected that he would be rejected so relentlessly right there.","Usually in such public occasions, Li Moying would give utmost face to him and absolutely would not make things difficult for him.","“You.... your wings have grown tough so you’re not even bothered about this Master of yours is it? Murong Fei she is your Junior Sister! You two have been childhood friends since young and you have the nerve to be so unwilling to forgive her over a small misunderstanding? Moreover speaking, the main person who harmed you is Li Lingchuan. Fei’er was just being threatened so just capture Li Lingchuan away is more than enough!”","Murong De was feeling extremely angry hence the words he said out were extremely harsh.","He increased his tone, thinking of using the past attitude to coerce Li Moying to listen to him.","However, when Li Moying heard that, his face was still filled with a cold expression as he opened his mouth and said, “Murong Fei had indeed not actively plotted against me but she almost killed Li’er! If the person she dealt with was me, on Master’s account, I might be able to forgive and forget but, she actually dared to harm Li’er.....”","Li Moying’s murderous intent in his eyes sparkled as his voice turned increasingly chilly, “Li’er’s life... is several thousand times more important than mine! I had once made a solemn oath that if anyone dared to harm even one strand of hair of Li’er’s, I will make them continue living which is way much worse than dying! With no chance to ever get up again!”","His cold voice drifted all over the public square and everyone’s face bore an extremely shocked expression."]},{"number":1629,"title":"Chapter 1629 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Everyone present had more or less heard of the rumours of how much Li Moying pampered his fiancée.","But no one had imagined that his feelings towards Huang Yueli had reached such a state!","All the young ladies present turned their envious and jealous gazes towards Huang Yueli who was standing behind Li Moying with only one thought in their minds: Why is this woman so lucky! She could actually make a man like Li Moying to risk his all to protect her, not even bearing to let her suffer a little harm/","Not to mention just how much love and adoration Li Moying had usually treated her. Such an icy cold man to everyone else, was always showing her a gentle smile, which made any young lady who saw that wish that they could replace her.","Huang Yueli’s lips curled up, with no intention to hide the complacent smile on her face.","No matter how much the other women liked her Moying, they had no chances at all. This man had been contracted by her many, many years ago! Hehe~","Li Moying’s words had undoubtedly expressed his own stand, sentencing Murong Fei to death.","Murong De looked at him in disbelief as his heart was infuriated to the max!","From what he thought, if it wasn’t for himself who saved Li Moying that year, no matter how talented he was, he would only be a dead corpse sooner or later.","So Li Moying’s achievements today were somehow linked to his credit and Li Moying should know when to repay the favour! How could he kill Murong Fei over a woman who appeared from god-knows-which-place?","But the ability which Li Moying had shown today was simply so strong that even Cui Yuan Shan was defeated easily. Murong De naturally knew that he totally wasn’t his match right now. This disciple who had surpassed the master had grown strong wings and had totally separated himself from his control.","However, Murong Fei was still screaming and struggling.","Murong De loved his daughter very much and simply could not continue watching this as he couldn’t help but spoke out again, “Li Moying! Are you really that heartless to totally ignore all the nurturing that Celestial Light Sect had done for you all these years? Have you forgotten that when you were young and was pursued by killers, who was the one who saved you, and taught you to cultivate, supplying you with various resources?”","Saying that, he suddenly thought of something as he casted a vicious word, “If you insist on taking action on your Junior Sister, then you will no longer be Celestial Light Sect’s disciple!”","Li Moying’s gaze congealed slightly as he went silent for a moment and then continuing to speak out icily, “I have never forgotten Celestial Light Sect’s gratitude to me but for so many years, all that I’ve done for Celestial Light Sect is already enough to return the favour! If it wasn’t for me, Celestial Light Sect would probably not become South Sky Region’s number one Sect today! So my relationship with Celestial Light Sect is considered settled! From today onwards, as what Sect Master Murong wishes, I and Celestial Light Sect.... will no longer have any relations!”","“What did you say??”","Murong De looked at him with his mouth agape and tongue tied!","When he said he was going to drive Li Moying out of the Sect earlier, it was merely a threat but whoever knew that Li Moying actually didn’t hesitate at all and directly announced that he would cut off all relations with Celestial Light Sect!","This.... what was he going to do about this?","Li Moying was Celestial Light Sect’s future hope!","Now that he had already broken through to the ninth stage realm, it was the timing for Celestial Light Sect to fly into greater heights with him but now he just cut off relations with the Sect.... what was Celestial Light Sect going to do?","Murong De then realised just how stupid his threat was earlier.","The situation now wasn’t that Li Moying couldn’t leave Celestial Light Sect, but it was Celestial Light Sect which needed him!","But since this sentence was out, there was no way that he could rescind it."]},{"number":1630,"title":"Chapter 1630 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Murong De’s expression stiffened as he felt extremely regretful! He couldn’t hope more than to take back his words on the shop, crying and pleading Li Moying not to leave.","But this was simply too ugly and no matter what, he was still a Sect’s Master, a top exponent in ninth stage realm so he really couldn’t make himself pull his face down.","Just as he was hesitating and couldn’t make up his mind, Li Moying had already taken action personally, striking the noisily screeching Murong Fei unconscious then throwing her to the Shadow Guards.","His action was swift like lightning and Murong De couldn’t stop him in time.","After Murong Fei had been tied up, he didn’t loiter around as he turned around and held his little fiancée’s hand, turning around to leave!","When Murong De saw this, he couldn’t be bothered if he lost face or not as he hurriedly chased up with a trembling voice and asked, “Moying, you.... you’re really going to leave Celestial Light Sect? Cut off all relations with Celestial Light Sect?”","Li Moying’s footsteps took a pause as he replied in a clear voice without turning back his head, “Isn’t that what you wished for?”","“I.... I’m not.....” Murong De really wanted to explain himself but his mouth was open yet nothing came out.","That’s right, Li Moying had indeed done everything that was asked of him for the sect, and he had also solved numerous prickly matters for Celestial Light Sect, gaining innumerable glory.","But the him who loved his daughter, had once and again ignored Murong Fei’s ridiculous ways, even using the past day’s gratitude to suppress Li Moying to request for him to forgive the things which Murong Fei had done.....","As what he wished, Li Moying had indeed given way many, many times. This made Murong De so pleased that he had lost his own sense of measure, thinking that he, his Master had enough standing, enough to control Li Moying’s actions.","In actual fact, he had forgotten that for such an exceptionally strong practitioner like Li Moying, how could he possibly be threatened into doing certain things?","Apparently in Li Moying’s heart, he naturally would have a balance on each and every matter which made him select the option of giving in. But when Celestial Light Sect demanded overboard on the gratitude which was given to him, he would automatically withdraw himself and unconditionally restrict the so-called “gratitude”, to stop all his actions.","It was right until his moment when Li Moying finally realised that, realising that his calculations..... had all been set wrongly!","Alas, it was all too late.","He sat despondently on the ground as he watched Li Moying and his group of men walking further and further away.....","However, just as they just reached the entrance of the mountain, the young lady beside Li Moying suddenly stopped and tipped her toes up as she whispered something into his ears.","Li Moying frowned, apparently not too willing to do so.","But Huang Yueli hugged his arm and swung it vigorously so under her strong stance of coquetry, Li Moying finally admitted defeat.","Huang Yueli gave a brilliant smile as she pecked him on his cheek and raised her hand to call out for Yuan Zeyu, giving him a few instructions.","Yuan Zeyu accepted the order as he walked through Celestial Light Sect’s public square, standing right in front of Murong De.","Murong De originally lowered his head in despondence but upon hearing footsteps, he thought that Li Moying had turned back and instantly lifted up his head in high spirits, “Moying, this Master knew that you.....”","On seeing the man in front of him was someone whom he didn’t recognise, Murong De was slightly stunned.","Yuan Zeyu said in a clear, distinct voice, “Sect Master Murong, my Third Miss has a few words which she wants me to convey to you.”","“Third Miss.....” Meaning Moying’s fiancée?” Murong De frowned.","Yuan Zeyu didn’t bothered to make any explanations as he continued saying, “Third Miss says she wouldn’t go to the extent of taking Eldest Miss Murong’s life, only going to let her take on the punishment that she deserved so Sect Master Murong need not act in this way.”"]},{"number":1631,"title":"Chapter 1631 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","When Murong De heard that, a spark flashed across his eyes as though he had clutched on to the last straw, as he questioned relentlessly, “Really? She wouldn’t harm Fei’er’s life? That’s great, Moying pampers this fiancée of his the most, her words.... Moying will definitely listen!”","Seeing Murong De heave a long sigh of relief, Yuan Zeyu silently shook his head.","Apparently, Murong De doesn’t understand this Mistress of his. Otherwise.... he absolutely would not be so happy, perhaps he might not even be able to cry out!","According to Yuan Zeyu’s slight understanding towards Huang Yueli, she indeed wouldn’t let Murong Fei die, but.... she would let her suffer a fate living which was worse than death!","But Yuan Zeyu naturally wouldn’t remind Murong De about this.","He cleared his throat and continued, “Third Miss also said that Celestial Light Sect is after all the place where my Master had resided in, so even if he left, he wouldn’t not have any feelings for it. Master is a sentimental man so if Sect Master Murong is able to find a suitable successor, in future if Celestial Light Sect runs into any huge trouble, Master he will not stand aside and do nothing.....”","“Will Sect Master Murong please consider this carefully!”","Yuan Zeyu left this meaningful word then turned around and left.","Murong De repeatedly thought about this for quite some time and the glow in his eyes started to lit up slowly!","Towards Huang Yueli’s words, he had developed his own understanding as he felt extremely indebted towards her.","“Moying’s fiancée is really a good person! Not only had she pleaded for Fei’er, she even helped Celestial Light Sect speak up.... ai, no wonder Moying likes her so much!”","As Li Moying and the others completely vanished from their sights, the entire public square started to clamour with voices of discussions.","The show today was simply too astonishing! It had totally exceeded everyone’s limit of imagination!","Originally they thought that it was merely a coronation ceremony of a Young Sect Master and all they needed to do was to be a silent spectator.","Whoever knew that Li Moying suddenly came back to life and had even became a ninth stage realm top exponent! After exposing Li Lingchuan and Murong Fei’s real faces, he left Celestial Light Sect in indignance!","With all of these, every single matter was enough to become a topic of discussion at one’s leisure.","It was obvious that after today, not too long later, news of what had happened in Celestial Light Sect would have been spread throughout the entire South Sky Region!","Whereas Li Moying was merely twenty one years old and had already broken through to the ninth stage realm would at first instance become South Sky Region’s top news!","This kind of peerless expert which made one unable to look straight at him would henceforth be the focal point for the entire Soaring Heavens Continent!","...","Outside the Sect entrance.","Hearing Yuan Zeyu’s report on completion of his mission, Li Moying took a look at the young lady in his arms with a smile which didn’t look like a smile, “Satisfied now? Murong De really treats you like his jolly good person! But you’re really just a sly little fox!”","Huang Yueli blinked her innocent big eyes, “What’s called ‘treat me like’ a good person? I am really a good person alright? Tell me, which part did I say wrongly?”","Li Moying shook his head helplessly, “No what you said is right! Whoever dares to say you’re wrong, I’ll be the first to disagree with it!”","Huang Yueli’s lips curled up as she smiled broadly while leaning over, “That’s right! Moreover speaking, isn’t it all because of you that’s why I said this?”","Li Moying exchanged glances with her. Their hearts and minds were interconnected hence he naturally knew what this young lass in front of him was up to.","His brows rose as he opened his mouth, “You’re counting your chickens before they hatch, not knowing if someone is willing to listen to you or not?”"]},{"number":1632,"title":"Chapter 1632 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli smiled, “This is a solution which he could have his cake and eat it too, why would he not agree to it? I know, he’s your loyal and devoted Junior Brother, so don’t worry, I’ll persuade him when the time is right!”","Li Moying pinched her perky cheek as he gave a low laugh, “Alright, I’ll be relying on my wifey to help me plan by then.”","“Who is your wifey?” Huang Yueli swept him a glance, she would not casually marry him just like that alright? Even if she only had eyes for this man, but if Li Moying didn’t bring out one hundred and twenty percent of his sincerity to propose to her, she would not casually nod her head!","She murmured, “I only felt that you’ve been in Celestial Light Sect for so many years and have already set up a strong foundation there so if you were to just give up like that, it was really such a pity. Furthermore, South Sky Region’s forces originally belong to Celestial Heavens Gate, so this chance is hard to come by.....”","She made it sound very vague but Li Moying completely understood her meaning.","He had been Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master for many years and his foundation was very deep. It could be said that the entire Celestial Light Sect was within his grasp and furthermore based on Celestial Light Sect’s status in South Sky Region, if it was used as a piece of chess in a suitable way, it could completely affect the entire South Sky Region’s situation.","So Li Moying’s leaving was really a pity but now that he had broken through to the ninth stage realm, it was definite for him to head towards Sky Emperor City to gain more space for development, rather than to continue mingling around in Celestial Light Sect.","In this way, the only way out for him was to leave a suitable successor, to help him take charge of Celestial Light Sect’s forces, and at the same time become his agent for South Sky Region.","The only choice for this person, naturally was his fifth Junior Brother, Luo Jiyun.","Luo Jiyun had always been loyal and devoted towards Li Moying and furthermore after Li Lingchuan and the others had all gotten into trouble, the only one with eight grade talent was him and in actual fact, he had already became Celestial Light Sect’s highest innate talent and strongest abled talented practitioner.","For him to take over the position of Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master, naturally he was the choice for them to strike a balance in all aspects.","Huang Yueli had made Yuan Zeyu told Murong De all these, was so that he could plant all these thoughts into reality.","Actually, Li Moying had also thought of the same thing but as he considered Luo Jiyun’s feelings, it was difficult for him to stand out but he had not expected Huang Yueli to be even more decisive than him as she immediately did so.","He lowered his head and took a look at his smiling Li’er as his lips curled up, with a slight tinge of sweetness and a little frustration.","Ai, to have an interconnected heart and mind fiancée, everything he was thinking of could not escape her eyes. Then in future wouldn’t he not be able to do a single bad thing at all?","He was plainly most afraid of losing his freedom but why was it that when he thought of it, it actually made him feel full of anticipation instead?","That night, Li Moying led the entire group of them into Sky Cloud City as they settled down in a luxurious mansion within the city.","This luxurious mansion was one of the properties under Li Moying’s name and he had first got the Shadow Guards to clean up the place, settling everything properly in advance.","Huang Yueli had been in a state of unrest for this period of time. Firstly she met with several dangers in Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region and later on they kept on hurrying back to Celestial Light Sect to exact revenge.","It was only until now that she had enough free time to soak herself in the mansion’s huge warm sauna pool, enjoying her flower petal sauna bath.","By the time she spent over an hour coming out from the refreshing bath which invigorated her skin, she discovered that Li Moying had gone missing.","She took a tour around the rear courtyard and saw Li Moying sitting in the pavilion as he gazed afar, seemingly lost in thought."]},{"number":1633,"title":"Chapter 1633 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli walked over in quick steps and hugged his arm as she looked at him from a slanted angle.","“Moying, what are you thinking about?”","Li Moying lowered his voice, “I’m thinking.... of what I should do next.”","Huang Yueli blinked as she recalled something in enlightenment, “That’s right, I haven’t asked you yet. What is our next step after leaving Celestial Light Sect?”","Actually, she more or less had confirmed that their next destination was a ninety nine percent chance of heading towards Sky Emperor City.","But for the exact next step, she wasn’t too sure of it. Only knowing that if Li Moying wanted to go over to take a look, she would follow him with no second thoughts, no matter if it was to the ends of the world...","But her fiance had always been a determined man, so he definitely had his own plan.","Li Moying turned back and took a look at her as he said, “We... shall stay in Sky Cloud City for a few days first. In the past decade, I have quite a number of properties in South Sky Region that needs to be handled, following that.....”","He paused for a moment and his voice seemed to add a few tones of anticipation.","“Following that, will be the time for us to return back to Sky Emperor City!”","Huang Yueli’s entire body shook!","Even though she knew long ago that Li Moying’s choice was so, but when she really heard it, it still made Huang Yueli’s heart undulate.","Sky Emperor City... Soaring Heavens Continent’s core, where innumerable top rated strong practitioners gathered. It was filled with opportunities anywhere and anytime, and at the same time, it was also filled with..... plots and betrayals!","That was also the place where she had lived for the past decades in her past life!","She had once been the existence of the most popular person in Sky Emperor City and as the Young Palace Lord of the Mythical Flame Palace, she was an exceptional genius with ninth grade upper talent and also the number one beauty who startled all the four seats in Soaring Heavens Continent.... Where innumerable light halos were placed on the top of her head.","However, even though she had the achievements which so many people were envious of, later on when everyone mentioned her, the first sentence would always be, “Number one top expert Mu Chengying’s woman”.....","Once, she disliked so much that she was casted this name by a man, as though all her hard work and achievements were all erased cleanly in an instance.","But now that she had already died once, she felt that this title sounded... rather flashy! Moreover it could also push back all those women who were eyeing Mu Chengying!","Sky Emperor City to her, did not have many beautiful memories.","That year when she was in the Northern Ice Fields, she had suffered the attack of three different Sects out of the Seven Sacred Lands. At that time her whereabouts were kept secretive and the only person who had sold her out was her best female friend – Celestial Heavens Gate’s Eldest Young Miss Ling Qing Yu.....","That kind of devouring hatred remained deep at the bottom of her heart. Like the cold from the Northern Ice Fields which had entered her bones that night had still not dissipated ever since that day.....","It was also this exact reason why she had been even more prudent this lifetime, putting on more defence against other people.","This lifetime, other than Li Moying, she couldn’t trust anyone else. Even though she didn’t usually display it, but she often left a hand in secret.","Furthermore, she didn’t have many friends this lifetime and all these were because of the psychological shadow which had been left from her past life.","Because of that, the mere thought of returning to Sky Emperor City had Huang Yueli feeling various kinds of feelings welling up in her heart so for a short moment, she was slightly dazed.","Li Moying raised his hand and caressed her silky long hair as he said softly, “Li’er, are you alright? I know what you’re upset about. Don’t you worry, I will help you get your revenge on the grievances in your past life one by one, absolutely not letting off a single one of them who dared to hurt you!”"]},{"number":1634,"title":"Chapter 1634 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (7)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli lifted up her head to meet those brilliant, sparkling peach blossom eyes.","Beneath those eyes was deep and tender sentiments, as though it would drown her within.","In an instance, Huang Yueli felt her eyes turning moistened, almost crying out right there.","Because she discovered that no matter if it was in her past life or current, no matter if she was in favourable circumstances or in adversity, the person who had stood beside her unwaveringly..... had always been this man!","She hugged Li Moying’s waist with increased strength, burying her face into his wide and robust chest. She blinked and tears seeped into the cloth material on Li Moying’s chest.....","Li Moying didn’t say anything much, only embracing her in an even more gentle and resolute manner into his arms.","Sky Emperor City.... To them, it was a place which was filled with memories!","It took quite a while before Huang Yueli raised her head and said to Li Moying, “Thank you, Moying. I know you wholeheartedly want to protect me. But revenge is a dish best served cold! You need not be too anxious as well. After we reach Sky Emperor City, let’s plan slowly! After all, things are no longer the same as before.....”","Huang Yueli sighed softly.","She was grateful to Li Moying for his willingness to give his all wholeheartedly but she really didn’t want him to take such a big risk just because of her own reasons.","After all, the Li Moying now was not the same as the-then Mu Chengying.","He had just broken through to the ninth stage realm and although his innate talent was much more superior than it was then but it was still totally different as when he was in ninth stage realm peak condition.","The difference in ability and battle power between ninth stage realm practitioners was actually extremely, extremely huge and the disparity between the strong and the weak was a world of difference.","Huang Yueli’s past life’s does were all part of Sky Emperor City’s largest powerhouses, Seven Sacred Lands where all of it had been around since ancient times. Their inheritances had lasted for several hundred thousands of years, as the top exponents under them were innumerable!","Even for the past life’s Mu Chengying, if he didn’t have a proper plan and just abruptly headed up, he would likely also suffer a disadvantage. What more now that his ability was a far cry from his past life, and that he had departed Sky Emperor City for more than a decade. Not knowing just how much force he would be able to gather back from the past, Soaring Heavens Continent’s current situation was something which they weren’t sure of....","Huang Yueli absolutely would not allow Li Moying to take action under such a situation!","Although she wanted very much to exact revenge, but after her rebirth, in her heart she was very clear that nothing was more important than Li Moying!","As compared to his safety, revenge of whatsoever had all become small issues.","Li Moying’s heart was moved as the arm which embraced her grew tighter as he lowered his head to take a whiff of the fragrance of her hair while sighing softly, “I know, Li’er, do you think I look like a rash person? Don’t worry, I won’t do anything which I don’t have any certainty of.”","As he was saying that ,Huang Yueli suddenly had a strange and uneasy premonition.","She suddenly raised her head and grabbed Li Moying’s collar, “Moying, you... you must promise me... no matter what situation you are in, you must place your safety in the first place and you must always, always accompany me, staying beside me properly!”","Li Moying went into a slight daze as his eyes flashed past an astonished glint.","Li’er... had she detected something?","Impossible, he had obviously..... concealed it very well.... It could be said that to be flawless.....","Li Moying merely hesitated for a breath’s time when he regained his senses and smiled, “What are you worried about? I’m right by your side isn’t it? I will naturally keep you accompanied properly, after all I’ve spent so many years before you finally nod your head to be together than me!”"]},{"number":1635,"title":"Chapter 1635 - Returning to Sky Emperor City (8)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Li Moying’s smile was extremely perfect as that gentle and adoring attitude was exactly the same as before.","Huang Yueli knew clearly that Li Moying was absolutely not some rash young lad.","But she didn’t know why she had an indiscernible feeling in her heart, as though she seemed to have missed out a very important matter.....","Li Moying saw her distracted look and frowned slightly as he lowered his head to plant a kiss on her cheek.","Huang Yueli’s face immediately flushed a bright red shade, “Why are you moving your hands while we are talking!”","Li Moying innocently replied, “I only moved my mouth, since when did I move my hands? You’re the one who is obviously lusting after my body, you hugged me so tightly so aren’t you laying your little hands on me? Isn’t this called thief yelling thief!”","When Huang Yueli heard that, she immediately became gloomy as she raised her little fists, just about to incur domestic violence onto him.","Li Moying could obviously evade her moves but he just stood there obediently, allowing his fiancée to vent her anger on him.","After a moment later, he grabbed hold of Huang Yueli’s wrist and dragged her into his arms, “Alright, alright, if you continue hitting me, your hands will start to hurt and in that way, I’m the one who will feel heartache... En?”","He leaned closed to her delicate fair cheek and blew some air on her in an ambiguous way.","Following that, while Huang Yueli had not regained her senses, he leaned forward and gave her a deep kiss.","A man’s overbearing presence invaded her as that handsome looking face was right in front of her eyes. Huang Yueli’s heart was pounding wildly as her brain turned into glue, other than obediently inclining towards the man in front of her and allowing him to kiss her wilfully, she totally could not react at all, not to mention having the mind to think about any other things.","This submissive her made Li Moying feel a passionate fire burn up within him and plus the fact that she had just taken a bath which made her body give off a light rose scent, it was even more effective than any aphrodisiac.","Li Moying kissed until he almost lost control, to the extent that..... he just pushed Huang Yueli onto a chaise longue as he buried his face into her slender long neck, following all the way downwards, planting deep strawberries (love bites).","Huang Yueli didn’t stop him because she felt very comfortable.","Everytime she laid in this man’s arms, she felt as though she was turning into a puddle of water, totally unable to control herself.....","“Eldest Senior Brother, I heard.... AH——!”","A shocked cry was heard.","“Ughh, ah, I didn’t know... that... I’m sorry, sorry! I didn’t see anything at all, I’m leaving, Eldest Senior Brother, lil Sister-in-law, please continue to be busy.....”","When Luo Jiyun got closer to them, he detected the ambiguous atmosphere in the pavilion and instantly understood why Mo Yi and the others kept stopping him from entering this place. Unfortunately he was just too rash and had given too much thought to their words.","Now.... it was too late for him to regret as he could only bore the brunt of his Eldest Senior Brother’s murderous gazes as he turned around and scurried away in a jiffy!","Interrupted by that joker, Li Moying turned around and sat up as his good looking face was taut bearing an icy cold expression.","Huang Yueli raised her head and sized him up as she couldn’t help but burst out “giggling”.","Li Moying turned back and started at that little fox who was gloating over his misfortune but the latter wasn’t a single bit afraid at all, as she intentionally smiled sweetly, “Moying, why are you unhappy? Are you in a bad mood? Do you want me to give you a kiss?”","She’s really a little fox who added oil to fire! Didn’t she know that with the love bites on her collarbone, saying such things, what kind of effect it would cause?","Li Moying’s gaze dimmed, “So proactive? Then let’s return to our room in case we get interrupted by some little brat.....”"]},{"number":1636,"title":"Chapter 1636 - Entering the city (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","As he said that, he walked to the front of the chaise longue and stretched out his hand as he was about to carry her up horizontally.","Huang Yueli immediately had a change of expression and right before he could even touch her, she jumped up like her butt was on fire.","“Alright, stop fooling around! Junior Brother Luo came running over at this timing must be because of that matter, we’d better hurry over to take a look at him!”","Li Moying laughed softly, “Why? Have the heart of a thief but no guts? Earlier who was the one who wanted to kiss me and comfort me? Thinking of just running away like that?”","Huang Yueli’s face turned red, as she really couldn’t hope more than to kick him!","Mentioning the pot which didn’t boil! Look at his ill-intentioned look, who dared to kiss him! What if she kissed him and it caused him to get heated up?","Li Moying looked at her biting her lips as her eyeballs kept roving around and found it extremely amusing as he couldn’t help but shot upwards like an arrow, pulling her wrist and wrestling her into his arms.","“Li’er, it’s not right to lie especially to your fiancé. Since you’ve agreed to kiss, then you’re not allowed to renege on it!”","Huang Yueli acted blur, “Renege on a debt? Since when had I reneged on a debt? I merely don’t want to kiss already, treat it like I owe you one for now!”","Owing and owning, and it would be forgotten.","However, how could Li Moying not know about this little thing’s tricks as he held her slender waist tightly and inched his face close to hers.","“Why not like this, you don’t kiss me, but it’d be the same if I kissed you.....”","When Huang Yueli heard the mellow and sexy voice around her ears then looking at his long and thick lashes which were like a fan drooping down, her heart jolted as she started to feel a little dizzy again.","But immediately she detected a flame in Li Moying’s profound eyes and this made the alarms in her heart rang as she hurriedly said, “I’ll kiss, I’ll kiss, don’t come any closer!”","Li Moying’s action paused and was just about to say something when he suddenly felt a warm sensation on his lips.","His little fox had swiftly pounced over and swiftly nibbled him on the lips then using force she pushed him away thinking of withdrawing herself from him.","Li Moying’s lips curled upwards, knowing that this lass was going to come out with the same tricks. Using a chick-pecking-on-grains-like kiss to pacify him? alas, a man wasn’t that easy to deal with. After being tricked so many times, he had learnt to become smarter.","His body hadn’t moved but instead he locked on to her waist with slightly more force as he turned from guest into host as he lifted up her chin and planted his kiss onto her once again.","Huang Yueli had not expected her plan to fall through as her eyes opened real wide and tried her hardest to push him away.","Li Moying was hugging a wriggling, uncooperative little fox and had no choice but to dabble and stop and not long later, he loosened his grip.","Huang Yueli started hard at him, “Quick, don’t... don’t fool around! Junior Brother Luo is still waiting outside and if he doesn’t go out, what will he think!”","Li Moying laid lazily on the chaise longue as he replied in an absent-minded manner, “Who cares what he thinks? Anyway.... What he’s thinking in his mind is the truth.....”","Huang Yueli’s face flushed a bright shade of red, she had truly been defeated by this thick skinned man!","She gritted her teeth and said, “Are you going out or not!”","Li Moying saw his little fiancée exploding and could only give a light cough, “I’ll listen, I’ll listen, let’s go.... but, can we wait a little longer first?”","Huang Yueli went into a short blank but immediately, her gaze started sweeping onto the horizontally inclined man lying on the chaise longue in a seductive posture and her gaze followed all the way downwards from his half exposed chest..."]},{"number":1637,"title":"Chapter 1637 - Entering the city (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","She had to admit that this man in front of her was an excellent piece of work. Every single muscle line was just nice, so beautifully perfect that made one unable to shift their eyes away.","In her past life, she thought that Mu Chengying was the most handsome man but in this life, as he possessed God Clan’s bloodline, his looks were even more breathtaking now.","Huang Yueli’s vision followed downwards subconsciously.","In an instant, her face turned even redder.","She finally knew why Li Moying had refused to stand up. Because his bodily reaction was just too obvious and with this state, it would be strange if he dared to meet anyone else.","“You..... You.....”","Huang Yueli simply didn’t know what to say as she bit on her lips and gave him a stare, then slipping away immediately.","Li Moying looked at her departing figure as he gave a bitter smile.","This lass.... indeed had the ability to force one into insanity. She set the fire and after realising that she had created trouble then ran off on her own, moreover bearing a look which looked like she was bullied by him.....","But even so, he was totally helpless as he could only allow his little fox to throw her tantrum in whatever tsundere (presenting as unfriendly and blunt but warm and tender inside) way she wanted.","Huang Yueli ran out of the pavilion and readjusted her clothes before she headed to the front lobby.","Luo Jiyun had been waiting there for quite some time as Mo Yi and the other Shadow Guards stood around chatting with him.","On seeing Huang Yueli appearing alone, everyone’s gazes all turned to her instantaneously. Not knowing if it was because she had a guilty conscience, she somehow felt that everyone’s eyes were filled with ambiguity.","She hurriedly gave a slight cough, “Ugh, that.... Junior Brother Luo, why have you come over so late at night?”","Luo Jiyun heard that and hurriedly explained, “Lil Sister-in-law, really.... Really sorry! I really didn’t know.... ughh, have I interrupted you two? I...”","This hotheaded lad had totally not noticed that Huang Yueli was showing an embarrassed expression as he was still apologizing non stop. It was right until Mo Yi pulled his from behind when he finally realised that something was amiss and hurriedly shut his mouth.","Huang Yueli’s lips twitched, “You haven’t interrupted.....”","She paused for a moment and continued, “You’re here today, to look for your Eldest Senior Brother regarding Celestial Light Sect’s matters?”","Luo Jiyun heard that and kept on nodding his head, and at the same time he put on a pitiful look while pleading for help, “Lil Sister-in-law, please me to persuade Eldest Senior Brother, ask him not to leave me here alone! I want to leave with Eldest Senior Brother!”","Huang Yueli’s brows rose as she looked at him, “Why? You’re not willing to stay on in Celestial Light Sect? You probably aren’t very clear yet right? Among the current direct disciples in Celestial Light Sect, there are just but a few top exponents left and plus the fact that your Eldest Senior Brother still had some power left around here, you only need to stay on and you will definitely become Celestial Light Sect’s Young Sect Master!”","“Actually, earlier Brother Mo Yi had already told me about the stakes involved. But, I... I don’t want to become a Young Sect Master! I just want to follow Eldest Senior Brother!” Luo Jiyun persisted.","Huang Yueli smiled slightly as she stared at him and continued asking, “Are you sure? Have you really thought through this clearly? Such matters cannot be decided so rashly alright? You’ve also witnessed with your own eyes on how Li Lingchuan had tried to obtain the position of Young Sect Master and expended so much effort, even plotting an audacious plan of murdering his Senior Brother but eventually he still didn’t get what he wished for!”","“Whereas for you, you could easily take on the position of Young Sect Master. Your Eldest Senior Brother would also support you in future, so are you really not going to do it? If you miss such a good chance, there will be no next time again!”"]},{"number":1638,"title":"Chapter 1638 - Entering the city (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli reiterated this once and again.","Actually, without her saying, anyone with brains were able to think of this as it was the next logical thing to do. Status and authority, were just an arm’s length away!","However Luo Jiyun continued to shake his head, “No, I don’t want to be some Young Sect Master, I only want to follow Eldest Senior Brother!”","Although Huang Yueli had long known of his unyielding loyalty towards Li Moying, but his resolute attitude had even eliminated any sense of hesitation, which made one surprised.","“Why? This is such a good opportunity, why do you choose to give it up? Haven’t you considered that your Eldest Senior Brother had betrayed Celestial Light Sect, running off to roam about in Sky Emperor City but there are so many top experts there, perhaps Moying isn’t even anything over there. He might even offend someone unknowingly, unlike you who could stay relaxed in Celestial Light Sect!”","Luo Jiyun lifted up his head and looked at him, “But isn’t the art of cultivation about pursuing challenges? Greedy for a peaceful life could not possibly bring out the potential within! Following Eldest Senior Brother around indeed isn’t as easy in Celestial Light Sect but I believe that it would lead me to head towards an even higher cultivational realm pathway! Moreover, Eldest Senior Brother wouldn’t continue to be a nobody forever. Based on his innate talent, he would definitely become a somebody who could command the wind and summon the rain, so following him around is definitely not a wrong choice!”","Huang Yueli saw Li Moying walk over slowly from behind Luo Jiyun and couldn’t help but laugh, “Moying, I really couldn’t tell that this Junior Brother of yours.... Really has unconditional trust in you!”","Li Moying grazed lightly over Luo Jiyun as he was apparently rather impressed.","He muttered, “Since you have this thinking..... then following me around is of no harm! But don’t be like me to separate yourself from Celestial Light Sect. Tomorrow you will go over to tell Murong De clearly that you’re just temporarily following me to Sky Emperor City to go on experience learning and will return in future.”","“But, Eldest Senior Brother—!”","Luo Jiyun was rather astonished, “You’ve already left Celestial Light Sect, I... why should I stay there for? I’m really not interested in the position of Young Sect Master!”","Huang Yueli beamed as she spoke up for her fiancée, “You’re not interested but your Eldest Senior Brother is interested! Moying’s foundation which he had laid over the years, should we just let go of it like that? In future, we will rely on you to help him safeguard it, don’t tell me you’re not willing to do so?”","Luo Jiyun then revealed an enlightened look as he patted his chest to express that he would definitely follow Eldest Senior Brother’s instructions.","After Luo Jiyun left, Huang Yueli pulled Li Moying back to their room and the minute they entered the room, she pursued him for an answer, “You agreed to let Jiyun to follow you? Why? Could it be that... you’ve already confirmed where we will be staying when we return to Sky Emperor City?”","Earlier when Li Moying nodded his head in approval, even she felt surprised.","She had assumed that Li Moying would not allow Luo Jiyun to stay in Celestial Light Sect, out of concern for his safety.","Later on, having a change of thoughts, she understood it immediately. Probably Li Moying had already thought of a plan hence he decided on this.","Li Moying’s arms were crossed as he lowered his head and looked at the young lady in front of him as his lips curled up, “You’re so impatient to pull me back to the room, I had thought that... you’re preparing to continue the matter earlier which you had not completed!”","“Earlier... what matter.....” Huang Yueli blinked and suddenly comprehended as her face flushed red, “You... you’re so shameless! Stop with the rubbish and quickly tell me the answer!”","Li Moying then slowly replied, “It’s not considered as a plan but since I was the Sovereign of Blue Profound Sect in my past life, naturally I will return to my own Sect!”"]},{"number":1639,"title":"Chapter 1639 - Entering the city (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli’s eyes turned wide open as she felt extremely surprised when she heard what he said.","“What? You want to return to Blue Profound Sect??”","From what she thought, this was the most impossible option which Li Moying would take.","After all, so many years had gone by and no one could be sure of the current situation of Blue Profound Sect. So heading back abruptly might not necessarily be a good thing, in fact it might be very risky.","Because Blue Profound Sect as the number one super powerhouse in the then Soaring Heavens Continent had plenty of strong exponents and based on Li Moying current ability, there was no way that he could resume to the same state that year, to suppress so many top exponents. At the very least, Li Moying’s Four Great Guardians under him were all much stronger than he was right now.","Li Moying met her eyes and nodded his head prudently, “That’s right!”","He quickly followed up with an explanation, “You don’t need to worry too much. That year when I left Blue Profound Sect, I’d already arranged everything that I needed to within the Sect. Some days after we left the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region, I’ve also sent out a secret signal and obtained contact with Blue Profound Sect. Although so many years have passed, there is bound to be changes within the Sect but I still have my own way to control the Four Great Guardians so you need not worry too much over this.”","“Moreover, based on our current ability, to help you exact revenge, it’s just too slow to do it step by step so it’s better for us to return back to Blue Profound Sect first, so that we can speed up the process of our strength quickly.”","Huang Yueli naturally believed his ability and also believed that since he said there would be no problem, then there would definitely be no problem.","But unknowing why, she somehow felt that something seemed wrong somewhere.","“But.....”","Huang Yueli frowned and thought for a moment as. Her eyes lit up and said, “Right! Last time when you were in Celestial Light Sect, your Soul Detachment Illness acted up and you regained most of your memories from your past life. Hadn’t you said in the past that all the memories that is related to my self-explosion, you weren’t really able to recall it all? How is it that you are able to remember what happened before you left Blue Profound Sect? Your memories.... Has it recovered completely?”","“Ughh...” Li Moying’s heart pounded wildly!","He simply had not expected that Huang Yueli would be so intelligent to this step, to actually see through the truth which he had tried all means and ways to cover up!","That was right, when they were in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region, his illness acted up when he was on the verge of death plus the fact that he was struck on lightning, all the memories came rushing back at one shot.","By the time he regained consciousness, he discovered that he had recalled everything that had happened.","Before this, no matter how he racked his brains, he totally couldn’t recall anything from after Huang Yueli’s death. That bit of lost memory had all returned to his mind this time round.","But it was exactly because of this which was why he knew that.... what exactly, was he about to face......","Li Moying’s thoughts turned swiftly. Although he was exposed earlier and had a slight instant of being dazed, but he quickly concealed his own loss of self-control.","“Ughh, Li’er, I also wished that I could recover all my memories but unfortunately it’s not within my control. I can only indistinctly remember bits and pieces of very small portions, basically just the portion on the agreement with the Four Great Guardians...”","Huang Yueli frowned, “Really? So coincidental? Has this memory come back to you the last time your illness acted up in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region? Other than this, what else can you remember? What happened after I self-exploded and why did you reincarnate and reborn as well? Have you recalled all of these?”","Of course he had recalled all of these, but...","Li Moying’s expression was as per normal as he shook his head slowly, “These... I can’t remember it at all! I’ve tried several times but the minute I try to recall, my head would hurt so much as though it was about to split open...”"]},{"number":1640,"title":"Chapter 1640 - Entering the city (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The minute Huang Yueli heard that, she immediately got tensed, not daring to ask any further.","“What? Why did this happen? Then you’d better not try to think about it, anyway.... Anyway from the looks of it, your memory is starting to come back to you bit by bit so there’s no need to force it. Perhaps when the time is near, you will know.”","Li Moying heard what she said and secretly heaved a sigh of relief.","However, Huang Yueli thought of something as she hurriedly added on, “Ah, that’s right! That year, Four Great Guardians were all your trusted aides! I think they would definitely know the situation then. When we reach Blue Profound Sect, we can interrogate each one of them so perhaps we might be able to discover something.....”","“Cough cough...” Li Moying’s expression turned slightly pale again.","Why was his fiancée so, so intelligent! It was practically impossible to defend against her effectively, it was simply too difficult to hide anything from her.","Luckily she told him whatever was on her mind, telling him her plan so he should nip the problem in the butt before it happened.","There were some things which he absolutely could not afford to let her find out!","Li Moying hurriedly said, “What you said is correct, as long as we reach Sky Emperor City, the truth will be out. Moreover whenever I advance into another level, there is also the possibility of regaining my memory so you shouldn’t worry too much! Or is it that.... if I didn’t had these memories, you don’t love me anymore?”","Huang Yueli rolled her eyes at him, “You.... what rubbish are you sprouting? I’m just worried about you! Somehow I feel that..... things aren’t that simply, what on earth had you done in your past life? Why is it that you have also reincarnated and reborn? And why is it that after I’ve self-exploded, but I recollected all my senses? I simply don’t understand all these...”","Li Moying sighed softly as he held her hand and said in a mellow voice, “Stop thinking about it. What matters now is that we’re together isn’t it? To me, for this moment to come true, I’d be more than willing to pay any price for it!”","Huang Yueli raised her head and looked at him as her heart jolted, unknowingly on why an indescribable heartache started to make her tremble slightly.","“You...”","“Li’er, you’re trembling, are you feeling cold?”","Li Moying immediately held her hands and took her into his arms.","The two of them embraced tightly at a close distance.","Taking a whiff of Li Moying’s familiar and mild scent of a man, Huang Yeuli finally felt a little better as the uneasiness in her heart wasn’t that much anymore.","Only, these questions had been shrouded around her mind – Just what happened after she self-exploded?","...","Li Moying and the entire group stayed on in Sky Cloud City for close to two weeks, processing the properties and other important matters he had in Sky Cloud City.","In between, Murong De sent someone over several times in bid to retain Li Moying but Li Moying’s attitude was resolute as he didn’t entertain him at all.","Huang Yueli also took some time to settle some matters, basically to make arrangements for the place of residence for those servants whom she had taken in.","The majority from Celestial Light Academy, did not have much outstanding innate talent and their achievements in the way of cultivation in future wouldn’t possibly be too high. Hence Huang Yueli didn’t forced them to head towards Sky Emperor City with her, but to let them choose their own path.","A portion of them chose to stay in Celestial Light Sect, and that included Su Qingyue.","Huang Yueli handed Cai Wei and some other lower levelled practitioners over to Su Qingyue to manage, allowing them to cultivate and manage the properties which she and Li moying had left behind in Sky Cloud City.","In future when Luo Jiyun returned to Celestial Light Sect successfully with achievements in his cultivation, he might need the aid of these hidden forces to stabilise his own status."]},{"number":1641,"title":"Chapter 1641 - Entering the city (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","As for Yuan Zeyu and some other practitioners with much better innate talents, they naturally didn’t wish to stay on in Sky Cloud City to waste their time.","They chose to head towards Sky Emperor City to make a name for themselves. After all it was only in such an environment with strong practitioners which would allow them to increase their own abilities to the maximum degree.","After settling everything, Li Moying and Huang Yueli then brought all their subordinates and left Sky Cloud City on a flying ship.","...","A month later.","The flying ship slowly got closer to the outer boundary of Sky Emperor City and they were able to see Sky Emperor City’s city wall from quite a distance away.","This day early in the morning, Luo Jiyun and the others dashed over to the deck of the flying ship and stood in a circle to watch as they all started to exclaim in admiration.","“Heavens, it’s just too spectacular!”","“I’d not expected Sky Emperor City’s city walls to be the same as the legends. It’s all built with aquamarine ceramic glazed tiles, just how much money is this worth!”","“It’s rumoured that on the outer boundary of Sky Cloud City, there’s a god grade city protection array left from ancient times, which is impenetrable!”","“It’s just too powerful! No wonder this place is the core of the entire Soaring Heavens Continent!”","When Huang Yueli heard these country bumpkins giving off such exaggerated praises, she couldn’t help but smiled.","Although Sky Emperor City was just a city, but in actual fact, it’s size was almost the size of the entire South Sky Region.","Moreover, as the Continent’s core, for several thousands of years, innumerable top rated geniuses had all brought everything they had, heading towards Sky Emperor City to seek for chances to breakthrough and to establish their fame overnight. This tradition had been accumulating from generation to generation, hence it led to Sky Emperor City becoming the gathering of innumerable top exponents, and also.... astonishing wealth!","Just how strong were Sky Emperor City’s top powerhouses, and how wealthy they were, was something which those practitioners from desolated Four Sky Regions weren’t able to imagine.","It could be said that for every practitioner who had just arrived to Sky Emperor City were deeply stunned hence Luo Jiyun and the other’s display wasn’t too exaggerated at all.","Li Moying looked at her weak smile as he suddenly recalled something and a smile curled up on his lips.","“Tsk tsk, these fellows.... Are they country bumpkins entering the city? To think that year, when I first arrived at Sky Emperor City.....”","Huang Yueli’s eyes shone as she immediately pursued after this topic excitedly, “How was it? Your first time in Sky Emperor City, was it very silly and laughable?”","Huang Yueli suddenly recalled that Mu Chengying seemed to come from a desolate village and although his Master who fostered him was a top exponent in Soaring Heavens Continent, but he had always been living in seclusion in the rural area to teach a few disciples. It was only until he reached seventeen or eighteen when Mu Chengying finally came to Sky Emperor City for experience learning.","Huang Yueli grew up in Sky Emperor City herself hence she had not felt that Sky Emperor City was a spectacular or outstanding place at all.","But now she was extremely curious, wondering how it was when he first entered the city. Did he act the same as those youngsters who were making a big fuss out of nothing?","Li Moying shot a glance at her in a smile which didn’t looked like a smile but under Haung Yueli’s impatient glare, he said a few meaningful words, “I don’t remember anymore....”","Huang Yueli’s eyes opened wide, “You, you, you.... how dare you trick me! Impossible, I don’t believe it! Such an important matter like your first time entering Sky Emperor City, how could you forget about it? This is the changing point of your past life so you definitely remembered it! Have you done something embarrassing? Quick, if there’s something unhappy that happened, tell me so that I can be amused by it!”","Li Moying looked at her in extreme innocence as he said, “I didn’t lie to you! I really don’t remember it anymore!”"]},{"number":1642,"title":"Chapter 1642 - Entering the city (7)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli absolutely refused to listen to his gibberish.","“How could you possibly not remember! Even I remember it! That year if it wasn’t to join Sky Emperor City’s genius tournament which is held once every ten years, would you have rushed over from the border? Moreover, at that tournament, you defeated various large influential powerhouses’ top rated talents consecutively to become the winner which shocked the entire Sky Emperor City hence you made a name for yourself ever since then! Such an important thing, how could you forget about it? Liar! Quickly tell me, tell me!”","She stuck close to Li Moying as she pestered him asking this and that, determining that since he refused to say, then he must have done something embarrassing at that time.","However, Li Moying continued to smile without replying. Instead he turned around and pulled her into his arms while whispering ambiguous words into her ears softly.","“I’ve not expected that you remembered my matters so clearly! Looks like ever since that time, you’ve been paying attention to me right? Then that time when I wanted to get acquainted with you, you still intentionally put on an arrogant look, not even looking straight at me in the eye! Isn’t that a little too tsundere?”","Huang Yueli’s face turned bright red, “Wh... When did I? The number one tournament in the world.... That’s... that’s Sky Emperor City’s first rate matter! I will naturally pay some attention to it! Moreover, the tournament came out with such a dark horse which had spread throughout the entire Sky Emperor City, it would be difficult for me not to know about it even if I didn’t want to, what... what does it have to do with you?”","She would never admit that during the number one tournament battle grounds when she unintentionally saw Mu Chengying, she was also attracted by his demeanour like those ignorant young ladies.","But very quickly when she saw a whole bunch of young Missys from other Sects crowding around him, the her who was still pure in the heart immediately plastered a “Casanova” label onto him and in order to conceal the feelings that she had towards him, she intentionally pretended not to see him.","Li Moying originally just mentioned it casually but when he saw her face flushed red, he couldn’t help but feel his heart pounding hard.","“Why? I’ve really hit the spot?”","Huang Yueli raised her head tsunderely as she stared hard at him, “Narcissism is an illness, you have to treat it!”","Saying that, she pushed him aside, “Alright, from the sound of their voices, it seems that we are about to reach Sky Emperor zone which restricts flying. Looks like we have to land soon, I’ll go out and take a look!” She disappeared like a wisp of smoke.","Li Moying saw her escaping rapidly as he rubbed his nose and the smile on his lips turned even deeper.","He had not intentionally lied to Huang Yueli earlier because he really didn’t recall what happened when he just entered the city.","Actually what Huang Yueli said wasn’t wrong. That was the most important day of his past life and by right, he shouldn’t have forgotten about it.","But after he entered the city, he immediately headed over to Sky Emperor City’s largest inn to have a seat and it was there when he first met the Young Palace Lord from Mythical Flame Palace for the first time as she passed by. He had barely caught a glimpse of a passing beauty and after that he forgot about everything totally.","Not to mention that he had forgotten the other matters which had happened that day, even the matters which happened a couple of months ago, he totally couldn’t recall clearly.","1He only remembered that he kept on cultivating and cultivating with only one thought in mind, which was to let Huang Yueli see that he had enough power to protect her, a man who could satisfy all her vanity! She could only marry him!","But these were something which he wouldn’t say.","After all, Huang Yueli had not admitted that she had feelings for him long ago so why would he bring it out? The number one top exponent had his own pride!","...","Not too long later, Li Moying’s flying ship landed in front of Sky Emperor City.","There was no array within the radius of one hundred miles outside Sky Emperor City and they didn’t allow anyone to ride on flying beasts or flying ships, nor utilise their flying Profound Skills."]},{"number":1643,"title":"Chapter 1643 - Entering the city (8)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","However, Sky Emperor City’s influential powerhouses weren’t included within the restrictions so occasionally there were still flying ships and Falcon Snow Condors.","But Li Moying had just returned and had not grasped Sky Emperor City’s current situation hence he didn’t want to attract attention so they chose to silently descend while preparing to enter the city through the normal procedures.","Huang Yueli’s right hand raised and kept the flying ship into the Sky Phoenix Ring.","Ever since she advanced into fifth stage realm, Sky Phoenix Ring’s storage area had been upgraded several times becoming larger and larger. Now it was about the size of a small village so putting a flying ship in there was enough and had space to spare.","But to be able to have the space to keep a flying ship, even in Sky Emperor City, was something which was rarely seen. Huang Yueli’s move would inevitably attract the surrounding practitioners’ attention.","Huang Yueli didn’t want to attract trouble but such a large flying ship originally could not just disappear without a trace so attracting others’ attention was something which she couldn’t help.","Luckily, among their group included a ninth stage realm top exponent like Li Moying hence ordinary practitioners totally didn’t dared to create any trouble.","Even until they reached Sky Emperor City’s towering city gates, Luo Jiyun and the others were still looking around curiously.","“The few of you, please stay put and pay the entrance fee here. One high grade spirit stone for each person.” A guard stopped them.","Luo Jiyun gave a shocked expression, “One high grade spirit stone for one person! This is daylight robbery!”","Mo Yi and the others were speechless as well.","One high grade spiritual stone was equivalent to ten thousand low grade spirit stones, enough to buy an inferior quality third tier Profound Armament, just to enter the city once! This was just too extravagant!","However, Sky Emperor City had quite a number of gates and the human traffic everyday would at least incur several hundred thousands, wasn’t this too profitable!","When the guards heard their discussions, he couldn’t help but creased his brows. He saw them coming over from a large flying ship and had thought that they were some wealthy people. Why were they kicking up such a big fuss over the entrance fee?","“Gentlemen here, this the regulations of our Sky Emperor City. If you don’t pay the entrance fee, you cannot enter the city, please comply!”","Huang Yueli knew that this was the usual regulation and didn’t say anything as she casually retrieved a handful of high grade spirit stones from her space and handed them over to the guard.","The guard counted the amount and realised that there was actually more, which should be tips for him.","His attitude immediately changed and using an extremely polite tone, he continued, “Please head in ahead gentlemen, welcome to Sky Emperor City.....”","Luo Jiyun saw the guard’s attitude which had switched from arrogance to deference as his lips twitched and couldn’t help but mumbled softly, “Money can really make the devil turn the millstone.....”","Huang Yueli turned around in amusement as she educated him, “It’s just a high grade spirit stone, is it worth it for you to act in this way! Take this and be more generous in future, don’t embarrass your Eldest Senior Brother! Your Sister-in-law, I am not lacking in money!”","Saying that, she drew out a money sack as she tossed it into Luo Jiyun’s arms.","Luo Jiyun took a look and his eyeballs almost fell out.","“This.... this....” the sack was filled not only with high grade spirit stones, but an entire sack full of medium grade spirit jades. Each piece was worth ten thousand high grade spirit stones!","Luo Jiyun’s hands started shaking, “Sister-in-law, this.... this.... is worth too much...”","Huang Yueli gasped with exasperation as she said, “Just hold on to it! In Sky Emperor City, there are plenty of chances so most practitioners are extremely snobbish! If you want others to respect you, the best way would naturally be having enough ability. But now you’re still lacking a little so you cannot afford to be too petty, otherwise you’d be bullied by everyone.”","The few of them were just chatting when they suddenly heard someone calling out to them from behind."]},{"number":1644,"title":"Chapter 1644 - The fight for the peerless genius (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Wait, the few of you please hold on, you cannot leave yet!”","They turned back in astonishment and saw an entire troop of guards dressed in uniformed Profound Armor rushing over from behind them, stopping them in their tracks.","Li Moying’s elegant sword shaped brows creased as cold intent flashed past his eyes.","“What’s the meaning of this? Trying to find trouble?”","Huang Yueli could tell that he was about to fly into a rage and hurriedly jumped out to speak, “Dear Sirs, we have already paid the entrance fee according to regulations, why do you still stop us?”","The leader heading the team took out a sedge scroll and looked at it against the light, he then took another look at Li Moying and Huang Yueli, apparently making a comparison.","Huang Yueli frowned slightly as she turned back and met Li Moying’s vision.","The both of them had the same suspicions. Could it be that... Li Moying had caught Li Lingchuan away and the news had been sent back to Leng family so quickly? Further, Leng family’s influence was so big and within such a short amount of time, they had managed to settle Sky Emperor City’s guards to help them capture them?","Logically speaking, it shouldn’t be so.","Although Leng family was said to be some “top ten clans”, but the Top Ten Clans itself was an overstatement.","In Sky Emperor City, only the Seven Sacred Lands were the genuine super powerhouses as their foundation was strong and deep with preeminent strength that no one dared to provoke them.","Other than that, the others like what Top Ten Clans, Eight large Sects or whatsoever were all self-claimed. Rather than saying that these were publicly acknowledged super powerhouses, they might as well say that they were the next in sequence forces which had gathered together to gain the right of speech.","So in essence, even if the entire Ten Clans grouped together, they still didn’t have the qualifications to speak of a single word in front of Mu Chengying.","Now just a measly last ranking Leng family could actually control Sky Emperor City’s guards? Somehow something didn’t feel quite right?","Although they were filled with suspicions, but the two of them were not feeling flustered.","Sky Emperor City originally wasn’t some place which was filled with pure and honest folkways so if they weren’t able to settle this small problem, then they can forget about continuing mingling here in future.","But Luo Jiyun and the others were apparently frightened as they exchanged glances to see the terror in one another’s eyes.","Since when had they encountered such a huge disposition of troops. That time Cui Yuan Shan spoke of how incredible Leng family was, it seemed as though they were able to crush the entire Celestial Light Sect with just one finger.","Thinking of their entire group of entourage, there was only Li Moying who was in ninth stage realm. The others’ abilities belonged to the middle and low classes in Sky Emperor City, totally unable to resist against them.","“We’re done for, finished! Could they be from the Leng family trying to create trouble for us! I’d never thought that Leng Yi Feng had such huge backing! Surely they won’t.... won’t really capture Eldest Senior Brother right?”","“Shouldn’t be that bad...” Even Mo Yi who deeply believed in Li Moying couldn’t help but get worried when he saw this.","“Master capturing that fellow is logical and reasonable, not intentionally creating any trouble! Leng family cannot just be unreasonable! If there’s really no choice.... Anyway since Li Lingchuan is still being locked behind in the carriage, should we just pass him over to Leng family, at least it’s better than being locked up the minute we enter the city!”","“Just afraid that Leng family’s people refuse to give up just like that!”","Huang Yueli heard those discussions behind her as her lips twitched, thinking of going forward to educate them.","But considering that the time wasn’t quite right, she could only endured it as she kept her mouth shut.","Just at this moment, after the team leader repeatedly verified the identity, he finally opened his mouth.","“May I ask... are you Young Master Li, Li Moying?”"]},{"number":1645,"title":"Chapter 1645 - The fight for the peerless genius (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Li Moying replied without batting an eyelid, “That’s right, what can I do for you?”","Out of their expectations, the team leader didn’t act like they expected; to abruptly capture them. On the contrary, his expression was full of praise.","“So you’re Master Li! Please kindly wait a moment longer, there’s someone who wants to meet with you.”","The team leader’s attitude was so humble which made Huang Yueli and the others extremely surprised.","Li Moying frowned as he sized up the drawing in the team leader’s hand suspiciously.","“Who is it who wants to meet me? Can you reveal the identity a little?”","The team leader hesitated, “That... anyway it’s someone from one of the powerhouse in Sky Emperor city and definitely not someone who has ill intentions towards you, so please kindly wait a little while more!”","From the equivocal answer, Li Moying replied slightly impatiently, “Since the person coming is unwilling to reveal his identity, then there’s no need for me to wait right here. It’s rather late and today I’ve just arrived in Sky Emperor City so there are just a number of things for me to settle, apologies but we’d be making a move first!”","To be able to let the most famous unparalleled top exponent in Sky Emperor City wait, other than his Li’er, there hadn’t been anyone else yet!","Looking at the team leader’s expression, it shouldn’t be Leng family who’s seeking revenge this time round.","Since that was the case, he wasn’t too interested in finding out the situation and he wasn’t interested to act like a country bumpkin who hadn’t seen the world to stay and wait for some “influential powerhouse” to meet him!","Li Moying turned around to leave and Huang Yueli merely shrugged as she hooked her arm around Li Moying’s and followed up in quick steps.","Luo Jiyun and the others apparently were slightly worried but they too, followed behind them closely.","The team leader saw that he was about to leave and hurriedly chased after them shouting out, “Master Li! Wait a minute, don’t leave! The person who wants to meet you is really someone important in Sky Emperor City, and furthermore he is very sincere in it! This is absolutely a heaven descended chance! If you don’t stay behind and wait then in future, it’d be too late for regrets!”","Hearing that, Huang Yueli seemed to have thought of something as her slender brows rose and a sliver of smile curled up on the corners of her lips.","She raised her arm and her elbow knocked against Li Moying’s as she gave a low chuckle, “I say, Moying.... from the tone, could it be that someone wants to.....”","Before she could even finish her sentence, a bright light flashed past and an imposing aura immediately swept across from their front.","The few of them stopped in their tracks and lifted their heads to take a look.","They saw an elderly man with a head full of white hair, dressed in luxurious apparel standing right in front of the both of them as he sized Li Moying up with a beaming face.","“Master Li, Miss Bai, don’t be in a hurry to leave alright? Just spend a little time having a chat with this old man, how about it?”","Li Moying’s expression was cold and solemn as he shot a fleeting glance at him but didn’t say a word.","Huang Yueli however, had a face which showed that she was thinking as she sized up the elderly man in front of her.","He was dressed in an entire set of tier grade Profound Armor and the sword which was hanging by his waist was an eighth tier upper grade Profound Weapon which looked acutely sharp.","Even in Sky Emperor City, eighth tier Profound Weapons were scarce and in the entire Armament Guild, they would only produce several hundred pieces yearly. In Sky Emperor City where there were plenty of strong practitioners, there practically wasn’t enough to meet the demand.","Hence to be able to use an eighth tier Profound Weapon reflected the status of someone very important in Sky Emperor City.","In this way, the team leader really wasn’t lying to them.","The elderly man apparently didn’t expect Li Moying’s attitude to be so arrogant but after he went into a slight blank, he didn’t show any signs of infuriation but instead he gave a smile.","“Ha Ha, Master Li is indeed as what the rumours say, extremely haughty!”"]},{"number":1646,"title":"Chapter 1646 - The fight for the peerless genius (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“But based on your innate talent, you’re worthy to be that haughty! In Sky Emperor City, youngsters with innate talent have the right to be haughty!”","The elderly man fiddled with his beard as he smiled and said, “Master Li, I truly have something important to discuss with you. How about this, not too far in front is Sky Emperor City’s famous teahouse Heavenly Aromatic House. Let me be the host and treat you all to some tea while we slowly discuss this matter, how about that?”","Li Moying’s expression remained indifferent as he said, “Apologies, I have something urgent on and have no time to have tea or whatever. If you have something really urgent, please do say it out directly now!”","The elderly man was slightly surprised as he had not expected that after he had shown 100% sincerity, he was still rejected by the other party.....","Honestly speaking, very few people would not dare to not give him face like that, not to mention that the person in front of him was a junior!","The elderly man’s heart started to feel discontented but thinking that he had unintentionally received this piece of news.... The young man in front of him had such outstanding talent that even Mu Chengying was left in this genius’s dust!","The elderly man’s anger suddenly disappeared totally.","He hurriedly said, “I’ve forgotten to introduce myself earlier. I am Feng Bozhong and I’m from the Feng family, one of the top ten clans in Sky Emperor City. This time round.... I’m here to represent my clan! Hoping to recruit Master Li. As long as Master Li is willing to join my Feng family forces, you will be able to enjoy the clan’s top rated genius’s treatment, with all the cultivation methods or resources at your disposition!”","After the elderly man self-announced his clan, his words immediately caused bursts of exclamations.","Sky Emperor City’s surroundings were filled with people and had always been crowded by a huge amount of practitioners gathering around.","Earlier when the team leader suddenly took out the portraits and stopped the entire group, that scene had already attracted quite a number of people to gather around.","Especially when Feng Bozhong appeared, it attracted all the bystanders to stay put and crowd around.","Hearing him say those words, some of them couldn’t help but start to comment.","“This elderly man is actually part of the Feng family! Feng family is the leader of the Top Ten clans and is an influential and famous powerhouse in Sky Emperor City!”","“Feng Bozhong.... Why does this name sound so familiar? Ah, I remember now! Isn’t he the clan leader for Feng family? He.... he, he... why would he be here personally?”","“This... just what situation is this? Feng family’s clan leader personally came over to the city gate to stop them, just to recruit this young man into their clan? Just what backing does this person have?”","“Heavens, it’s just too fascinating! Top ten clans are not only powerful, they also have plenty of inheritances and usually seldom recruit members outside their bloodlines. This time round their clan leader actually personally came. Could this handsome man in front of us really be some peerless genius?”","“But.... what kind of genius is worth making Clan Leader Feng come out personally? There is a younger generation in the Feng family, who is a ninth grade mid level genius!”","The crowd were whispering and commenting as they casted envious and jealous gazes onto Li Moying, all trying to guess his identity.","To be recruited by Sky Emperor City’s powerhouse to become the party whom the clan used ways and means to nurture them was the opportunity which every single young practitioner was searching for, even in their dreams.","But most of them buzzed around for many years and were still unable to attain their dreams, to join a genuine strong powerhouse to obtain the inheritance.","But now, someone had just entered the city gates and was recruited personally by the clan leader from one of the Top Ten Clans, so how could they not feel envious over this?"]},{"number":1647,"title":"Chapter 1647 - The fight for the peerless genius (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","When Feng Bozhong heard the praises from the crowd, he couldn’t help but felt complacent.","Looked like he, Feng Bozhong in Sky Emperor City was also considered as an important character. Just standing on the streets like that and so many of them actually recognised him!","This time round, just how influential Feng family was, surely Li Moying was able to understand that even without him to say it out right?","Feng Bozhong fiddled with his beard as he smiled, Master Li, we the Feng family has the utmost sincerity, so I wonder what you think of it?”","Li Moying’s expression was unfathomable.","Huang Yueli, however, almost burst out laughing!","This time round it was already very clear. The guess which she had earlier wasn’t wrong at all, this old man was here to recruit her fiancé!","Not knowing where Feng family’s clansmen heard about Li Moying’s innate talent? Sky Emperor City’s powerhouses had usually felt disdainful to even go take notice of the Four Sky Region’s geniuses wasn’t it?","But it was no wonder that Feng Bozhong was in a hurry to stop them at the city gates.","If he was indeed clear on Li Moying’s innate talent, then he naturally knew that for a peerless genius like Li Moying, the minute he entered Sky Emperor City, he wouldn’t be someone whom a mere Feng family could afford to recruit! He absolutely must hurry over to cheat Li Moying into his hands before he understood the entire situation!","Feng Bozhong was indeed flexible in his thinking.","Alas, Li Moying wasn’t some blur fool who had just entered Sky Emperor City for the very first time. On the contrary, he was Sky Emperor City’s Big Demon Lord!","Feng Bozhong’s calculations were all wrongly done.","“Clan Leader Feng, I’m sorry and we appreciate your good intentions. But we have already arranged for these few days and have no intention to join any powerhouse yet, so we hope you can understand!”","Huang Yueli knew that Li Moying couldn’t be bothered to deal with these sorts of matters so she had to stand out to reply on his behalf.","Feng Bozhong wouldn’t give up that easily as he tried his best to persuade further, “Master Li, our Feng family’s inheritance has been around for ten thousand years and we have also occupied several ore veins in the outskirts of Sky Emperor City hence the clan has a vast amount of resources especially in terms of heaven grade cultivation methods and profound skills. We also have a few ancient scrolls so as long as you nod your head, all these are at your disposal!”","Huang Yueli curbed herself from laughing out, “Clan Leader Feng, we really don’t need these! We really have something urgent and our Moying still doesn’t have any plans to lean onto any powerhouse yet so will you please let us through! How about this, now that we’re considered as acquainted, when there is a need in future, we’ll go pay you a visit!”","Feng Bozhong started to become anxious, “What urgent matters do you have to handle? You’ve just arrived at Sky Emperor City and rather than going round in circles blindly, why not just join our clan. Feng family’s name is everywhere in the entire Sky Emperor City so no matter what you need to do, you will be able to get it done easily!”","What a joke, what was meant by going to look for him in future when there’s a need?","Feng Bozhong was just too clear that the minute Li Moying entered the city and got in touch with various powerhouses, there would be something strange if he chose to join a mere Feng family by then!","Based on his innate talent which had surpassed Mu Chengying, wasn’t it as easy as lifting a finger for him to join whichever powerhouse he wanted?","Huang Yueli was not able to answer in time when Feng Bozhong suddenly thought of something and said, “I know! You’re in such a hurry to enter the city because you’re worried of the Leng family coming to find trouble for you?”","Huang Yueli blinked and asked out of surprise, “How did you know?”","Huang Yueli was surprised on how he got information on this matter but Feng Bozhong had misinterpreted, assuming that they were really afraid of the Leng family.","Feng Bozhong suddenly felt that he had grasped the crux of the problem!"]},{"number":1648,"title":"Chapter 1648 - The fight for the peerless genius (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","He hurriedly said, “Master Li, Miss Bai, both of you please be assured. I found out that you’re entering the city today from the clan leader from the Leng family. Leng family wanted to take action against Master Li so he asked me to help bribe the city guards to capture you! But he was instead lectured by me! For a genius like Master Li to be offended, how could you not exact revenge for it?”","Saying that, Feng Bozhong changed the topic.","“But, Leng family’s people have apparently not given up. Perhaps they might find other ways to deal with Master Li. But Master Li please be assured, we the Feng family definitely can deter the other top ten clans! As long as Master Li is willing to join us, we can help to settle the Leng family’s trouble!”","He said this with an impressive style.","But actually, the meaning in his words had a threatening effect in it.","What he meant was actually to hint Li Moying that he was already being forced into a corner. If he wanted to avoid Leng family from exacting revenge, then the only way was to join Feng family otherwise Feng family would not bother about this matter!","This move was well executed and if they really didn’t know the current situation which Sky Emperor City was in, they might really have fallen for his lies!","Huang Yueli didn’t know if she should laugh or cry but she finally understood that it was Cui Yuan Shan who had sold Li Moying’s matters out.","Seeing her own fiancé already showing an apparent impatient look, she hurriedly opened her mouth, “Clan Leader Feng, we.....”","Suddenly while she was still speaking, she was interrupted by someone.","“Old man Feng, you’re a reputable clan leader and instead of staying at home, why have you run out to the city gates so early in the morning. Just what are you trying to do?”","Following that a burst of laughs echoed as a silhouette appeared at the entrance of Sky Emperor City.","The person was dressed in a navy blue long robe, looking around forty plus years of age and there were two blades of moustache on top of his lips, bearing the temperament of a scholar.","But the Profound Energy fluctuations coming from him clearly told them that he was a genuine ninth stage realm eight level practitioner!","In terms of cultivation, he was above Feng Bozhong’s!","The minute he appeared, the surrounding practitioners couldn’t help but started to gasp in exasperation again.","“That’s... Cheng Zhenbo! Vice President of Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild’s Cheng Zhenbo! He is a famous character in Sky Emperor City’s sky chart! Usually it’s practically impossible to see him, why had he appeared right here today?”","“So he’s Cheng Zhenbo! I heard that other than the few who are in ninth stage realm peak, he’s the next in line whose most powerful, Not only that, he has the huge backing of Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild and has easy access to Profound Weapons and medicinal pills! In terms of battle power, he’s absolutely top rated!”","“I’d not expected that we would be able to see this legendary character today. What... is he here for?”","Everyone had a puzzled look on their faces.","Or perhaps, they already had a faint guess in their hearts but they weren’t willing to believe that such a thing could happen!","When Feng Bozhong saw Cheng Zhenbo appearing, his expression changed and it immediately turned extremely anxious and uptight.","“President Cheng, these words of yours sound strange. I can be anywhere that I want to so why can’t I be right here at the city gates? How about you, haven’t I heard a few days ago that you’re going into closed door cultivation at home and not going to meet anyone? Why have you suddenly appeared right here? Could it be that you’ve already come out of closed door cultivation so quickly?”","Feng Zhongbo’s enmity was extremely obvious.","Cheng Zhenbo saw that but merely cracked open his lips a little as he replied in ridicule, “Clan Leader Feng’s question is so interesting. I’m here for the same motive that you have as well!”"]},{"number":1649,"title":"Chapter 1649 - The fight for the peerless genius (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","This really was whatever was feared would happen!","Feng Bozhong’s heart thumped wildly for a moment, not expecting that the news of the peerless genius entering Sky Emperor City would spread so fast! Even Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild rushed over!","Originally he thought upon hearing this news from Leng family and even bribing the city gate guards was absolutely the fastest and would definitely be able to lay hands onto Li Moying before everyone else!","In the end, the development of things happened in the opposite direction of what he had expected. Li Moying was totally not easy to trick as he totally disregarded everything that he had said!","And now precisely because he was delayed for a slight moment, even Cheng Zhenbo managed to reach in time!","Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild which backed Cheng Zhenbo was a famous and reputable large powerhouse in Soaring Heavens Continent. Although they were not part of the Seven Sacred Lands, but their forces in terms of retail outlets, auction houses and business transactions firms spread throughout the entire Soaring Heavens Continent, welding a shockingly vast amount of fortune.","Although Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild didn’t have that kind of ten thousands year old inheritances from those large Sects or large clans, but as long as they had money in their hands, there was always a way to get cultivation methods and resources, not to mention a vast amount of intelligence network.","All these were something which the Feng family weren’t able to match up against.","On seeing Cheng Zhenbo appearing, Feng Bozhong knew that things were going to be troublesome.","Indeed, Cheng Zhenbo shot a provocative glance towards Feng Bozhong and turned towards Li Moying. While sizing him up for a short moment, a sense of admiration flowed within his eyes.","“Master Li, I’ve been looking forward to meeting you for a long time! You’re indeed a man of striking appearance, truly living up to one’s reputation! Even if it was Sovereign from Blue Profound Sect then, he unfortunately wasn’t able to match up to you now!”","This was the highest compliment, Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign Mu... was exactly Mu Chengying himself!","If it was any other ordinary practitioner, upon hearing such compliments, they would not be overly excited but rather shocked overboard! To be compared to Mu Chengying.... If their innate talent wasn’t enough yet being raised to such a high platform, it was simply akin to shortening their lifespan!","But Li Moying didn’t reveal any excitement nor shock, merely narrowing his eyes as he said softly, “President Cheng, you’ve overpraised me.”","Huang Yueli threw a gaze towards him and knew what exactly he was thinking.","Cheng Zhenbo actually used Mu Chengying as a topic!","Although what he said was indeed the truth but if it was fifteen years ago, no practitioners in the entire Soaring Heavens Continent would dare to treat Mu Chengying with any kind of disrespect. Not to mention having the rights to even use him as a topic!","But Mu Chengying had disappeared into “closed door cultivation” for fifteen years and all those astonishing things that he had done then had long been forgotten by most people.... otherwise in the yesteryears, even if Cheng Zhenbo wanted to die to say such things, no surrounding practitioners around him would have the guts to listen to him talk!","Thinking of this, Huang Yueli’s lips uncontrollably curled a little.","No matter what, the Big Demon Lord had already returned to his kingdom, and moreover his innate talent was much higher than before.","She wondered if those large powerhouses which were ready to make trouble found out about this, would they be shocked to death?","Cheng Zhenbo didn’t realise that something was amiss as he continued speaking.","“Master Li, let me introduce myself. I’m Cheng Zhenbo, I’m guessing that you must have heard of my name before! The wealth of Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild is something which I imagine that I shouldn’t need to explain further. We are not lacking in money, nor resources! As long as you’re willing to join Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild, we will definitely utilise the entire Guild’s power to provide you for cultivation. No matter what kind of condition you raise, how many medicinal pills, spirit stones, Profound Weapons, cultivation methods, we will be able to satisfy you!”","Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild had wealth which spoke louder than others and just this opening from Cheng Zhenbo had immediately turned Feng Bozhong into dregs."]},{"number":1650,"title":"Chapter 1650 - The fight for the peerless genius (7)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Feng Bozhong only mentioned about giving Li Moying the utmost top rate genius treatment but Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild was different. The minute they opened their mouth, it was to fulfil whatever demands he had, appearing relatively superior as compared to anyone else.","Not only that, when Cheng Zhenbo swept one glance at Feng Bozhong once again, he continued, “Furthermore, no matter what problems does Master Li have in Sky Emperor City with whichever forces, we will be able to resolve it. I just heard that Master Li seemed to have accidentally killed some direct descendant of the Leng family? This is just a small matter which could be appeased with money, so Master Li need not worry about this.”","When Feng Bozhong heard that, he almost coughed out a mouthful of blood!","Earlier in order to make Li Moying feel grateful towards him, he intentionally made the Leng family sound as though they were very incredible, as though settling this matter was a difficult task.","In the end, this Cheng Zhengbo actually made this sound so simple, as though it could be settled with just a wave of a hand.","In this way, under comparison, didn’t it mean that his Feng family was much worse off then the Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild? A matter which they found it difficult to settle, to Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild, was just a small matter which wasn’t even fit to be mentioned about!","This was simply trying to be clever but ended up with egg on his own face!","Feng Bozhong felt extremely furious and immediately stood up as he stared angrily at Cheng Zhenbo.","“President Cheng, this is just too much! Everything should be done in order of arrival! Master Li is the person whom we Feng family had taken interest in and you suddenly popped out like that, what’s the meaning of this? Poaching someone from other Sects publicly is the disruption of the society regulations. No matter how much wealth your Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild has, surely you can’t be that unreasonable right?”","Whoever knew that Cheng Zhenbo couldn’t even be bothered to look at him straight in the eyes as he continued to persuade Li Moying.","“Master Li, how is it? Do take a moment to consider this? You should be very clear that based on your innate talent, it was a sure thing that your existence in Sky Emperor City is definitely top rated. But in order to speed up your cultivation even quickly, the amount of money that you need to burn would be much more! Even if it was a powerhouse like the Top Ten Clans, they aren’t able to come out with so much money. Only we, Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild..... have this ability!”","Feng BoZhong blew his moustache with his eyes wide open as he really wished that he could send this Cheng Zhenbo who had cut right in, a flying kick!","Alas, he could only blame himself for not being fast enough and for not showing enough sincerity, even thinking of using the least price to trick Li Moying into joining their family!","With the comparison right now, even an idiot would know that he would choose to join Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild.","Li Moying listened to Cheng Zhenbo finishing his words expressionlessly before he started to open his mouth calmly, “I think both of you for thinking highly of me, but as what my fiancée had mentioned earlier, we have no intention to lean towards any powerhouse for now, my apologies.”","Cheng Zhenbo’s expression stiffened, apparently not expecting that he had actually been rejected!","This young lad really didn’t know what he was rejecting?","Feng Bozhong however heaved a sigh of relief as he almost laughed out. So what if Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild was rich and overbearing, weren’t they also unable to settle this matter?","Cheng Zhenbo did not give up as he continued, “Master Li, don’t come to a conclusion so quickly. How about this, I’ll invite you over to our Guild’s Treasure Pavilion to take a look, you can decide after you’ve.....”","As Cheng Zhenbo was endlessly trying to persuade him, suddenly, they heard gasps of exclamations coming from the crowd.","“Quickly look! What’s that?”","Quite a number of people heard that and looked over, and immediately following that, they all started screaming in shock.","“Heavens, that’s.... that’s Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s flying ship...”","“It’s no wonder they’re one of the Seven Sacred Lands in Sky Emperor City. Only a super powerhouse like this could steer their flying ship in the Sky Emperor City’s skies so arrogantly!”","“Strange? From the direction of that flying ship, it seemed to be flying towards our direction?”"]},{"number":1651,"title":"Chapter 1651 - The fight for the peerless genius (8)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Under the astonished gazes of the crowd, that huge and luxurious flying ship flew above everyone’s heads.","The flying ship lowered slightly and a silhouette flew downwards, landing right in front of Li Moying.","The man had a head full of white hair and he was holding on to a walking stick in his hands as though he was so old that he almost couldn’t walk.","But when Cheng Zhenbo and Feng Bozhong saw him, their expressions changed and bowed slightly as they cried out, “Elder Guo!”","Even Li Moying and Huang Yueli were astonished!","Because this Elder Guo’s name was Guo Zhenqing, someone whom the both of them knew. Fifteen years ago, he was already one of the famous ninth stage realm peak practitioners from Splendid Violent Heavenly Palace!","This old man’s character was extremely arrogant and they had not expected that he appeared at this place. Could it be that he was here to recruit Li Moying as well?","Li Moying and Huang Yueli exchanged glances as they both had the same helpless thought in their minds: Originally they were thinking of sneaking into the city to grasp the situation of Sky Emperor City first. Whoever knew that.... they had just entered the city and had thoroughly become famous!","This was what’s known as causing a sensation in the martial arts circle, startling a great number of people!","Among the crowd, there were apparently even more people who recognised Guo Zhenqing as their discussions became even louder. Furthermore, even more people now looked at Li Moying as though they were looking at a monster.","“Elder Guo from Splendid Violent Heavenly Palace! Soaring Heavens Continent’s Sky Chart ranking number twelve!”","“This is one of the top exponents behind the scenes in Sky Emperor City who wouldn’t reveal himself easily! He actually came here as well, surely it can’t be that... he’s also here to recruit that what Master Li right?”","“Surely not right.... Impossible right? Elder Guo’s backing is one of the Seven Sacred Lands Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace! Seven Sacred Lands.... Just what kind of place is that? Even if it was a peerless genius with ninth grade talent, he also had to pass through various assessments like ordinary practitioners before he could join them!”","“Unless.... This Master Li is a ninth grade upper talented genius!”","“Hah! What kind of joke is that? Can you even believe the things that you said? Ninth grade upper talent’s genius, in the past one hundred years, there were only two, Mu Chengying and Huang Yueli!”","“But... earlier when that President Cheng praised Master Li, he seemed to have mentioned that his innate talent was comparable to Sovereign Mu!”","“What? How is that possible? Anyway I’m not going to believe in that! Elder Guo must have another motive in his trip here! Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace had never actively recruited any genius before!”","The crowd refused to believe which was understandable.","Seven Sacred Lands were different from ordinary large powerhouses. All of them, without any exception, had ancient inheritances and the number of top exponents under their wings had accumulated since ten thousand years ago! Just a mere immature genius was commonly seen so how would they even treat him as something?","Plus the Seven Sacred Lands sang their own praises of their statuses, they wouldn’t possibly lower their heads to go beg anyone!","Not to mention Li Moying, who was just a newbie who had just entered Sky Emperor City!","However, different from the surrounding ordinary practitioners, Cheng Zhenbo and Feng Bozhong were silently anxious because they were very sure that Guo Zhenqing’s motive was ninety nine percent the same as theirs!","Those so-called “peerless” geniuses, in Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s eyes, were indeed just like that.","But, Li Moying was different!","Just twenty over years old and had already broken through the ninth stage realm stage, just what kind of innate talent was that? It was a shocking piece of news, which made one frightened to even think carefully along this line!","That year when Mu Chengying broke through to the ninth stage realm, he was almost nearing thirty years old and that had already caused a huge commotion throughout the entire Soaring Heavens Continent!"]},{"number":1652,"title":"Chapter 1652 - The fight for the peerless genius (9)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","But Li Moying was much faster than Mu Chengying by such a large margin, completely leaping upwards in one shot!","It was imaginable that it would take at most five to six years for him to promote into ninth stage realm peak, perhaps even surpassing the once number one top exponent Mu Chengying!","After some time, what would his achievements be?","Would he become the first practitioner to break through the tenth stage realm and ascend to God Realm, after so many years since the fast change of Heaven and Earth during ancient times?","This kind of genius had already surpassed everyone’s imagination and in front of him, even the Seven Sacred Lands weren’t able to sit still!","Feng Bozhong and the others felt the anger within! But they didn’t dare to say it!","Seven Sacred Lands statuses were very high in Sky Emperor City and the strength of their ability was something which the people outside the city could hardly imagine, hence he was someone whom the both of them could not afford to offend!","Moreover, since Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s people were here, they would definitely have no chance anymore so they could only watch with their eyes open as Guo Zhenqing abduct them away.","Guo Zhenqing was a man who was even more particular then Feng Zhenbo and the others hence he didn’t personally go up to fawn on Li Moying, instead he brought along two sidekicks.","A young man behind him took quick steps up ahead as he cupped his fist into the other hand and said, “Master Li, I am Wen Yikai, a direct disciple from Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace.”","He paused for a moment, waiting for Li Moying to express a shocked and adoration look.","Whoever knew that the crowd around them were already gasping in shock and astonishment but Li Moying merely casted him a look which was cold and distant, not knowing if he had heard what he said or not.","Wen Yikai’s expression turned slightly ugly as he had not expected that Li Moying to actually be that conceited!","No matter how strong Li Moying’s innate talent was, but he was after all a direct disciple of Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace. In the future when Li Moying joined their Heavenly Palace, he was considered as his Senior Brother! How could he not give him face in such a manner?","Wen Yikai was infuriated but he remembered that he was acting on Guo Zhenqing’s instructions, to treat this peerless genius with extreme deferential treatment hence he forcibly controlled his own temper and continued to speak to him in a pleasant countenance.","“Master Li, my Master had passed by today and heard about your matter. He had always been interested in young men with great innate talent and wanted to have a chat with you, so I’d like to trouble you to come over with me to meet him!”","Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace sung their own praises of their statuses so the words which they say out were unlike Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild to be so mercenary, outright and straight.","They had not even said anything about recruiting Li Moying under their wing.","But whoever present would have understood that this was Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s way of expressing their good intentions towards Li Moying!","For a moment, everyone was filled with envy.","“Heavens.... Elder Guo had really come for this Master Li!”","“To make Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s Elder come over to recruit him personally, just what backing does this man have!”","“Don’t know, I really don’t know! This is the first time I’ve seen this man appearing in Sky Emperor City! If he was some old man in Sky Emperor City, he wouldn’t absolutely be some intricate nameless youngster which no one could recognise! So today must be the first day that he had entered the city!”","“First day entering the city and he already attracted Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s attention! Just what kind of innate talent does he have? Really when one is compared to another, one would die from it!”","“Great innate talent, and able to join one of the Seven Sacred Lands, this Master Li’s future is limitless!”","When Wen Yikai heard these discussions, he somehow felt slightly imbalanced inside.","Speaking of that, he himself was had ninth grade lower innate talent and that year, he had begged shamelessly, passing several rounds of assessments before he was able to formally become a disciple to Guo Zhenqing as his Master but now Guo Zhenqing actually came over personally to take Li Moying as his disciple?","This young lad looked very young, with his hair not fully grown yet."]},{"number":1653,"title":"Chapter 1653 - The fight for the peerless genius (10)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Other than being exceptionally good looking which would make any ladies who saw him going weak in the knee, there didn’t seem any other exceptional part about him?","Could he really be more powerful than himself?","Wen Yikai silently decided that in future after Li Moying became his Junior Brother, he would ‘take good care’ of him, to let this fellow know just how deep the concrete details of Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace was, and that he wasn’t the only genius there!","Wen Yikai was planning these in his mind but by surprise, he suddenly heard Li Moying’s cold and distant voice ringing from above his head.","“Master Wen, I appreciate your Master’s kind intentions but I have no interest to meet with him, please leave!”","Wen Yikai went into a blank, “..... what did you say?!”","He simply felt that he must have heard wrongly!","Because this matter should absolutely not have happened!","An Elder from one of the Seven Sacred Lands came here personally and even sent his beloved disciple under his wing to introduce themselves. To any young men in Sky Emperor City, it was an utmost glory! Even if the recipient was a ninth grade talented genius, that person should regard it as an honour and immediately run over to fawn on them with jolting buttocks.","Wen Yikai had not expected that there would be anyone who would reject the meeting!","Li Moying’s gaze brushed past Feng Bozhong and the others and he calmly replied, “We’ve delayed our journey for quite some time and I understand all your intentions but I’ve also made things very clear, I will not lean towards any of your forces.”","When Wen Yikai heard what he said, he suddenly came to realise the truth.","It really wasn’t him having any hallucination but this so called peerless genius had water in his brain, otherwise he was really crazy!","“Do you know what you’re saying? Did you think Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace can be compared to the Feng family, that kind of small powerhouse? This is one of the Seven Sacred Lands! Do you know just how many Elders in the ninth stage realm do we Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace have? How many ancient historical inheritances that we have? How many exclusive cultivation resources?”","Wen Yikai raised his voice.","He felt that if Li Moying didn’t had any issue with his head, then he must be a country bumpkin who had just entered the city and wasn’t sure of what’s going on, to actually put Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace together on the same level as Feng family that kind of forces!","However, even after he exhausted his shouting to advertise, Li Moying still wasn’t moved at all as his brows rose, “So what about that?”","Wen Yikai’s eyes turned wide, “So what about that? Do you know that is the opportunity which so many practitioners had dreamt of??”","Li Moying replied indifferently, “Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace is indeed extraordinary but it doesn’t suit me. I can only apologise as a reply!”","Saying that, he held Huang Yueli’s hand in his and calmly replied, “Goodbye” as he prepared to leave.","Everyone had an extremely astonished gaze as they stared fixedly at his silhouette, watching as he carefully held his fiancée and brought her into his arms evading the crowd.","No one dared to believe that Li Moying had really rejected the good intentions from Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace!","Even though Guo Zhenqing was just standing not too far away, he did not even head over immediately to meet him!","Wasn’t this just a little too arrogant! Not even placing a ninth stage realm peak top practitioner, who did he thought he was? What kind of status did Elder Guo had, for him to treat him with such disdain. Under his rage, he might even just kill him with one strike!","As expected, the crowd’s mind had just flashed by this thought when they saw Guo Zhenqing’s figure moving.","A blurry bright silhouette flashed past and he immediately stopped Li Moying in his tracks.","“Lad, you’re indeed bold! Do you know who I am?”","Guo Zhenqing’s face was filled with wrinkles but his eyes were exceptionally bright with an imposing glint."]},{"number":1654,"title":"Chapter 1654 - Who will win (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Just as Guo Zhenqing was talking, he silently unleashed the Profound Energy within his body.","Strong suppression enveloped the entire region.","“Pfft!””Pfft!””Pfft!”","The weaker practitioners around them had immediately thrown up blood and fainted!","Li Moying’s expression remained indifferent as though he had not suffered much suppression.","The influence on one’s Profound Energy suppression was first determined on one’s cultivation and then followed by the intensity of their meridians.","The more stable the foundation and more tenacious it was in talented practitioners, the more they were able to take the suppression from practitioners who were of higher cultivations than them.","Based on Li Moying’s current god grade innate talent, even if a powerful practitioner from God Realm descended, it would be difficult to use suppression to cause him any harm, moreover Guo Zhenqing was just a ninth stage realm peak practitioner?","The number of practitioners who were throwing up blood around them were increasing and quite a number of them could not withstand the suppression from such a peerless top exponent hence they had all fallen onto the ground twitching as they foamed at the mouth.","If it was any other Sect’s forces, on seeing so many practitioners around them being affected, in order not to cause too much of a chaos, they would definitely have stopped by now.","However, Guo Zhenqing didn’t even bother to cast a look at those weak ones as he had once again increased the degree of his Profound Energy, directly casting towards Li Moying’s direction!","The life and death of those “weak” surrounding them was of no concern to him at all!","Seven Sacred Lands.... Was just this overbearing and conceited!","Li Moying’s expression met Guo Zhenqing’s vision coldly.","He knew for sure that Guo Zhenqing would make a move to test him. Part of the reason was because he couldn’t accept Li Moying’s rejection whereas on the other hand, which was the more important reason, it was definitely to test his potential!","After all, that rumour regarding Li Moying’s innate talent was just too ridiculous!","Unless he witnessed it with his own eyes, otherwise anyone would have their suspicions.","Li Moying narrowed his eyes slightly as numerous thoughts flashed past his mind swiftly.","If he were to exhibit his potential right here now, it was possible that Guo Zhenqing would not be willing to let him off even more so! But if he had to pretend to not go up against him and lose in a sorry state.... Even if it was just a pretence, based on his conceited pride, it was totally unacceptable!","While Li Moying was thinking it through, Guo Zhenqing had increased his Profound Energy’s suppression by another notch!","Even a ninth stage realm practitioner like Feng Bozhong found it hard to sit or stand still.","Just at this moment, Guo Zhenqing suddenly let out an exclamation “Hmm” as his vision shifted from Li Moying to his side.","Li Moying’s heart jolted as he turned around to look at Huang Yueli.","He saw this young lass having a slightly pale expression but she was still standing firm on the ground, totally not falling down or throwing up blood.","“This young lady.....” Guo Zhenqing suddenly opened his mouth!","If Huang Yueli was a ninth stage realm practitioner, this expression could only be said to be just passable, and not attract Guo Zhenqing’s attention.","However, the Profound Energy fluctuations from her apparently meant that.... she only had a mere fifth stage realm later stage cultivation!","Honestly speaking, based on her age, to be in the fifth stage realm already wasn’t bad at all but just based on cultivation alone, in Sky Emperor City, she was only considered to be middle class and below.","The surrounding practitioners who had the same cultivation level as her had all fallen down twitching and fainted. But although she was in the centre of suppression, she still remained standing properly.....","This innate talent.... was indeed shocking, probably not too far off from the man standing next to her!","When Li Moying saw Guo Zhenqing’s bright eyes, his heart silently sighed!","This round things weren’t going so well. No matter if he moved or not, none of them were going to be able to leave!"]},{"number":1655,"title":"Chapter 1655 - Who will win (2)","paragraphs":["Li Moying took a side step and blocked himself in front of Huang Yueli.","On one hand, it was to obstruct a large part of Guo Zhenqing’s Profound Energy suppression while on the other hand, it was to block the investigative vision which this old man had landed onto Li’er.","“Elder Guo, you’re looking for my fiancée, what may we do for you?”","Guo Zhenqing met Li Moying’s cold gloomy eyes and went into a slight blank, “.....your fiancée?”","It was now that he finally recalled that it was once mentioned in the report regarding Li Moying’s data, that this astonishingly peerless genius had already gotten engaged at such a young age!","But Guo Zhenqing totally didn’t bother to take notice of his fiancée’s biodata at all.","From what he thought, if Li Moying indeed had that kind of rumoured innate talent, then even a top talented lady in Sky Emperor City would only be suited to be his concubine, what more for a young lass who had popped out from some countryside?","After Li Moying had entered Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace, the Sect would definitely arrange for other ladies with much outstanding innate talent for them to engage in double cultivation.","A country lass from the South Sky Region was not even qualified to be his bondmaid!","But if Li Moying really liked her that much, taking her in as a servant to warm up his bed wasn’t impossible.","With this first impression which lasted in his mind, Guo Zhenqing totally wouldn’t admit that Li Moying had a fiancée so naturally he wouldn’t go take notice of what her innate talent or cultivation was at!","It was right until he met her in person that he realised that.... he had thought wrongly!","Furthermore it was extremely ridiculously wrong!","Based on fifth stage realm cultivation to easily deflect a ninth stage realm practitioner’s suppression, that kind of innate talent was at least ninth grade upper talent and above! There wouldn’t be a second in the entire Sky Emperor City!","No wonder Li Moying was in such a hurry to tie her down, so.... he wasn’t silly nor was he indulging in her female charms but he had already long knew that the young lady beside him was the only one whose existence was compatible with his!","(Li Moying: What on earth do you know? This Young Master here is indulging in her female charms.....)","Guo Zhenqing was instantly excited!","What was called cake dropping from the sky? This was it!","He had not expected that he came because of Li Moying alone but he had discovered two peerless geniuses at one go instead!","The more fortunate thing was these two were a couple and their relationship was really good. As long as he could settle Li Moying, he would definitely be able to take in this young lass into his wing as well, which was killing two birds with one stone.","To take in two ninth grade talent disciples.....","If it really went according to his way, Guo Zhenqing would probably wake up from his dream while laughing!","Thinking of this, Guo Zhenqing totally discarded the stance of a Seven Sacred Land Elder and kept away all the Profound Energy which he had unleashed. His wrinkled face revealed a smile as he took a step upwards and his attitude instantly became unusually amiable and kindly.","“Master Li, Miss Bai, which powerhouse do you intend to lean towards? Which area does Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace make you dissatisfied? Or could it be that you have other conditions? Feel free to speak your mind and let’s discuss it! Why must you keep people at a distance of one thousand miles away the minute you voice out?”","When Guo Zhenqing said these, those practitioners who had not fainted all opened their eyes wide as their chins all fell onto the ground.","This, this, this... just what situation was this?","Why had Elder Guo who had always been cold, aloof and arrogant suddenly had a change of face?","Hearing this tone, he seemed to be getting into Li Moying’s good books? Just what was wrong with this?","Li Moying had totally not hesitated to reject his recruitment so shouldn’t Guo Zhenqing be throwing a rage and killing him with one palm strike? Why was it that he actually smiled instead?"]},{"number":1656,"title":"Chapter 1656 - Who will win (3)","paragraphs":["Li Moying knew clearly that Guo Zhenqing had taken interest in his Li’er for sure.","This old man’s sight isn’t too bad, but unfortunately he had misjudged the scenario wrongly.","Li Moying shook his head without any hesitation, “Elder Guo, we really don’t wish to raise any conditions but we just merely don’t want to join Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace...”","Guo Zhenqing frowned, apparently not believing in what he said.","“Mister Li, we are upright people so we won’t say unclear things! You and your fiancée have arrived in Sky Emperor City, certainly to seek more chances and to seek a breakthrough in your way of cultivation! Based on your innate talent, to breakthrough, you’re merely lacking in cultivation methods, inheritances and various resources and all these.... are exactly our Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s forte!”","“Although among the Seven Sacred Lands, we Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace had always been the lowest key clan, but in terms of inheritances and resources, we are in no way inferior to the other few families! Moreover I can guarantee that you and your fiancé will obtain Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s full support, choosing freely from any cultivation method or resources which you want!”","The minute he said that, it caused another bustle.","The conditions which Guo Zhenqing had raised actually wasn’t much different from Cheng Zhenbo but the amount of money involved was miles apart.","Soaring Havens Merchant Guild’s inheritance and resources, were after all limited.","But Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace as one of the Seven Sacred Lands, the number of inheritances which they helmed were as vast as the deep sea, innumerable.","Many ancient cabala which seemed to have been lost from an outsider’s view, could all be found in the Scripture Depository.","However, in such a large powerhouse, inheritances were also hard to obtain as the management was extremely strict. Even for direct disciples, it was necessary to use the Clan’s contributions to exchange for it.","Now Guo Zhenqing actually made the promise of choosing freely as they wished, just what kind of concept was that?","Even if he was Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s Elder, not everyone had this kind of authority! If this went out, it would make all the practitioners in Sky Emperor City envy them to death!","Everyone assumed that when Li Moying heard this condition, he would definitely not hesitate any further and agree to it immediately.","This was a rare opportunity which could not be found easily and once they’ve missed it, how would there be a second time?","Even if Li Moying really didn’t want to incline towards any forces but he would surely change his mind at this time right?","Even Luo Jiyun, Mo Yi and the rest also felt that Li Moying would nod his head!","Whoever knew that when Li Moying heard that, the expression on his face did not change as he resolutely shook his head.","“Elder Guo, I’ve already made things very clear! No matter what conditions you offer, it’s impossible for me to join the Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace!”","“You.....”","Guo Zhenqing also couldn’t breathe!","As Sky Chart’s twelve ranked top exponent, he didn’t have many opponents in the entire Sky Emperor City so whichever practitioner saw him wouldn’t shiver in fear and trepidation, treating him like an Emperor?","How many years had it been since he had automatically expressed any good intent towards anyone?","Whoever knew that he had already got off his high horse and yet Li Moying actually refused to give any face to him?","On hearing the surrounding’s whisperings, Guo Zhenqing’s old face couldn’t hang on any further!","“Good, you’re indeed a peerless genius who had appeared once every ten thousand years, indeed conceited! A pity, no matter how high your innate talent is, your wings have yet to grow and you’re being too arrogant! Since you refuse to listen to my kind words, then don’t blame me for being nasty!”","Guo Zhenqing couldn’t take his loss of face as his expression changed and the Profound Energy in his body suddenly gathered in an instant as he abruptly struck out!","A ninth stage realm practitioner’s penetrative and overbearing Profound Energy suddenly struck out towards Li Moying!"]},{"number":1657,"title":"Chapter 1657 - Who will win (4)","paragraphs":["Momentarily, intense Profound Energy fluctuations forced the surrounding practitioners to keep on retreating.","Bursts of shrill cries filled the sky and a flash of striking bright light enveloped with shocking power rushed towards Li Moying!","This burst of turbulent surge of Profound Energy was like flood waters. Not only was it extremely overbearing, it also blocked off Li Moying’s up, down, left right, all directions as it all charged towards the position which he was standing at.","The minute the bursts of energy closed in around him, Li Moying would be wrapped in between the Profound Energy causing instantaneous injuries all over.","Guo Zhenqing had a cold smile on his face as he stared intently at Li Moying, just waiting to see his dishevelled look after he was struck!","However, Li Moying merely casted a slight glance at him and his right finger pointed upwards as he lightly pointed in mid-air!","A word came out of his mouth softly, “Break!”","Following his action, Guo Zhenqing’s burst of Profound Energy actually burst in accordance with his command as an intense explosive sound was heard in mid-air, causing the surrounding few blocks of houses nearby to suffer from the explosion!","Whereas Li Moying himself who was standing in the middle of the Profound Energy storm was totally unharmed.","On the contrary, Guo Zhenqing suffered the backlash from his own Profound Skill which hurt his chest as his blood started churning, almost throwing up blood.","“You.... you... how is this possible??”","Guo Zhenqing stared at him with his eyes wide open fixedly, totally unable to believe what he had just seen!","He had intentionally shown off his might in front of Li Moying, to let him see his own ability hence when he made a move, he had used the Profound Skill which had set a name for himself, something which he was most proud of – River Convergence Sea Palm Strike!","But Guo Zhenqing’s motive was still to take him in as a disciple hence he didn’t want to cause any serious damage to Li Moying so he only used thirty percent of his energy.","But even so, this move was still exceedingly powerful because this was Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s exclusive god grade Profound Skill which was passed down from an ancient inheritance!","Ordinary practitioners from small forces, even if their cultivation reached ninth stage realm ninth level, they wouldn’t have any resistance against this kind of astonishingly destructive power.","Whereas Li Moying was only at ninth stage realm first level where his ability was miles apart from Guo Zhenqing! Furthermore he came from a small Sect in South Sky Region, hence he couldn’t possibly have seen any kind of god grade Profound Skill.","How could he possibly have such precise sight to be able to see through the only Achilles’ heel in just a flash of thought, and even pinpointed it exactly in just one move?","How would Guo Zhenqing ever know that Li Moying was not some ignorant young lad from a small Sect, but he was the most knowledgeable Big Demon Lord in the entire Soaring Heavens Continent!","Just Guo Zhenqing himself, he had already been beaten hands down by Mu Chengying so just how much skills did he had, how would Li Moying possibly not know?","But in the eyes of those who didn’t know the truth, this scene was just simply too shocking!","A newly arrived freshman in Sky Emperor City, actually didn’t suffer any losses under Guo Zhenqing, and even easily blocked his turbulent move?","This kind of genius... was simply unheard of!","Guo Zhenqing’s elderly face started to be filled with an embarrassing red shade, feeling that his face was thoroughly lost!","At the same time, he valued Li Moying’s innate talent even further as his thirst to take him under his wing grew.","He gave a slight cough as he covered up and said, “This young lad, your... power of comprehension is indeed not bad at all, and your innate talent has passed by me! How about taking a few more strikes to try it out?”","His skillful words made the surrounding practitioners reveal an enlightened look.","“So.... Elder Guo was just testing Master Li’s ability! That palm strike had probably not even used fifty percent of his strength, no wonder he could take it on so easily!”"]},{"number":1658,"title":"Chapter 1658 - Who will win (5)","paragraphs":["Chapter 1658: Who will win (5)","“Elder Guo really gave a lot of thought into this!”","“That Master Li is able to get such nurturing from Elder Guo, it’s really his blessing for three lifetimes!”","Under everyone’s praises, Guo Zhenqing finally found back some face as his expression seemed slightly better.","He fiddled with his beard as he put on an unfathomable look and said, “Master Li, have you thought it through already? If you haven’t, then I will continue to show you my moves!”","Huang Yueli looked at his pretence and couldn’t help but laughed out.","Luckily the bustle from their surroundings overpowered her voice hence Guo Zhenqing didn’t notice it at all.","Huang Yueli shook her head as she was also shocked by Guo Zhenqing’s thick skin! In the past she had always thought that this old man was especially pretentious and from the looks of it now, it seemed that it was really so.....","But from his stance that revealed his unwillingness to forgive, could it be that he really intended to forcibly bring her and Li Moying away? Now was the sounding out phase which was still ok, but if they really started to fight, just based on her and Li Moying’s current ability, no matter what they wouldn’t be able to fight with a ninth stage realm peak practitioner!","Adding on to the fact that Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s flying ship had stopped right above their heads.....","Looked like they had to think of an idea to get away.","Just as she was racking her brains, she suddenly felt a tug on her sleeve from behind.","Huang Yueli turned around and saw Luo Jiyun moving close up as he whispered, “Lil Sister-in-law, you.... you’d better hurry and persuade Eldest Senior Brother!”","Huang Yueli went into a blank, “Persuade him? Persuade him on what?”","Luo Jiyun frowned, apparently not expecting that Huang Yueli would be that dazed.","“sigh! Lil Sister-in-law, why are you also.... do you guys know or not, Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s recruitment, what does that mean?”","“I’ve heard of the practitioners in Sky Emperor City mentioned that Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace is one of the Seven Sacred Lands but they are one of the top forces in the entire Soaring Heavens Continents! All the geniuses who are able to join the Seven Sacred Lands treat it as an honour and every ten years when the Seven Sacred Lands recruit disciples, many geniuses from everywhere all rushed over, just fighting and hoping to gain a quota!”","“Now Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s Elder actually personally came over to invite Eldest Senior Brother, wanting to take him in as a disciple! Moreover from his tone, it seemed that he seems to be one of the top rated top exponent in Sky Emperor City! Why wouldn’t Eldest Senior Brother agree to it? What is he still waiting for? If he misses this town, then he won’t come across this shop anymore!”","Luo Jiyun tweaked his ears and scratched his cheek as he was so anxious that he kept stomping his feet.","He was really feeling anxious for Li Moying!","This was the Seven Sacred Lands! Moreover the minute he joined them he would become an Elder’s direct disciple, freely choosing from the cultivation methods or resources!","Who could offer better conditions than these?","Luo Jiyun really couldn’t understand what his own Eldest Senior Brother was still hesitating about?","Even the usually composed Mo Yi couldn’t sit still, as he lowered his voice and asked, “Third Miss, why does Master refuse to go to Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace? This Elder Guo is really very sincere.....”","They really couldn’t understand...Li Moying came to Sky Emperor City, wasn’t it for the sake of formally becoming an apprentice to a master to cultivate?","Why didn’t he just follow the flow and joined Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace?","Huang Yueli didn’t know if she should laugh or cry. She had some dealings with Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace in her past life so did she need them to tell her about their condition?","She helplessly said, “Can all of you have some confidence in Moying... he definitely has some arrangement of his own so you need not worry.”","A mere Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace had made them so unperturbed already. If they found out about the ultimate place which they were going to end up at, the legendary number one Sacred Lands in every practitioner’s heart – Blue Profound Sect, wouldn’t they be so shocked that they would faint?"]},{"number":1659,"title":"Chapter 1659 - The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 1659: The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (1)","By now, Guo Zhenqing had already lost his patience.","The surrounding practitioners didn’t know but he understood it very clearly. Li Moying was young and had lofty aspirations with excellent innate talent hence it was reasonable for him to be this conceited!","Towards this kind of peerless genius, he could only use absolute power to convince him totally!","Hence Guo Zhenqing didn’t hesitate any further as he gave a light cough, “Mister Li, this old man is going to strike again!”","He had decided that this time round, he must absolutely display his absolute power to let Li Moying understand his incredibility!","Whoever knew that his words had just fallen when a resonant neigh was heard! Immediately following that was the sound of the fluttering of wings.","Guo Zhenqing had already extended his right hand halfway as he stopped in mid-air, entirely stunned!","Because in the entire Sky Emperor City, powerhouses which had special authority to fly in the skies could be counted with one’s fingers but amongst them, the only one who didn’t require a mechanism to operate the flying ship but insisted on using flying beasts to pull the ship was...","The fluttering of wings sound got nearer and nearer, and also more and more distinct.","The flying beasts which pulled the boat were entirely white Ink Crown Snow Condors. Other than the ink coloured crown, tip of wings and tail feathers, the other parts of it were of pure snow white colour.","Every Ink Crown Snow Condor’s wings extended to at least twenty meters long and when so many of them extended their wings, it hid the sky and covered the earth, hiding a large portion of the sky above everyone’s heads, causing a part of the region to turn dark.","Ink Crown Snow Condors were genuine eighth grade magical beasts. Not only were they flying speed extremely swift, their attack power was also shockingly incredible!","Ordinary ninth stage realm practitioners might not even be able to escape from an Ink Crown Snow Condor alive!","But such valiant flying beasts were just like ordinary horses right now, being reared as they were sheathed with ropes to pull the ship.","Furthermore, it wasn’t just one or two but an entire fleet of thirty six of them!","A large majority of practitioners had never seen this stance as their eyes widened like full moons with their mouths agape, staring blanking into the sky, all assuming that their conscious weren’t clear and they had developed hallucinations.","But when the trio Guo Zhenqing, Cheng Zhenbo and Feng Bozhong saw that flying ship above everyone’s heads, they were so frightened that their legs almost turned into jelly!","“This is... This is Sovereign Mu’s Snow Cloud Sky Ship!”","There was only one in the entire Sky Emperor City who used Ink Crown Snow Condors to pull the flying ship and that was.... Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign Mu, number one top exponent in Soaring Heavens Continents Mu Chengying’s personal use flying ship!","In the past whenever this flying ship appeared, numerous practitioners would be frightened out of their wits as they knelt down onto the ground but this flying ship had not appeared for the past fifteen to sixteen years hence those ordinary practitioners who had just entered the city had not recognised it.","But for those top exponents who had established themselves for a long time, it was impossible for Guo Zhenqing and the others to not recognise it.","Just what was going on? Could it be that the unparalleled peak practitioner that year had reappeared in Sky Emperor City??","Guo Zhenqing and the others looked at one another in dismay as all they could see from each other’s eyes were shock and surprise.","This was impossible right? Didn’t they all say that Mu Chengying had entered Qi Deviation when he was in closed door cultivation and there was an eighty percent chance that his bones had turned into ashes?","Even Huang Yueli widened her eyes in surprise.","She was the most familiar with this flying ship because this was the most complex ninth tier Profound Armament which she had refined personally.","Snow Cloud Sky Ship required eighth grade magical beasts to pull the ship absolutely not because it was glamourous but because the internal structure was just too complex and if it had to be operated with mechanics, then it would simply be too heavy!"]},{"number":1660,"title":"Chapter 1660 - The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (2)","paragraphs":["In order to maintain the best condition of the flying ship, they decided on using Ink Crown Snow Condors to pull the ship.","In this way, not only would it lessen the weight, it would also raise the flying speed to a new limit! In a flash, it would reach a hundred miles!","This was one of the most delighted words of Huang Yueli’s and only Blue Profound Sect had the ability to tame so many Ink Crown Snow Condors to materialise her concept.","Huang Yueli raised her head and observed for a moment then tugged Li Moying’s back as she whispered, “Why had the Snow Cloud Sky Ship appeared here as well? Have you asked Blue Profound Sect’s people to come for reinforcement?”","Li Moying nodded his head and lowered his voice as he leaned towards her ear, “Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s Old Man Guo has his sights on us and earlier his disciple had ran away secretly, apparently to look for reinforcements. If we don’t have any reinforcements, then we can forget about leaving! If we were really captured to Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace, then things would take a difficult turn.....”","Huang Yueli looked at his slightly frowning face and she couldn’t help but burst out into laughter.","No wonder Li Moying was at a loss.","If the two of them were forcibly brought back to Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace, then ultimately he would still require the Four Great Guardians to pick them up, then they would totally not be able to keep low key at all.","The worst of it all was that Li Moying’s identity would be exposed sooner or later and if his capture to Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s matter was exposed, it would be the only stain towards his entire wise times. If this was known to anyone else, they would probably laugh their tooth off, it was really damaging to the number one top exponent’s pride.....","Li Moying stared at his black bellied little fox in his arms, “You’re still laughing!”","He really couldn’t wait to take a bite off her. Her own fiancé was stuck in a difficult position and yet she was still gloating over his misfortune? She was really a little thing with no conscience!","Huang Yueli stopped laughing, “Who asked you to be so genius? Now you’re finally famous eh?”","Li Moying pinched her gently at her waist, “My genius fiancée’s contributions wouldn’t go unnoticed as well!”","Under everyone’s awestruck gazes, the Snow Cloud Sky Ship slowly landed above everyone’s heads.","It was until now that a few practitioners finally recognised the huge totem at the bottom of the Snow Cloud Sky Ship.","“Take a look quickly! That’s.... the emblem of Blue Profound Sect! This is Blue Profound Sect’s flying ship? No wonder.... no wonder it’s so eye-catching!”","“Heavens, isn’t Blue Profound Sect very mysterious and rarely appeared in Sky Emperor City? Now it actually appeared with great fanfare in the city entrance? What big matter is happening?”","“Could it be... could it be.....surely it isn’t like what I’m guessing right?”","“What is your guess?”","“Could it be that Blue Profound Sect has the same idea in mind with Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace, just to recruit that Mister Li??”","“Impossible, this is absolutely impossible! What kind of place is the Blue Profound Sect? That is the most sacred land among the Sacred Lands! Even ninth stage realm peak practitioners can forget about joining them easily and Sovereign Mu had never personally recruited anyone before! How would he personally send anyone over for a genius?”","“But... if it’s not like this, why would Blue Profound Sect’s flying ship suddenly appear at this place?”","Everyone’s vision started to float uncontrollably towards Li Moying.","Everyone kept on pondering in their minds, guessing just what was his background!","Why did he attract so many powerhouses’ attention on the first day of his entry to the city, moreover the backing just got bigger and bigger!","Now even the Blue Profound Sect was alarmed!","Just at this moment, a ramp was slowly released from the side of the flying ship and a man’s silhouette appeared in mid air!","Guo Zhenqing and the others shivered all over as they immediately turned their gazes towards that figure."]},{"number":1661,"title":"Chapter 1661 - The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (3)","paragraphs":["By the time they saw the incoming person clearly, they all heaved a sigh of relief.","The person who appeared at the top of the ramp was not Mu Chengying, but the leader of his Four Great Guardians – Cang Po Jun.","Blue Profound Sect’s clansmen were filled with plenty of people with power and Mu Chengying’s most trusted Four Great Guardians were all ninth stage realm peak practitioners. Cang Po Jun was ranked eight on the Sky Chart, and his potential was even higher than Guo Zhenqing.","Cang Po Jun naturally wasn’t some easy going person but no matter what, he wasn’t Mu Chengying himself.","After Guo Zhenqing and the others saw him, the stone in their hearts was finally let go by a chunk.","If it really was Mu Chengying who had appeared, it would really scare these people to death alive!","Heavens knew just how much that shockingly powerful king with no match had increased in his ability to what degree after so many years of closed door cultivation?","For the past ten over years, many of them had assumed that he was dead and had secretly done some things behind his back and if he really met with it personally, the only end result was death with no burial grounds!","Luckily, luckily, they were only scaring themselves.","The one who appeared on the Snow Cloud Sky Ship was only Cang Po Jun!","Even so, Guo Zhenqing and the others still felt a little uneasy as they kept sizing up their options while staring at the flying ship continuously.","After all, the Snow Cloudy Sky Ship was Mu Chengying’s personal use flying ship in the past and even if it was his most trusted aide Cang Po Jun, he didn’t have the guts to use it privately.....","Now that he dared to sit in this flying ship, was Mu Chengying really dead or not? Or... was Mu Chengying on the ship, just now showing himself?","Just as Guo Zhenqing and the others were being apprehensive, Cang Po Jun had already led his subordinates, landing onto the ground.","Guo Zhenqing and the others immediately swarmed upwards as they kept fawning on him.","“Sir Po Jun, we haven’t met for a long time! How have you been!”","“It’s been some time since we last met, Sir Po Jun’s cultivation seemed to have advanced.... Congratulations!”","“I was just thinking of heading over to Blue Profound Sect some other day to meet with Sir, I’d not expected that we would meet here so coincidentally!”","Guo Zhenqing was still considered alright as he politely cupped his fist into his other hand but Cheng Zhenbo and Feng Bozhong ran over rather dog leggily as they were just short of cleaning Cang Po Jun’s shoes for him.","Cang Po Jun seemed as though he didn’t hear their flattery as he didn’t even shift his sight and headed straight upwards.","Everyone involuntarily retreated as they opened up a path for him.","Cang Po Jun walked towards Li Moying and when he was just a few steps away, he stopped and sized up the young lad in front of his eyes.","After his rebirth, Li Moying’s current looks was simply too young and moreover the imposing manner from him, although to an ordinary practitioner, was already extremely powerful but to Cang Po Jun’s impression of that unparallel strong practitioner, he seemed to be just short of that little bit.","Just as Cang Po Jun was hesitant, Li Moying abruptly lifted his eyes and met with his. The bitter frost beneath his eyes appeared and that severe and fearful murderous intent was so realistic that it made one feel fear all over!","Cang Po Jun’s body shivered as his legs turned soft, almost kneeling down right there!","This familiar gaze and temperament, he absolutely would not recognise it wrongly... this was Mu Chengying’s reincarnation!","Just as Cang Po Jun was about to kneel on the ground, Li Moying suddenly spoke out.","“Sir Po Jun, what may I do for you?”","That cold voice which bore the suppressing feeling that assimilated one’s will and soul made Cang Po Jun’s brain buzzed!","When he heard Li Moying actually greeting him as “Sir”, he suddenly regained his composure recalling the instructions that Li Moying had sent to him in his letter, to not expose his identity in public."]},{"number":1662,"title":"Chapter 1662 - The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (4)","paragraphs":["Cang Po Jun hurriedly steadied himself as he forcibly stood upright.","But in outsiders’ eyes, his earlier action was a little too strange, as though he wasn’t able to walk steadily, almost falling down flat on his face.","Huang Yueli almost burst out laughing again. It was simply like a mouse seeing a cat!","But this had also verified just how powerful Mu Chengying was then. Even after so many years, he was still able to make his subordinates fall under his awe-inspiring ability!","Cang Po Jun was stared coldly by Li Moying and he shivered, instinctively feeling that he had almost messed up the task which he was given.","He hurriedly mended the pen after the sheep were lost as he gave a slight cough and put on an arrogant posture.","“You are Master Li? Since you already know who I am, then I need not give any more explanations. With respect to Sovereign Mu’s orders, I’m here to invite Master Li back to Blue Profound Sect.”","When those words were heard, the surrounding practitioners’ eyes almost all popped out!","They had not expected that Cang Po Jun’s appearance right here, was actually... actually really to recruit Li Moying!","Just what kind of innate talent did this Li guy had, even Blue Profound Sect came up and expressed their good intentions!","Guo Zhenqing and the others felt as though they were struck by lightning!","They had already long guessed Cang Po Jun’s intentions and knew that since Blue Profound Sect’s Great Guardian had appeared, the bunch of them would definitely not have any more chance, which wasn’t so surprising.","What was really shocking was Cang Po Jun’s sentence, “With respects to Sovereign Mu’s orders”!","Hearing the meaning in his words, could it really mean that Mu Chengying had really come out of his closed door cultivation?","Li Moying pretended to consider for a short moment and nodded his head, “Since that’s the case, will Sir Po Jun please lead the way!”","He couldn’t be bothered to put on an act any further because based on Blue Profound Sect’s status, no matter how arrogant the geniuses were, they all treated entering Blue Profound Sect as an honour. His sudden change of mind would not make anyone feel surprised at all.","Cang Po Jun wasn’t willing to continue acting as well because being greeted by his own Sovereign with a word “Sir” made his spine felt chilly every single time he heard that.","He hurriedly nodded his head in a fluster, “Master Li please come along with me!”","Saying that, he turned around and wanted to leave, thinking of leaving this awkward place.","On seeing the both of them about to leave, Guo Zhenqing stood up in a hurry and he shot upwards quickly and asked, “Sir Po Jun, please... please wait a moment! This old man has a word of enquiry.”","Cang Po Jun’s footsteps took a halt, “Elder Guo, today it indeed was your Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace who had reached here first but Master Li had chosen Blue Profound Sect, this is.....”","“No no no, this old man here doesn’t mean that! Master Li choosing Blue Profound Sect is a justified and reasonable choice.” Guo Zhenqing hurriedly shook his head and followed asking carefully, “Sir Po Jun, the Snow Cloud Sky Ship had not appeared in Sky Emperor City for ten over years and today its’ sudden appearance, does it mean that... Sovereign Mu has come over personally?”","He watched Cang Po Jun’s expression carefully, trying to find an answer.","If it was only Cang Po Jun who had taken interest in Li Moying, wanting to snatch him away, Guo Zhenqing would not easily pass him up so easily.","The person who was truly snatching him away was in Cang Po Jun’s hint in his words. If Mu Chengying had really come and he truly went against Blue Profound Sect’s meaning, wouldn’t it be seeking for death?","Guo Zhenqing wanted to probe on the truth of this matter.","Cang Po Jun turned his head back and looked at him straight in the eye as he replied calmly, “Elder Guo is an established top exponent for many years. Surely you’re very clear that other than our Sovereign, no one else would be able to utilise this Snow Cloud Sky Ship isn’t it?”","He intentionally avoided Guo Zhenqing’s question."]},{"number":1663,"title":"Chapter 1663 - The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (5)","paragraphs":["He didn’t admit nor did he deny.","Guo Zhenqing’s expression instantly turned extremely pale.","From what he saw, Cang Po Jun’s answer was simply equivalent to admitting that Mu Chengying was sitting right in the Snow Cloud Sky Ship!","Guo Zhenqing totally didn’t doubted Cang Po Jun’s words because any practitioner who had experienced Mu Chengying’s fully flourished times knew that the Snow Cloud Sky Ship was refined by Huang Yueli for Mu Chengying so Mu Chengying had never allowed anyone else to utilise it without authority!","Whereas for Mu Chengying not to appear was very normal. After all, what status did the Sovereign have? Surely they didn’t expect him to appear right here to exchange humble greetings with an Elder from Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace right?","The more Guo Zhenqing thought, the more terrified he got as the cold sweat on his back kept profusing.","Mu Chengying was out of his closed door cultivation!","He had to hurry back immediately to report this huge matter to his Palace Lord!","Cang Po Jun carefully shot a glance towards Li Moying and upon realising that he wasn’t upset, he hurriedly turned around and led the way.","Li Moying held Huang Yueli’s hand as he walked in a neither fast nor slow pace towards the Snow Cloud Sky Ship.","Standing behind them, Luo Jiyun and the others were completely stunned and even after a while, they were still unable to get used to it.","It was because the appearance of Cang Po Jun had made them too surprised! They had originally thought that to be able to gain the interest from Splendid Violet Heavenly Palace’s Elder was already Li Moying’s streak of good luck as that indicated that he would fly into greater heights in future.","In the end, whoever knew that an even greater surprise was waiting for them, Li Moying actually successfully joined Blue Profound Sect!","Blue Profound Sect! That was the Sacred Land among the Sacred Lands in all practitioner’s minds! They really didn’t dare to believe that such a lucky thing would happen!","Huang Yueli realised their abnormality as she stopped and turned back to wave at them, indicating for them to follow up.","Luo Jiyun, Mo Yi and the others then woke up from their dream as they hurriedly chased up to them.","On seeing that vast and luxurious flying ship in front of his eyes, Luo Jiyun was simply unable to suppress the excitement and emotion stirred in his heart as he leaned closed towards Huang Yueli’s other side.","“Lil Sister-in-law, can you... can you quickly pinch me! I... am I really not dreaming? Eldest Senior Brother actually joined the Blue Profound Sect!”","When Huang Yueli heard that, her brows rose and she swiftly stretched out her fingers as a burst of Profound Energy struck Luo Jiyun below his ribs.","“Ouch—! OUCH.....” Luo Jiyun almost cried out miserably but he still remembered that Cang Po Jun was some ninth stage realm peak top exponent whom he could not afford to offend and as he was afraid of making him upset, he hurriedly stopped his groaning at the back of his throat but his face had already flushed a deep red shade.","“Lil... Lil Sister-in-law, you’re too vicious!” He grimaced in pain softly.","Huang Yueli innocently shrugged her shoulders, “You’re the one who asked me to pinch you!”","“Bu... But.....”","“Do you still feel that you’re in a dream now?” Huang Yueli interrupted him.","Luo Jiyun looked left and looked right and realised that there wasn’t any change in his surroundings as he said, “It’s... it’s really real! Eldest Senior Brother is simply too powerful, even Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign came to recruit him! Then can we assume the status of his servants to enter the Blue Profound Sect as well?”","Huang Yueli laughed meaningfully, “You cannot be servants.”","“What? Can’t even be servants? At least I am of an eighth grade talent!” Luo Jiyun’s shoulders drooped down in disappointment.","Everyone knew that large powerhouses’ high grade inheritances were plentiful and even a cultivation method learnt by the servants were much higher class than a direct disciple from a small force.","Hence there were plenty of practitioners every year who didn’t mind becoming servants, just to join the Seven Sacred Lands."]},{"number":1664,"title":"Chapter 1664 - The most sacred land among the Sacred Lands (6)","paragraphs":["Luo Jiyun naturally was no exception.","Actually, based on his eighth grade talent, there was still hope for him to join one of the Top Ten Clans or Soaring Heavens Merchant Guild level kind of powerhouse.","But in order to join the Seven Sacred Lands, it was practically hopeless.","Because although his innate talent wasn’t not, but he was no longer in his peak age to start cultivating. Practitioners who were over twelve, their ability and future would no longer be reliant on innate talent. More so, it was related to the cultivation methods which they cultivated with and the resources which they obtained in their younger days as well as luck.","Equivalent practitioners with the same innate talent, if their experience training was different, it would merely take a few years to show the difference in their abilities.","Although Luo Jiyun’s innate talent wasn’t bad at all but he had grown up in South Sky Region so his ability as compared to those who had been nurtured in Sky Emperor City’s large powerhouses’ eighth grade talented practitioners, the distance was still extremely huge. Perhaps he might not even match up to many seven grade talented practitioners.","Not to mention entering Blue Profound Sect that kind of number one Sacred Land, even if it was the other Seven Sacred Lands, the possibility of recruiting him was very low.","So Luo Jiyun was hungering to follow Li Moying into Blue Profound Sect, even if it was to be a servant, it was a heavenly chance to him.","Huang Yueli looked at his disappointed look and smiled as she shook her head.","She hoped that when he found out about the truth later, he had better not faint from the shock.....","Very quickly the few of them followed Cang Po Jun into the Snow Cloud Sky Ship.","Luo Jiyun’s body apparently tensed up as he hung his head low in fear and trepidation, not daring to look around at all.","Mo Yi and the others didn’t even dared to breath loudly.","The minute they entered the flying ship, it was entering Sky Emperor City’s number one Sacred Lands territory! How many practitioners wouldn’t feel tensed and excited entering this kind of place?","Huang Yueli however surveyed the surroundings at ease and following that, she gave a slight smile.","“Blue Profound Sect’s Four Great Guardians, had indeed all arrived.....”","Hearing that, Luo Jiyun was so tensed that his cold sweat kept on sprouting as his voice quivered, “Wh... What? Four Great Guardians... have all arrived? Then could it be that Sovereign Mu has also.....”","Blue Profound Sect’s Four Great Guardians were all top rated exponents in Sky Emperor City’s Sky Charts top twenty ranking practitioners and when the four of them appeared together in the Snow Cloud Sky Ship, the enclosed area which had been completely dominated by ninth stage realm peak practitioner’s Profound Energy, that overpowering suppression made one unable to breathe.","Luo Jiyun only felt his scalp turned numb as he was so tense that he didn’t know where to place his hands and feet.","Just at this moment, Cang Po Jun’s footsteps suddenly stopped as he turned around.","Luo Jiyun thought that he was about to start his lecture and had already prepared to bow in respect.","Just at this moment, Cang Po Jun suddenly “plopped” onto the ground on his two knees and bowed down in front of Li Moying.","Luo Jiyun and the others were startled!","“Sister-in-law, this.. what’s going on? What on earth happened.....”","Huang Yueli was not able to answer in time when the other three Guardians had also hurriedly knelt down.","“Our respects to Sovereign, welcoming Sovereign’s return back to Blue Profound Sect!”","The four guardians spoke out at the same time as they respectfully bent their heads over.","Under Luo Jiyun and the other’s awestruck gazes, Li Moying lifted his hand slightly as he spoke out in a cold chilly voice, “Stand up all of you. It has been hard on you for the past few years. This Sovereign has taken note of your contributions to the Sect.”"]},{"number":1665,"title":"Chapter 1665 - Cannot tell! (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Li Moying swept a glance at the few present and said, “No need to be so humble. This Sovereign had left for so many years so there should be quite a number of huge matters which had happened in Sky Emperor City hence there is an urgent need for This Sovereign to understand about it all.”","The Four Great Guardians escorted Li Moying to the first place and respectfully stood upright by the side.","Luo Jiyun and the others were completely mortified as they stood in a daze by the side, not even daring to make a single move.","Seeing this scene was just too fascinating!","Cang Po Jun and others actually greeted Li Moying “Sovereign”!","But, Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign, as everyone knew, was the number one top expert in Soaring Heavens Continent, Mu Chengying! What relation did it have to do with Li Moying?","Could it be that the Li Moying in front of their eyes was fake, and they had recognised the wrong person?","Or perhaps they were poisoned and their consciousness were unclear, hence they had developed hallucinations?","Li Moying was seated right in the middle and his gaze swept towards the entrance and saw the dazed Luo Junyun and others.","He naturally knew that his identity being exposed would bring about what kind of shock to them but there wasn’t any time to explain to them right now.","Li Moying turned his head back towards Cang Po Jun and said, “This Sovereign had brought along some people and they have been following This Sovereign since in South Sky Region and are extremely loyal. Arrange a place for them to have some rest first and in future, they will all be disciples of Blue Profound Sect.”","Cang Po Jun hurriedly responded as he called out for two attendants, “Go, bring those few people over there to the superior room to have a rest.”","Even after Luo Jiyun and the others were brought out of the main cabin, they still felt as though they were dreaming and their feet were threading on clouds, totally not being able to steady their footsteps.","Every one of them had an extremely distracted expression, totally not knowing what they were doing at all!","It simply was because the matter which had just happened was too sensational until even the usually composed Mo Yi also felt that he was still in a dream!","The other two attendants were extremely envious of them as they couldn’t help but opened their mouths, “You few have really good luck! That year when we wanted to join Blue Profound Sect, we spent quite a number of years to pass through the various assessments before outranking the top few hundreds of talents to shine! Now you’re just so lucky to have followed Sovereign in South Sky Region and be able to join the Sect. Moreover.... From Sovereign’s tone, you will at least get the treatment of inner disciples! The entire Sect’s disciples would envy you guys to death!”","What they didn’t mention was that Blue Profound Sect had never accepted formal disciples of eighth grade talents and below.","If one wanted to become inner disciples, they were required to be ranked top ten in various Sect’s internal tournaments before they had a chance.","But who asked Mo Yi and the others to be Li Moying’s trusted aides when they were in South Sky Region?","This luck..... was really something which the others weren’t able to help but only to be envious of it!","When Luo Jiyun heard their sourish words, his confused thoughts finally regained some clarity.","He held on to one of the attendants as he asked in a unhesitant manner, “This.... elder brother, I.... I’m a little.... have I heard wrongly earlier? Earlier Sir Po Jun actually called my Eldest Senior Brother.... Sovereign? But.... this.... how is this possible? Eldest Senior Brother had grown up in the South Sky Region since young?”","Because of shock, Luo Jiyun had already started to speak incoherently.","But upon hearing his words, the two attendees were even more stunned than him as their faces looked as though they had just seen a living ghost.","“What did you say? Our Sovereign is your Eldest Senior Brother??”","“What is your relationship with the Sovereign??”","Luo Jiyun was stared at by them so fixatedly until he didn’t know what to do, as he blinked his eyes with an extremely troubled expression."]},{"number":1666,"title":"Chapter 1666 - Cannot tell! (2)","paragraphs":["“It’s.... it’s just Senior and Junior Brother relationship? Eldest Senior Brother and I, are all South Sky Region’s Celestial Light Sect’s direct disciples and today we have just entered Sky Emperor City.....”","His words had just fallen as the two attendees exchanged glances.","The duo’s attitude immediately underwent a change. Earlier the glance towards Luo Jiyun and the others was rather disdainful because of their incapability.","But now, the two of them were extremely respectful.","“Oh, this Young Master here is Sovereign’s South Sky Region’s Junior Brother, we have disgraced ourselves earlier.”","Although the two of them assumed the identities of attendees, but they were Cang Po Jun’s trusted subordinates and their statuses in Blue Profound Sect weren’t lowly at all. Furthermore their cultivations were currently at sixth stage realm later stage so in terms of battle power, they were far above Luo Jiyun!","Luo Jiyun saw them being so courteous and felt extremely embarrassed as he hurriedly said, “Elder Brothers, you’re too kind! I... I’m just an ordinary practitioner in South Sky Region. Contrariwise my Eldest Senior Brother, he... what identity does he have? Why did Sir Po Jun even.... even.....”","Thinking of the scenario when Four Great Guardians knelt down towards Li Moying earlier, Luo Jiyun was disarrayed in the wind once again.","This simply was just too inconceivable, even until now he still felt that he was in a dream!","The attendants hesitated for a moment and asked, “Mister, don’t you know even a little bit on your Eldest Senior Brother’s identity?”","Luo Jiyun shook his head, “What identity?”","The attendants thought about it and said, “Anyway, Mister Li is indeed Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign. If this was not the case, how would the Four Great Guardians possibly kneel down to him so easily?”","Luo Jiyun naturally knew this logic but he just couldn’t get it!","“But... But... Eldest Senior Brother grew up with me since young and today is indeed the first time he entered Sky Emperor City, how did he suddenly become Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign? If he was your Sovereign, then how about Sovereign Mu.....”","The attendant smiled, “Since you’re Sovereign’s Junior Brother, then I will not be able to comment any further on this matter. In future you will naturally find out about the truth. Now, will all of you please come along with us!”","...","In the main cabin.","Luo Jiyun and the others left but Huang Yueli didn’t move at all.","Cang Po Jun had just noticed that exceptional beautiful young lady who had always stood beside Li Moying and recalling back about the intimacy she had with Li Moying earlier, a shocking idea suddenly festered in his mind.","He forgot his manners and cried out in shock, “Sovereign, this young lady.... She... could she be.....”","Li Moying frowned slightly as a displeased look appeared on his face while berating softly, “What’s the fuss about? This lady here... is the reincarnation of Miss Huang!”","Huang Yueli smiled as she showed her pearly white teeth, “Hi Guardians, long time no see.”","Since earlier, she had been observing Li Moying’s Four Guardians.","Other than the first Guardian Cang Po Jun, Cang Po Yu helmed a refined temperament, taciturn and low-keyed person who was a ninth rank Array Grandmaster and also one of Mu Chengying’s think tank team members. The one with a smile always hanging on his face and also the youngest member with the highest innate talent was Cang Po Hun while the cold faced ice beauty Cang Ning Yue was the only female among the Four Great Guardians.","These four were considered as old acquaintances with Huang Yueli.","Only thing was, that year all of them had treated Huang Yueli with utmost respect.","As expected, upon hearing Li Moying’s words, the Four Great Guardians all revealed an extremely shocked expression as they stared intently at her."]},{"number":1667,"title":"Chapter 1667 - Cannot tell! (3)","paragraphs":["After some time later, Cang Ning Yue was the first to start exclaiming.","“Not possible right? How could this be possible? Could this really be.... Be.... Grandmaster Huang?”","Cang Po Hun scrutinized Huang Yueli for a long time as his mouth opened wide while speaking in disbelief, “this.... looks really a little like Grandmaster Huang.... seriously?”","Even the most composed and stable Cang Po Jun almost slipped and overturned the tea cup on the table.","Only Cang Po Yu kept silent as he looked thoughtfully at Huang Yueli’s dainty little face.","Huang Yueli’s lips curled up as she was totally not surprised by everyone’s reaction at all.","After all, the scene where she had self-exploded in Northern Ice Fields was something which everyone in Soaring Heavens Continent knew about!","Theoretically speaking she could no longer reincarnate but she was suddenly reborn and even standing right here alive so anyone would feel shocked from this!","She smiled and said, “I’m Huang Yueli, replacement guaranteed if not genuine! Furthermore I’ve already gotten engaged officially to your Sovereign so in future.... I’ll be depending on you guys!”","When she said this, it was another heavyweight bomb dropping on them.","The few guardian’s chins almost dropped onto the ground.","Who didn’t know that Mu Chengying had wooed Huang Yueli for more than a decade but Huang Yueli wasn’t willing to nod her head to marry him. In the end the both of them had just reincarnated and Huang Yueli decided to marry? Just what happened in the past ten over years?","Cang Po Jun’s brows creased as he thought for a moment and suddenly spoke out in enlightenment, “Oh.... Congratulations to Sovereign and Grandmaster Huang, all’s well ends well. Sovereign, I’d not expected that your plan actually succeeded... this is really... for the past hundred thousand years, no one had ever managed to complete this astonishing pioneering work..... Congratulations Sovereign!”","Hearing Cang Po Jun’s words, the other three Guardians also revealed an enlightened expression as they all bowed towards Li Moying to pay their respects.","“Congratulations Sovereign, finally getting what you desired!”","“Congratulations Sovereign!”","Huang Yueli was originally filled with smiles but when she heard Cang Po Jun’s words, not knowing why, her heart suddenly felt a little uncomfortable.","Cang Po Jun’s words sounded rather strange and there were quite a number of areas which she didn’t understand.","Huang Yueli asked in curiosity, “What does Sir Po Jun mean? What plan were you talking about? And what astonishing pioneering work had not succeeded for the past hundred thousand years? What riddle are you playing?”","Cang Po Jun went into a blank as he apparently did not expect Huang Yueli to ask about this.","He looked at Huang Yueli and turned back to look at Li Moying.","He saw an obvious fury surfacing on his face as his cold and harsh stare shot over towards him.","Cang Po Jun shivered as he suddenly realised that he had committed a serious mistake!","The Sovereign seemed to not have told “that matter” to Grandmaster Huang yet! In this case, wasn’t he acting like a smart aleck as this slipped out from his mouth.....","Sensing Li Moying’s murderous glare, Cang Po Jun trembled as he hurriedly gave a dry laugh in an attempt to conceal his mistake.","“Ughh, where.... where’s the riddle? It’s merely because Grandmaster Huang is just too difficult to woo so this subordinate is feeling happy for Sovereign! I wonder when will Sovereign and Grandmaster Huang be officially getting married? Your subordinates, we have been waiting for this day for a long time!”","“Really?” Huang Yueli’s brows rose in suspicion.","She somehow felt that Cang Po Jun was saying that but his original meaning was another thing and still wanted to pursue the topic.","Just at this moment, Li Moying suddenly gave a cold harrumph as he said, “The few of you, why are you still in a daze over there for? Since Li’er is already engaged to This Sovereign, then in future, Grandmaster Huang will be Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereigness, still not coming over to pay your respect to Sovereigness?”"]},{"number":1668,"title":"Chapter 1668 - Cannot tell! (4)","paragraphs":["The Four Great Guardians shivered as they hurriedly turned around and bowed down towards Huang Yueli’s direction.","“Our respects to Sovereigness!”","Huang Yueli was a little surprised and after a short blank, she indicated for them to get up quickly.","At the same time, she couldn’t help but turned back to stare at Li Moying as she mumbled in dissatisfaction, “What’s up, why call me Sovereigness?” We have merely gotten engaged so there’s no need to make me sound that old right? Moreover speaking, we have yet to be married officially so whether I will really be getting married to you in future, that’s actually hard to say.....”","Li Moying originally wanted to divert her attention hence he made the Four Great Guardians bow down to pay their respects to her.","But when he heard her words, he immediately shot her a cold stare and established the command towards the Four Great Guardians, “Remember this, after we get back to Blue Profound Sect, pass down This Sovereign’s command. Whenever anyone sees Grandmaster Huang in the Sect, they must address her as Sovereigness and whoever who disobeys will be punished severely!”","Huang Yueli’s eyes grew wide as she simply could not believe what she heard!","Li Moying had just returned to Blue Profound Sect, not even for an hour and he immediately turned as overbearing and conceited as in his past life!","This was simply compelling her to submit!","Huang Yueli stomped her feet and shot up to him in a few quick steps as she whisked his clothes around his chest area while angrily retorting, “What do you mean by that! Haven’t you heard what I said? I don’t like to be called.... mmph!”","She had yet completed her words when Li Moying suddenly lowered his head and blocked her pink tender lips which kept on opening and closing, at the same time stuffing back the words of resistance back into her mouth.","Huang Yueli pushed his chest and tried to evade him but was locked in securely by that man, rendering her totally immovable.","Luckily Li Moying probably considered the current situation hence he only dabbled and stopped. Not too long later, he released her.","Huang Yueli covered her mouth as her face was already flushed with a shade of red, “You.... you.....”","Li Moying laughed, “Sovereigness, other than marrying this Sovereign, there’s no second choice for you so you’d better keep a tight reign over your heart!”","Huang Yueli couldn’t wait to bite him but a pity that this action was just too ambiguous and under the Four Great Guardians’ attention, she simply couldn’t make herself do it....","She stared angrily at Li Moying and while she was in the middle of thinking, Li Moying had already turned towards Cang Po Jun as though nothing had happened.","“When This Sovereign wasn’t around, how is the situation in the Sect?”","Cang Po Jun was originally stunned from watching but upon hearing Li Moying’s question, he abruptly regained his senses and responded, “Yes.... Report to Sovereign, the Sect’s internal situation is considered rather stable and Sovereign’s fame is rather all like thunder piercing the ear. In the first ten years, no one dared to be rash but in the recent few years... ughh.... some situations still happened.”","Li Moying could tell that he hemmed and hawed as he couldn’t help but give a cold sneer, “Looks like, a lot of people assumed that This Sovereign had already died and are starting to stir?”","“Yes, Sovereign is wise.”","Li Moying’s slender long fingers played around with the exquisite flower patterned tea cup on the table as his tone was tranquil and calm, “Who are those people?”","He seemed as though he couldn’t care less but the Four Great Guardians were his trusted aides and could tell the silent murderous intent hiding in his heart.","Apparently, Big Demon Lord had returned and these people who actually dared to betray him.... their ending would be extremely miserable!","Cang Po Jun silently sighed as he hurriedly stated everything to Li Moying clearly.","Huang Yueli was also attracted by this topic and sitting beside Li Moying, she pricked up her ears to listen.","Li Moying was listening to Cang Po Jun and secretly stole a glance at the quiet and graceful young lady’s side view as he secretly heaved a long sigh of relief.","This lass, seemed to have already forgotten the things which Cang Po Jun had accidentally let slip earlier."]},{"number":1669,"title":"Chapter 1669 - Cannot tell! (5)","paragraphs":["Chapter 1669: Cannot tell! (5)","The few of them had a discussion in the main cabin for over two hours and Li Moying finally grasped the big picture on Blue Profound Sect and Sky Emperor City’s situation.","Just as this timing, the Snow Cloud Sky Shuo had already arrived in the skies above Blue Profound Sect and started to descend slowly.","Li Moying stood up and stretched out his arm towards Huang Yueli, “Li’er, come!”","Huang Yueli obediently leaned over as he held herself into his arms, wrapping around her waist as he brought her out.","The Four Guardians watched their departing backs as they were slightly dazed, each of them with complicated emotions flashing past their eyes.","It was until the two’s figures disappeared in their vision of sight when Cang Po Hun’s sauce face revealed a sliver of profound look while his mouth broke out into laughter, “I’d not expected Grandmaster Huang actually really agreeing to get engaged to Sovereign! From their looks... it seems that their relationship shouldn’t be too bad? Sovereign is finally not on a one sided love track?”","Cang Ning Yue heard him and gave a cold humph as she took the lead to walk out.","Cang Po Hun rubbed his nose as he followed suit.","Snow Cloud Sky Ship directly descended onto the core region of the Blue Profound Sect, at Levitation Sword Palace.","Luo Jiyun and the others were still on the Sky Ship but were already stunned by the view below them so much that they couldn’t say a single word.","Blue Profound Sect’s location was on the largest spiritual artery in the entire Soaring Heavens Continent where Heaven and Earth Profound Qi was at its strongest degree, around five times or more of normal circumstances. Especially for the core region Levitation Sword Palace, it reached almost ten times of Profound Qi intensity.","Intense Profound Qi formed into a light fog as it enveloped the skies above the Levitation Sword Palace. From above, it looked as though it was surrounded by clouds and mist.","Under the fog, hundred thousand high grade flying swords hovered above the palace with the sword tip pointing upwards forming into a sword formation, surrounding and protecting the palace rooms and pavilions.","Frost-like sword edges under the ray of the sunlight glistened brightly as its cold murderous aura intimidated people’s hearts.","This kind of god grade ancient sword formation wasn’t something which the current Array Masters could lay out, but was passed down from generation to generation in Blue Profound Sect.","Levitation Sword Palace was Soaring Heavens Continent’s genuine cultivation Sacred Land and there wasn’t a practitioner who didn’t know of its name.","But even if Luo Jiyun and the others had long read and understood from ancient manuals or legends of Levitation Sword Palace’s situation, witnessing it for themselves still made them so stunned that they were totally immovable.","Snow Cloud Sky Ship quickly landed safely as the slight of stairs descended.","Li Moying led Huang Yeuli as they walked down.","In the front of Levitation Sword Palace were two rows of direct disciples who were dressed in their uniforms and at the instant when they saw Li Moying, they all knelt down and prostate onto the ground.","“Welcome Sovereign back to the Sect!!!”","Li Moying’s eyes flashed past a strict gaze as he took a deep breath and on that profound, aloof handsome face of his, it revealed a slight stir.","“This Sovereign.... Has finally returned!”","Huang Yueli turned her head over and looked at that perfectly contoured side view infatuatedly, as she was struck in awe by that revered glare in his eyes.","So many years had passed and after experiencing two rounds of lifetimes, actually this man had never changed!","It wasn’t the first time she stood at this place and it wasn’t the first time she entered Levitation Sword Palace with this man.","But it was until this moment she realised that every single time she returned back with him to this place, what that undulated emotions in her heart meant!","The two of them walked past the crowd and slowly walked into Levitation Sword Palace.","Li Moying embraced Huang Yueli’s slender waist gently as he whispered, “Li’er, I still have some Sect’s affairs to handle, why not take a rest first? The room which you had been staying in that year, I’ve been preserving it for you.”"]},{"number":1670,"title":"Chapter 1670 - Cannot tell! (6)","paragraphs":["When Huang Yueli heard that, she nodded and said, “Alright, you go be busy with your work, I have something to settle as well.”","Li Moying was stunned, “What matter?”","Huang Yueli turned her head back and pointed towards the entrance at the Shadow Guards and Luo Jiyun who were acting very carefully as though they were country bumpkins who had just entered the city and said laughingly, “Haven’t you seen the few of them, all thoroughly shocked silly? It’s better to explain some things to them carefully, after all they are extremely loyal and with Blue Profound Sect’s resources, after careful nurture, they will have bright futures.”","Li Moying’s gaze fell onto Luo Jiyun. Looking at his look which shook in fear and trepidation, he couldn’t help but found it amusing while shaking his head.","“Sigh, really.... then you’d better go. Later when I’m done settling these matters, I’ll send someone over to tell you when it’s dinnertime.”","Huang Yueli nodded as she waved her hand at him and then turned around and walked towards Luo Jiyun and the others.","Li Moying bade her farewell with her eyes before leading the Four Great Guardians and a few trusted managers who had just arrived, into the main palace.","The palace doors had just shut and Li Moying abruptly turned back his head with a severe gaze as it swept past across every single person, lastly falling onto Cang Po Jun.","“This Sovereign’s return to Blue Profound Sect meant that the plan had already succeeded! But This Sovereign does not wish for Grandmaster Huang to know what had happened, hence.... No one is allowed to spread the matter which happened sixteen years ago that happened in Levitation Sword Palace out! Everyone.... control your own tongue, do you understand? Even if Grandmaster Huang were to come ask you on her own, you’re not allowed to reveal a single word!”","Cang Po Jun’s sweat soaked through the back of his clothes as he knew clearly that he had said the wrong thing earlier, which had thoroughly angered this Sovereign.","He hurriedly lowered his head, “Yes, this subordinate understands and will also constrain everyone in the Sect!”","Still slightly unresigned, Cang Ning Yue’s pale and stunning face appeared anxious from the uneasiness as she couldn’t help but voiced out, “But, Sovereign, you’ve done so much for Grandmaster Huang, why not.....”","Before she could even finish her words, Li Moying’s frigid gaze shifted onto her.","Cang Ning Yue shivered, not daring to say a single word more as she silently lowered her head.","Li Moying said icily, “This Sovereign will only say it one more time, this matter.... no one should talk about it! Those who violate this..... will be killed without any pardon!”","Everyone trembled upon hearing his words and immediately lowered their heads to accept the command, “We comply by Sovereign’s command!”","Cang Ning Yue bit on her lips hard as she still felt unresigned in her heart but she didn’t dare to create any more trouble in front of Li Moying.","Cang Po Yu also frowned slightly but he had always been reserved in his thoughts hence he didn’t say out his thinking in front of everyone.","Li Moying sensed his gaze and shot a warning glance towards him.","Actually he himself knew that paper was unable to wrap up fire and Huang Yueli would find out about this sooner or later.","But.... if he could hide it from her for some time, he would hide it for as long as he could!","...","In the empty ground in front of Levitation Sword Palace, Huang Yueli chased up to Luo Jiyun and the others quickly.","“Junior Brother Luo, Brother Mo Yi, wait for me!”","Luo Jiyun saw her running over and was firstly slightly pleasantly surprised but immediately following that, he appeared rather embarrassed, “Lil Sister-in-law, this... this.....”","Huang Yueli couldn’t help but laughed as she said, “I know what you want to ask and I’m here to explain to you. But this is not a place that we can converse in, come over with me!”","She led the few of them into the rear palace with familiarity as she immodestly utilised the largest guest room, directing Levitation Sword Palace’s serving maids to serve tea to them.","Luo Jiyun was totally stunned from this scene.","This was Levitation Sword Palace!","She ordered the serving maids from the Levitation Sword Palace as though it was a matter of course!"]},{"number":1671,"title":"Chapter 1671 - For you, Sovereign..... (1)","paragraphs":["Did she know what she was doing?","Levitation Sword Palace’s serving maids were all talented young ladies who were picked out from ten thousand candidates and no matter if it was in terms of looks, innate talent or ability, they were all of superior calibre. Quite a number of large powerhouses direct disciples couldn’t even be compared to an ordinary serving maid from Levitation Sword Palace.","Just referring to those few who were ordered by Huang Yueli, their cultivations were at least sixth stage realm and above whereas Huang Yueli herself was only at fifth stage realm ninth level!","However what made Luo Jiyun and the others even more surprised was that these serving maids really listened to whatever Huang Yueli instructed!","Moreover, each and every one of them were exceptionally respectfully, totally not having the kind of arrogance which a Blue Profound Sect disciple should have. Instead they all treated Huang Yueli with respect and reverence.","After the serving maids brought tea and snacks for them, Huang Yueli waved her hand and said, “That’s all we need, you may leave now. Unless the Sovereign is looking for me personally, otherwise don’t come in to disturb us.”","The serving maids respectfully curtsied, “Yes, Sovereigness.”","When Huang Yueli heard their greeting, her lips twitched as her heart cried out a gloomy sigh!","She had not expected Li Moying’s command to actually be conveyed throughout the Sect so quickly! This man... he really was too tyrannical!","She also knew that there was no use for her to correct these serving maids. No one dared to oppose Li Moying’s commands hence it could only be left like that.","After she dismissed the serving maids, she turned back and saw Luo Jiyun and the few Shadow Guards all surrounding a small narrow corner, looking at her in shock and uneasiness.","Huang Yueli smiled and said, “What’s the matter? Haven’t I asked you guys to sit down and drink some tea? Why are you guys all standing around?”","The few of them exchanged glances and Luo Jiyun opened his mouth to ask, “Lil....Lil Sister-in-law, stop playing riddles with us. Quickly tell me what this... what this is all about? Eldest Senior Brother and Blue Profound Sect.... what relationship do they have?”","Huang Yueli thought about it for a moment and smiled, “Regarding this matter, it’s indeed a little inconceivable when I talk about it and there’s a possibility that you guys will find it hard to believe but.... what you’ve heard earlier are all true. Moying he is indeed... Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign!”","The few of them looked at each other in dismay because this kind of answer was something which they could not accept!","Luo Jiyun was like a headless fly turning round and round on the original spot as he kept mumbling to himself, “How is this possible? How could this be possible? I must be dreaming, and in my dream even Lil Sister-in-law is sprouting rubbish! Ah, who can pinch me?”","Huang Yueli was utterly speechless as she shook her head and her right hand waved as she continuously shot out three bursts of Profound Energy.","Furthermore her moves were swift and the position which she struck out was especially tricky.","Luo Jiyun was totally unprepared and was struck immediately. It hurt him so much that he directly jumped right up from the ground.","“Ouch, ouch, ouch!! So painful! Lil Sister-in-law, I... I only asked you to pinch me once, why did you hit me three times?”","Huang Yueli’s lips curled up slightly, “I see that you seem to keep asking me to pinch you every other hour so thought you’re in need of being pinched! So I might as well pinch you a few more times to satisfy your needs! How is it, are you satisfied enough? Do you still want to continue being pinched?”","Luo Jiyun grimaced in pain and furiously shook his head, “No.... No need!”","“So are you finally awake? Or do you still think you’re still dreaming? Still thinking that I’m spouting nonsense?” Huang Yueli asked again.","Hearing that, Luo Jiyun didn’t reply immediately but hesitated for a moment before opening his mouth to ask cautiously and solemnly, “Lil Sister-in-law, Eldest Senior Brother he.... surely he can’t be Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign right? How could this be possible? Could he.... he.....”"]},{"number":1672,"title":"Chapter 1672 - For you, Sovereign..... (2)","paragraphs":["Looking at Luo Jiyun’s extremely tangled look, Huang Yueli casually picked up a tea cup and sent it to her lips as she asked curiously, “Could it be that?”","Luo Jiyun suppressed his voice as he asked mysteriously, “Could it be that... Eldest Senior Brother is actually Sovereign Mu’s illegitimate child?”","“PFFFFTTTTT—!!”","Huang Yueli had just drank a mouthful of tea and immediately sprayed it out, moreover it sprayed precisely onto Luo Jiyun’s face, making that outstanding young lad turn into a dishevelled drowned rat.","Luo Jiyun stood in a daze on his original spot as tea started dripping down from his hair, as he looked embarrassed and totally at a loss.","“Lil.... Lil Sister-in-law?”","“Cough cough, cough cough cough...” Huang Yueli herself choked and she coughed furiously for half a day before she finally got over it.","Her lips kept on twitching as she gazed at Luo Jiyun, “You.... how would you possibly think of it in this way? Who told you such nonsense?”","Luo Jiyun said foolishly, “Ah? No... it’s not like that? Have I guessed wrongly? But everyone in the entire Soaring Heavens Continent knows that Blue Profound Sect’s Sovereign is the Continent’s number one top exponent Mu Chengying! Whereas Eldest Senior Brother is just a practitioner from South Sky Region. No matter how genius he is, surely he could not directly become the Sovereign, right?”","“Even if Sovereign Mu is really like what the rumours said, that he had gone into Qi Deviation while in closed door cultivation, but no matter what it shouldn’t be Eldest Senior Brother’s turn right? So the only logical explanation, that would be... ughh.... don’t tell me it’s wrong?”","Huang Yueli rolled her eyes towards the sky as she mumbled softly, “If he dares to have an illegitimate child outside and even dare to bring him back to Blue Profound Sect to be the successor of the Sovereign seat? Isn’t he afraid that I will murder him?”","“Ah? Sister-in-law? What did you say?” Luo Jiyun didn’t hear what she said as he hurried over to ask her.","Huang Yueli gave a light cough and said, “Things are not what you imagined. But it might be even more unimaginable than what you think. It’s a long story, so take a seat, all of you.”","After the few of them were seated, Huang Yueli then toughly told him about the scenario about her and Li Moying’s rebirth.","In order to clear everyone’s suspicions, she gave them a rather detailed picture, from the time she and Li Moying met each other to the time when they discovered each other’s identity, as well as the process where Li Moying slowly regaining his memory, everything included.","Hearing her completed story, Luo Jiyun and the others seemed as though they were struck by lightning and couldn’t regain their senses back for more than half a day.","It took quite a while later when Luo Jiyun opened his eyes wide as he asked in disbelief, “So to speak, Eldest Senior Brother he.... he’s actually the reincarnation of Mu Chengying? And Lil Sister-in-law, you are... are.... The number one Armament Master in Soaring Heavens Continent, number one beauty, peerless top exponent, that renowned Mythical Flame Palace’s Young Palace Lord Huang Yueli???”","Huang Yueli chuckled, “This flattery isn’t bad at all, I like it!”","Luo Jiyun totally didn’t notice what she was saying as he was still in a state of dizziness while muttering to himself.","“No wonder Eldest Senior Brother’s innate talent is so heaven defying and no wonder he’s so knowledgeable, and for no rhyme or reason being able to master so many heaven grade and god grade cultivation methods and Profound Skills when Celestial Light Sect obviously didn’t had those ancient inheritances! And same for Lil Sister-in-law, not only is her innate talent in cultivation outstanding, her armament refining skills are so stunning, as though there was nothing that she didn’t know .....”","“Heavens, so the truth is actually like this... this is just too unimaginable.....”","Mo Yi and the others state of mind weren’t any better than his."]},{"number":1673,"title":"Chapter 1673 - For you, Sovereign..... (3)","paragraphs":["This news was just too shocking and no one was able to accept it in the short duration of time.","Huang Yueli waited for a moment but still saw their dazed looks as she helplessly shook her head.","“Alright, things are more or less like this but we require you to keep this in top secrecy. In Blue Profound Sect, only the Four Great Guardians, Levitation Sword Palace’s trusted aide and attendants, as well as a few managers know about it. The rest including Blue Profound Sect’s Elders or the others do not know about this matter hence no matter under what circumstances, remember not to divulge the information!”","Everyone shivered as they immediately voiced out in agreement.","Luo Jiyun asked, “Lil Sister-in-law, why can’t Eldest Senior Brother announce his own identity publicly? Could there be any dangers?”","Huang Yueli remained silent for a moment and continued, “Fifteen to sixteen years had passed and Sky Emperor City’s circumstances are different from then. Before your Eldest Senior Brother resumes to his peak ability, it’s best that we remain low key for now.”","Saying that, she recalled something, “That’s right, your Eldest Senior Brother mentioned this earlier to let the manager make arrangements for you guys. Brother Mo Yi and the others will be treated as inner disciples while Junior Brother Luo you will become Blue Profound Sect’s direct disciple... should I say congratulations?”","“Rea....Really?? Heavens, something so great is happening!!” Luo Jiyun was so excited that he almost fainted!","Happiness came too suddenly!","Just before today, he thought that it was a difficult feat for him to become a servant of the Seven Sacred Lands, not to mention officially joining the Sect to become a disciple of the Seven Sacred Lands.","But now..... he abruptly transformed, without even needing to take the assessment, to become the number one Sacred Lands’ direct disciple!","This was the status which so many peerless talents in Sky Emperor City had tried means and ways, fighting head over heels but were still unable to obtain!","Mo Yi and the others were extremely excited as well. Although it was only the status of an inner disciple, but based on their innate talent, they would not even be able to get into any of the large powerhouses in Sky Emperor City based on their own abilities and to gain this status was akin to running into some unexpected luck.","Huang Yueli smiled and said, “But your potential and innate talents as compared to Blue Profound Sect’s ordinary disciples have quite a huge distance. So you must value this chance and work hard to cultivate!”","The few of them hurriedly bowed their bodies and chorused in unison, “Third Miss please be assured. Your subordinate will not make Master disappointed!”","Even if they already knew Huang Yueli and Li Moying’s real identities, but they still weren’t able to change their appellations towards them.","Huang Yueli nodded her head and wanted to continue saying something.","Suddenly there was a knocking sound coming from the outside of the door.","“Grandmaster Huang, Sovereign sent someone over to pass a message, to invite you to head over to the front hall to have dinner with him.” The serving maid respectfully reported from outside the door.","Huang Yueli then realised that the sky had already darkened.","She had spent quite an amount of time here.","Huang Yueli stretched her limbs as she stood up, “Alright then, I’m going to accompany Moying now. Just relax and stay on in Blue Profound Sect! No matter if it’s terms of cultivation or life, just look for me if you face any difficulties! Rest assured, there’d be plenty of places where we will need you!”","Saying that she waved her hand and left in anticipation.","She was in a hurry to go meet Li Moying so she totally didn’t wait for the serving maid to lead the way as she found her way familiarly to the front hall.","She had been to Levitation Sword Palace numerous times in her past life and was extremely familiar with this place.","However just as she was passing by the right side of the front hall’s decorative carved patterned corridor, suddenly someone called out to her from behind her."]},{"number":1674,"title":"Chapter 1674 - For you, Sovereign..... (4)","paragraphs":["“Grandmaster Huang!”","A clear and melodious voice rang out, sounding slightly familiar.","Huang Yueli paused and turned her head back as her eyes met with the ice beauty who was standing at one corner of the corridor.","Cang Ning Yue stared at her with an icy cold expression as her chin was slightly lifted upwards, bearing a conceited look.","It was undeniable that she was an extremely outstanding tender beauty with perfect features and an exquisite figure. Moreover as a ninth stage realm peak practitioner, she bore a kind of cold arrogant temperament which overlooked the people below.","If it was sixteen years ago, Cang Ning Yue’s bit of overbearing grandeur would naturally not be able to be compared with Mythical Flame Palace’s Young Palace Lord, but now that Huang Yueli had changed into such a young body, her cultivation was also only at fifth stage realm.","In comparison, Huang Yueli appeared to be younger and inexperienced.","Huang Yueli’s expression also turned chilly as her lips were slightly pursed as she replied coldly, “Guardian Yue, what may I do for you?”","Cang Ning Yue was also sizing her up at the same time.","Sixteen years had passed and the person whom they had originally thought was definitely dead had suddenly returned. Moreover she was still as enchanting as before with the same excellent innate talent, still..... attracting Li Moying’s vision tightly!","Thinking of this, Cang Ning Yue gritted her teeth silently as she could no longer hold on to the fake ice beauty façade.","“Grandmaster Huang, I’ve not expected that after so many years, I’m still able to meet you again. This is really.... an accidental surprise!”","Cang Ning Yue forced this sentence out from the slits of her teeth.","Huang Yueli’s lips curled as she gave an unknown implied smile, “Yes, sixteen years have passed.... Is Guardian Yue married already? I remember that year my fiancée personally pulled the red strings for you and Guardian Yu. Guardian Yu is a ninth ranked Array Grandmaster and also a man of talent and outstanding looks, Guardian Yue must cherish him well!”","When Cang Ning Yue recalled the scenario then, she was both indignant and embarrassed, as her face flushed instantly.","She would never forget the matter which had happened in Levitation Sword Palace twenty over years ago for her entire lifetime.","Cang Ning Yue had been adopted by the previous Sovereign of Blue Profound Sect and after Mu Chengying had identified as the next successor, the previous Sovereign always had been keen to betroth Cang Ning Yue to Mu Chengying as a concubine for double cultivation.","After all, Cang Ning Yue had an inborn Heavenly Yin physique and to any practitioner who engaged in double cultivation with her would obtain extremely huge benefits from it.","However, Mu Chengying totally ignored the benefits which she could give and only liked Huang Yueli right from the start. Although it was because of the previous Sovereign’s personal favour which coerced him to keep Cang Ning Yue by his side, but he had always treated her and Cang Po Jun and the others on the same level, nurturing her as a Guardian.","In order to make Mu Chengying see her in a new light, Cang Ning Yue worked doubly hard and was finally able to shine and be chosen from among the ten over Guardians for the position.","Alas, although she had successfully obtained the chance to stay beside Mu Chengying, but she had not expected that this unexcelled man wouldn’t even grant her an extra look!","To win over Cang Po Yu, Mu Chengying even went to the extent without any hesitation, listening to Huang Yueli’s suggestion to betroth her to the newly ascended ninth ranked Array Master Cang Po Yu.","In this way, it had completely ruined her beautiful dreams of flying up the branch!","When Cang Ning Yue thought of this, her heart grew even more melancholic and ill at east as the glare she shot towards Huang Yueli was filled with jealousy and fury!","Why... did Sovereign only like Huang Yueli, not even willing to take another look at anyone else?","Huang Yueli had obviously not treated Sovereign as anything, only indulging in Sovereign’s pampering and fawning, but with no thoughts of being willing to respond to Sovereign!","Sovereign had a legendary reputation for his entire lifetime but why must he chase after this kind of woman, not hesitating to go through life and death for her multiple times, and even at the end, he even..."]},{"number":1675,"title":"Chapter 1675 - For you, Sovereign..... (5)","paragraphs":["The more Cang Ning Yue thought, the more jealous she got as she couldn’t hold it in and just blurted out!","“Grandmaster Huang, although I’m only one Sovereign’s subordinates, but I really cannot take it any longer! Why do you have to return to the Blue Profound Sect, haven’t you got Sovereign into enough misery? He had already gone to such a step for you so can I beg you to leave him a little further and stop trying to harm him! You.... you staying beside Sovereign will only harm him! You totally don’t like him, why must you keep appearing in front of him?”","Huang Yueli’s face was filled with ridicule.","Cang Ning Yue’s little bit of thoughts was something that she was very clear of when she was in her past life.","But there were so many ladies who had openly and secretly admired Mu Chengying whereas Cang Ning Yue merely had a Heavenly Yin physique which was a top rated material for being a bondmaid. Just based on this alone... frankly speaking, Huang Yueli totally couldn’t care less about her.","In her past life, she just casually found a reason to make Mu Chengying marry her off.","This lifetime, she and Li Moying’s heart and mind were interconnected and moreover they had already gotten engaged. So these butterflies who came close to them naturally weren’t of any threat at all.","Huang Yueli originally had intended to teach her a good lesson but whoever knew, upon hearing Cang Ning Yue’s words, she instinctively felt something was amiss.","Huang Yueli couldn’t help but frowned, “Wait, what do you mean? Since when have I ever harmed him? And, it’s not me who appeared in front of him, it’s he himself who kept coming to look for me!”","Cang Ning Yue looked at her puzzled look as she felt even more indignant, feeling unjust for her Sovereign!","Momentarily, she was flushed with jealousy and had forgotten about Li Moying’s warning at the front palace, casting it out of her mind totally!","“Grandmaster Huang, how could you even ask this kind of question? Haven’t you ever thought about why was it that you’d already self-exploded causing your soul and spirit to be scattered but why were you still able to be reborn, moreover still retaining your past life’s memories living a good and proper life until now? Right before you, every single practitioner who had self-exploded had all completely disappeared!”","Huang Yueli went into a blank, “That’s right, this is indeed very strange, but.... could it be that you know something?”","Soul and spirit had been scattered but still having the chance to be reborn.","This was indeed a miraculous thing which had never happened since ancient times.","Ever since she had awoken in Bai Ruoli’s body, she had thought about this multiple times but still wasn’t able to find out any reasons so she could only conclude that it was because she owned the Sky Phoenix Ring, the piece of super God Relic.","However, little phoenix Wang Cai had also indeed mentioned that although it was a God relic, it could only develop its corresponding uses according to Heaven and Earth’s law.","To want to congeal one’s soul and spirit which had already been scattered, it was a heaven defying action and the corresponding price must be paid which was not something that a God Relic could achieve by itself!","Now hearing Cang Ning Yue’s meaning, could it be that... this matter was related to Li Moying?","Huang Yueli frowned and pursued, “Cang Ning Yue, what on earth do you mean? Speak clearly! What exactly happened after I self-exploded in my past life? What did Mu Chengying do? I why... why have I managed to awaken?”","Cang Ning Yue laughed coldly, “You don’t know? You’ve already been reborn for such a long time and even spending so much time with Sovereign but yet you don’t know anything! For you, Sovereign has done so much but you only know how to feign ignorance.....”","The more Huang Yueli listened, the more she felt something was wrong and the ominous premonition in her mind became more distinct.","“I’m not feigning ignorance! But you, tell me directly if you have something on your mind. What’s the purpose of speaking in circles like this?”"]},{"number":1676,"title":"Chapter 1676 - For you, Sovereign..... (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Cang Ning Yue suddenly hesitated for a moment when the words were already by her mouth.","Li Moying’s harsh warning rang by the side of her ears and upon recalling that severe expression, Cang Ning Yue couldn’t help but give a cold shudder.","Huang Yueli saw that she was going to withdraw what she was about to say as her gaze suddenly flashed and lifted up her chin slightly, she glanced sideways at her, “What’s the matter? Don’t dare to say? I think you’re merely starting a rumour!”","“You.... who said I’m starting a rumour? Alright, I’ll speak!” Cang Ning Yue clenched her teeth and she completely pressed her luck!” I’m telling you, sixteen years go after you self-exploded in the Northern Ice Fields, originally your soul and spirit should have dispersed but Sovereign he just nicely.....”","“Cang Ning Yue! What rubbish are you sprouting? Shut your gap up!”","Just as Cang Ning Yue was prepared to tell the truth, a burst of exasperated voice was heard as it harshly stopped her!","Huang Yueli went into a blank and saw Cang Po Jun and Cang Po Yu standing not too far away.","Cang Po Jun strode over quickly as he spoke in a cold tone, “Ning Yue! Can you sprout nonsense about such a matter like this? This is merely a rumour in the country, how dare you even gossip in front of Grandmaster Huang!” Saying that he turned towards Huang Yueli, “Grandmaster Huang, my sincere apologies, please do not take Ning Yue’s nonsense to heart.”","Huang Yueli took a suspicious look at the few of them as her gaze turned even more profound.","She had originally suspected this was Cang Ning Yue’s plot but upon seeing Cang Po Jun’s anxious look, it actually made her believe that there was some shocking inside story and furthermore everyone were trying their best to hide it from her!","Huang Yueli gave a cold ‘hmph’ as she said, “Sir Po Jun, are you trying to trick me? Since this is unfounded ravings, why don’t you allow Guardian Yue to finish her words? What on earth are you trying to hide from me?”","Cang Po Jun frowned slightly but since he was also a peerless top exponent who had experienced huge waves before, he quickly resumed his composure and put on an expression which seemed as though nothing had happened.","“Grandmaster Huang, you’re really thinking too much! Ning Yue has been a little tired recently and she heard those crazy and unfounded rumours from some outsiders hence she spoke blindly in front of you! We really have nothing to hide from you!”","Huang Yueli laughed instead of flying into a rage, “Do you really treat me like an idiot? Cang Ning Yue had said this very clearly earlier that right after I self-exploded during my past life, in order to save me, your Sovereign had done something which you cannot afford to let me know? What matter is it exactly? Speak!”","Huang Yueli was feeling exceptionally anxious inside.","If it was any other matters, there was no absolute need for her to find out the answer but this matter was related to Li Moying!","She was very afraid and very worried, feeling that this man would do something which was irrevocable.","In her past life, Huang Yueli was also a long established peerless top exponent and having stayed beside Mu Chengying for such a long time, the minute she flew into a rage, the aura and prestige that shot out from her had an eighty percent similarity to Mu Chengying’s.","In the few Guardians’ view, all of them uncontrollably gave a bitter cold shudder.","However, Cang Po Jun clenched his fists tightly as he said the same thing through the slits of his teeth, “Grandmaster Huang, you’ve really thought too much, there really isn’t anything special.....”","Huang Yueli gave a cold laugh, “Nothing special? Then let me ask you, I’m obviously the one who self-exploded in the Northern Ice Fields, but why did Mu Chengying also die and even reincarnated along with me? How on earth did he die?”","“This.....” Cang Po Jun was tongue tied.","“Why? Unable to tell me? Then let me ask you again. One who had self-exploded would have their soul and spirit dispersed, never to enter the reincarnation wheel but why is it that I am still able to be reborn?”"]},{"number":1677,"title":"Chapter 1677 - For you, Sovereign..... (7)","paragraphs":["Cang Po Jun was intimidated by her Mu Chengying-alike overbearing presence as the cold sweat on his forehead kept dripping.","But he insisted in his saying, “Grandmaster Huang, there really isn’t anything special. That year after your self-explosion, Sovereign he was devastated and shut himself up in Levitation Floating Castle to cultivate, probably out of the devastation from your death, it led him to go into Qi Deviation.... As for how you had reincarnated and reborn, this is really a miracle which this subordinate is unable to comprehend as well...”","Huang Yueli sneered as she heard his words.","Cang Po Jun was stared at so much by her that he felt guilty as his voice became softer and softer.","Huang Yueli said, “Sir Po Ju should have finished your story right! Then.... will Guardian Yue please explain next?”","Cang Ning Yue’s expression was pale as she withdrew into a corner and when she heard Huang Yueli pointing out her name, she jumped up in fright.","“Wh... What? Grandmaster Huang, this subordinate.... this subordinate.....”","“Haven’t you said so earlier? In order to save me, your Sovereign paid a heavy price for it, what exactly is that price?”","“I.... this.....”","Cang Po Jun’s warning look and immediately shot towards Cang Ning Yue.","Cang Ning Yue’s heart was filled with jealousy and envy but she didn’t dare to tell the truth!","Earlier when she met Huang Yueli at the corridor, she was even younger and outstanding than before. Although she had yet to fully grow up, but she could tell that she would be an exceptional beauty which was not outdone by her past life.","More importantly, in this lifetime, Huang Yueli and Sovereign were each other’s sunshine and from the excitement in meeting him again, Cang Ning Yue had totally let her jealousy rush into her brain.","Hence that was why she jumped out to provoke Huang Yueli!","After all, Huang Yueli’s cultivation was only at the fifth stage realm now, and her ability as compared to her past life was as different as sky and earth! Towards her, Cang Ning Yue wasn’t that fearful of her as compared to in her past life.","But before she could even finish her words, she was interrupted by Cang Po Jun and like a deflated balloon, she momentarily lost the courage to speak out the truth.","If she dared to say the things which she shouldn’t in front of Cang Po Jun, the loyal Cang Po Jun would absolutely tatter on her immediately to the Sovereign and by then, she would die a horrible death with no burial grounds!","Cang Ning Yue was at a loss for moments but in the end she still chose to remain silent.","Cang Po Jun replied, “Grandmaster Huang see, she doesn’t dare to say anything so it looks like she knows she herself is sprouting nonsense not daring to admit to it.”","Huang Yueli could tell that they would never admit to it so momentarily, she couldn’t do anything to them.","If it was in her past life, she would utilise her Piercing Sky Eye technique to make them speak obediently.","Alas, as her cultivation was weaker by quite a lot and the four guardians were all established top exponents with unwavering determination, they were absolutely not someone whom a fifth stage realm practitioner’s eye technique could easily control.","Huang Yueli gave a cold harrumph and said, “Alright, since that’s the case, I’ll go ask your Sovereign personally! I hope you don’t give me a chance to find out that you’re lying to me, otherwise.....”","The three guardian’s backs all felt a cold feeling running down their spines.","This lie would eventually be exposed and by then, they wouldn’t be able to escape the blame!","But yet, no one dared to say a word more.","Anyway, no matter what the result was, as subordinates, they would always be the ones to get into trouble.....","Cang Po Jun bowed and said, “Grandmaster Huang, you’ve thought too much, how would this subordinate dare to lie to you?”","Huang Yueli gave a chuckle and without a word more, she turned around and left.","When Cang Po Jun heard her icy cold chuckle, he turned apprehensive.","Just at this moment, a resounding slap was heard from behind!"]},{"number":1678,"title":"Chapter 1678 - The truth back then (1)","paragraphs":["Cang Po Jun turned back abruptly and his forehead creased.","He saw Cang Po Yu who was standing at the corner silently earlier suddenly turning around and giving a slap to Cang Ning Yue.","“You... you actually slapped me??”","Cang Ning Yue was dazed by the slap as she covered her face and only cried out in shock a moment later.","Mu Chengying had betrothed her to Cang Po Yu twenty years ago so Cang Po Yu was considered her fiancé.","But Cang Po Yu had always been Mr Goody-goody and in the entire Sky Emperor City, he had always been known for not showing any emotions. Moreover he had been very accommodating towards her. No matter what excuses Cang Ning Yue used to muddle through, refusing to get married to him officially, Cang Po Yu had not said a single word about it.","Which was why Cang Ning Yue totally disregarded him as her fiancé and she had never thought that he would make a move towards her!","“Cang Po Yu, you dare to slap me, you actually dare to slap me!!” Cang Ning Yue shrieked out as she tried to hit him back.","However Cang Po Yu’s ability had far surpassed her and he easily gripped onto her wrists.","“Cang Ning Yue! No matter how you made a din usually, I would tolerate you because of the fact that you are the woman whom Sovereign had betrothed to me but that doesn’t mean that I will tolerate anything and everything! You actually dare to come sprout rubbish in front of Grandmaster Huang, who do you think you are? What is your identity? What qualifications do you have?”","“I... I... why can’t I say anything? What I’m saying is the entire truth anyway! Moreover, I indeed don’t deserve Sovereign, but does Huang Yueli deserve him? Ever since Sovereign had been together with her, which time had he not caused himself to be riddled with injuries? Later on... later on he still.... Unfortunately she is still that innocent and so complacent!”","Cang Po Yu laughed coldly as he replied, “So what about it? That is Sovereign’s woman and Sovereign himself is happy to do it! As subordinates, we can only accept it! Do you really think that I don’t know what’s on your mind?”","Cang Ningyue gnashed her teeth and said, “You... what do you mean? Did you really think that you’re my fiancé? That you can control me? Let me tell you, in my eyes, you’re a nobody!”","Cang Po Yu’s expression turned twisted for an instant but very quickly he managed to control himself.","He said in an icy cold voice, “Do you think that I’m willing to marry a wanton woman like you? Rest assured, I will report to Sovereign sooner or later to separate from you. But let me warn you, don’t ever go provoke Grandmaster Huang again. If you cause us to be implicated with you, I will absolutely not let you off!”","Cang Po Jun frowned as well, “That’s right, keep yourself under control! The entire Blue Profound Sect is riddled with internal trouble and outside aggression and is already messy enough! Sovereign had just returned and his ability has yet to reach the peak so he is originally too tired to handle these all, so don’t you come add trouble to him! Really don’t know how the word “death” is written!”","After Cang Ning Yue was berated by the both of them in rounds, she didn’t dare to say a single word more and could only bite on her lips in fury as she lowered her head.","At a place when the both of both could not see, her eyes flashed past a vicious cold glint.","That woman... on what basis did she have to drag down Sovereign? She didn’t have the qualification!","...","At the back of Levitation Sword Palace was a vast sea of Cinnabar Geraniums.","Before nightfall, the setting sun’s rays shone onto those half luminous petals and as the gentle breeze grazed past, the petals moved irregularly, reflecting brilliant radiance lights.","Li Moying sat in the pavilion as he watched the bed of flowers from afar, his lips uncontrollably curling upwards.","This bed of Cinnabar Geraniums was something which Huang Yueli especially liked that year and he had tried ways and means to plant them.","Cinnabar Geraniums were a rare seventh level upper grade ingredient and in the wild, it was a rare sight to be able to spot even one stalk."]},{"number":1679,"title":"Chapter 1679 - The truth back then (2)","paragraphs":["That year, he had expended quite an amount of effort to plant this bed of flowers in an attempt to please Huang Yueli.","Later on, under Liu Buyan’s aid, he tried ways and means and finally succeeded in planting it.","Later on.... Blue Profound Sect had reaped enormous profit from selling the Cinnabar Geranium fruits.","After so many years, this bed of flowers was still retained so perfectly which was out of Li Moying’s expectations.","Thinking of Huang Yueli’s excited expression when she saw this scenery later, he waited in anticipation.","This is the first night after their return to Blue Profound Sect.....","“Li Moying—!”","A young lady’s crisp shouting voice was heard from behind his back.","Li Moying turned his head over as the smile on his lips deepened even further, “Li’er, you’re finally here, what did you talk to Jiyun and the others, why did you take so long.....”","By the time he saw Huang Yueli’s expression, he was dazed, “What’s the matter? Who offended you?”","Huang Yueli’s willowy brows were upright as she shot towards him and grabbed hold of his shirt on his chest.","“Who else could it be? It’s you who have offended me!”","“.... Me?” Li Moying was dazed, “How could it be? I.....”","Huang Yueli impolitely interrupted him, “You what you? I ask you, what matter are you hiding from me? Why is it that you have been acting suspiciously for the entire period of time!”","Li Moying’s expression sunk, could it be that Li’er found out about something? Surely not right? He had obviously just instructed those who knew about this to not let this matter go to her ears.....","His expression appeared to be extremely innocent, “I’m innocent, Li’er, how would I dare to hide anything from you? Who in the entire Soaring Heavens Continent doesn’t know that I’m a slave to my wife and I’ve always been suppressed by my fiancée, the kind who totally don’t even dare to stand up straight.....”","He was shouting for innocence and at the same time stretched out his arm to hug Huang Yueli’s waist, intending to repeat the same trick to use his handsome male trick to shift his fiancée’s attention then later smuggle through this stage.","However, Huang Yueli totally didn’t fall for it this time round. Not only was she not smitten this time round like in the past, instead she pushed him away hard.","“Stop pretending! Since you said it so beautifully and have hidden nothing from me, then let me ask you a few questions, you must answer me honestly! If I find out that you’re lying to me....”","She lowered her voice and her expression sunk.","Li Moying quivered. For an overbearing man like him, fearing nothing at all, yet in front of his beloved woman’s cold face, his heart was shaking with fear and trepidation.","“Alright, then... then go ahead and ask.....”","Huang Yueli started off, “First question, in our past lives after I self-exploded, by right my soul and spirit should have dispersed and I will never be able to enter the reincarnation wheel, why did I successfully reincarnate and reborn? How is this achieved?”","Li Moying’s gaze became profound as he knew that what Huang Yueli was going to ask would definitely be these questions.","It was strange. Earlier when she set off to look for Luo Jiyun and the others, her mood was apparently quite good but why did she suddenly think about all these matters now?","Could it be that someone had defied his orders and spoke about something in front of her?","He had just returned and someone actually dared to pay lip service to him so he absolutely could not tolerate this!","Huang Yueli stared at him intently as she observed his unfathomable expression on his good looking face in detail.","“How is it? Very difficult to answer? Alright, here’s the next question!”","“After I self-exploded, what did you do? Why did you ninth stage realm peak practitioner like you, who should originally have thousands of years of life expectancy suddenly reborn?”"]},{"number":1680,"title":"Chapter 1680 - The truth back then (3)","paragraphs":["“This.... Li’er, why do you.....”","Li Moying was racking his brains on how to reply.","However, Huang Yueli didn’t wait for him to finish talking as she broke him off once again.","“Ha, actually you don’t need to tell me and I also know the answer. Since you’re reborn, that obviously means you’re dead! Continuing from here, there’s the third question, how on earth did you die? Who is able to kill the invincible Sovereign Mu? Or could it be that... you committed suicide?”","“Fourth question, how could you get in touch with Blue Profound Sect so simply? What agreement did you set with the Four Great Guardians? Why do they trust you? This must have something to do with what you did before you died in your past life? What is it exactly??”","Huang Yueli threw out a long chain of questions and her interrogative tone turned more and more flustered.","These questions were something which instinctively popped up in her mind ever since Li Moying regained a portion of his memories and she had been extremely puzzled over it.","But every single time this thread of thought popped up in her mind, Li Moying would try ways and means using mostly his charismatic charm to divert her attention, obviously not intending to tell her about it.","Moreover she felt that the two of them being able to reunite and even falling in love with each other with interconnecting minds was the luckiest thing that had happened. Some things weren’t that urgent to pursue after the truth endlessly as she would finally find out the truth one fine day.","Hence when Li Moying didn’t want to say, she just let it slide.","But this time round, Cang Ning Yue’s words were like a bucket of cold water pouring onto her.","Some fine details which had been skipped and those suspicious pointers which she had never thought about before, upon delving into it deeply, made her heart felt shocked as she thought more and more on this!","That’s right, how would there possibly be such a coincidence in this world. She was ‘coincidentally’ reborn after her soul and spirit dispersed and Mu Chengying ‘coincidentally’ also was reborn after an accident and the two of them were ‘coincidentally’ born in the same country and even engaged?","How would there be so many coincidences under this heavens? If every matter were so coincidental, that would only meant that it was being pre-arranged.","But...Huang Yueli still didn’t get how this man actually managed to do it??","Li Moying looked at the young lady in front of him with great sentiments and that sweet tempting little face was rightly wound as her usually clear bright eyes were filled with worry and heartache for him.","He couldn’t help but give a light sigh, “Li’er, don’t worry.....”","He wanted to hug his fiancée but Huang Yueli immediately took a step backwards.","“How do you expect me not to worry?? Quickly tell me clearly!”","She put on a straight face as her eyes lifted to look at him, obviously meaning that this time round, she would absolutely not give in easily.","Li Moying said, “Li’er, you cannot be like this.....”","However, Huang Yueli was not moved at all.","Li Moying’s heart turned melancholic and at the same time he was certain that Huang Yueli would absolutely not start a fight with him for no reason. Someone had definitely said something to her behind his back!","No matter who it was, causing him to end up in this state where he was unable to explain himself, he would absolutely not allow that person to end up well!","But luckily, though Huang Yueli’s questions were extremely tricky and very difficult to answer, but he had already thought of a plan to deal with this and even prepared a set of model answers. He had just not expected to use it so quickly.","As Li Moying was pondering over this, he headed up once again as he held Huang Yueli’s shoulders.","“Li’er, don’t be too agitated. I’ve never said that I don’t wish to tell you the truth right?”"]},{"number":1681,"title":"Chapter 1681 - The truth back then (4)","paragraphs":["This time, Huang Yueli still wanted to evade his touches but Li Moying didn’t allow her to push him aside as what she wished, but instead pulled her emphatically into his arms, with a posture which didn’t allow her to reject him.","Li Moying’s cultivation was right there and if he really wanted to force himself onto her, there was nothing that Huang Yueli could do about it.","But she remained restless in Li Moying’s arms as she wriggled around.","Li Moying held on tightly as he said, “Actually, it’s not that I really don’t want to say, but.... there are many things that I really can’t totally recall!”","Huang Yueli’s action took a pause, “Can’t remember?”","Li Moying nodded his head and continued, “That’s right, have you forgotten? When we first met, all the matters that had happened in my past life, I totally couldn’t recall it at all! Later on as my interaction with you deepened and with my cultivation increasing continuously, it was when I started to slowly recall what happened then.....”","“But this is a very long process and my memories didn’t come back to me all in one day, but slowly accumulated during each full moon’s night. So the memories in my mind still remain very confused till today. Especially the things which happened after you self-exploded, the amount that I can recall is even lesser....”","“So it’s not that I’m not willing to tell you but those questions that you asked, many of which are something which I’m puzzled as well but no matter how I tried, I just can’t recall them all.”","As Li Moying was saying these, he kept a watchful eye while observing Huang Yueli’s expression.","Seeing his little fiancée frowning slightly with a pensive look and he hurriedly added more.","“But every time I regain my memories, it was always during full moon’s night when my illness acted up. The longer the acting up timing, the more things I will recall. Since we’re already back in Blue Profound Sect, then in future when my illness acts up, you can wait a little longer before you save me, so test if I can remember something faster.....”","“Not allowed!”","Before Li Moying could even finish what he was saying, Huang Yueli jumped right up and shouted out strictly.","“Ughh.....”","Huang Yueli was so exasperated which made Li Moying jump with shock.","Huang Yueli stretched out his hand to pinch his face as she retorted angrily, “Have you forgotten that whenever your illness acts up, each and every single time it is so dangerous?! There are many times whenever it acts up and drags on for a slightly longer time and you’ve almost lost your life! Do you really want to scare me to death? No way, what silly ideas are those! Anyway when your illness acts up, you must tell me immediately and treat it immediately, not even sparing any time to waste!”","“But, my memories.....” Li Moying looked like a little wife who had suffered domestic violence as his tone sounded weak and timid.","Huang Yueli stared at him ferociously, “I don’t believe that you can’t remember a single bit of it! Moreover speaking, if you really can’t recall, there must be other ways to regain your memories! You’re not allowed to take this risk, do you hear me??”","“But I also want to know what happened that year.....”","Huang Yueli gritted her teeth as she hissed, “Anyway, you’re just not allowed to!”","“Then... then I’ll think of other ideas, don’t squabble with me alright?” Li Moying’s eyes flashed past a crafty glint as he intended to work it up and dupe Huang Yueli over this issue.","Whoever knew, Huang Yueli stared at him for a moment and the frustrated expression on her face suddenly became peaceful.","“No way, this matter is just too important, we can’t just let it pass like this! I don’t believe that you really can’t recall anything at all!”"]},{"number":1682,"title":"Chapter 1682 - The truth back then (5)","paragraphs":["Li Moying thought that he had successfully muddled through this so he had not expected Huang Yueli to suddenly pop this sentence out.","His face instantly turned pale, apparently cutting a sorry state.","Having an extremely intelligent fiancée was usually something which made one feel proud but when it came to the time when one was doing something bad, if a woman was too intelligent, the man would get into trouble, for example like what he was going through right now.....","When he really wanted to tell a lie, he was resolutely exposed right there and then.","However Li Moying still refused to admit and persisted in his explanation, “Li’er, you... you’re really framing me! Don’t you believe me at all? Since when have I lied to you?”","His expression of looking wronged did not make Huang Yueli’s heart soften.","Huang Yueli raised her chin up slightly as she immodestly exposed him, “You’ve lied to me so many times! Every time you’re injured or encountered some danger, since when have you not lied to me? Did you really thought that I’m so retarded??”","Li Moying’s face was filled with sweat, why was this little fox so difficult to lie to! This time round what was he supposed to do?","This matter.... he indeed didn’t want Huang Yueli to find out.","After all, there was no use even if she found out. It would only... make her feel upset over nothing.","While Li Moying was still racking his brains, Huang Yueli gave a chilly smile, “Why? Why aren’t you saying a single word? Thinking of how to lie to me later? Have you planned your story already?”","“Ughh.....” Li Moying’s sweat on his forehead was about to drip down!","Li’er was really the woman who knew him the best. Whatever he was thinking, it totally could not escape her eyes.","Meeting Huang Yueli’s eyes which were raging with fury, Li Moying totally couldn’t think of a way out so he could only.... start to act shamelessly!","“Anyway I just forgot about it! I really can’t remember at all! Even if you beat me to death, I also can’t remember so what else do you want me to do? I can’t do anything if you don’t believe in me!”","These words were similar to the kind of explanation that a two timer would use when he had been caught while having an affair. But when it came out of Li Moying’s mouth, it made Huang Yueli not believe him as her eyes turned wide.","Moreover in order to intensify the effect of what he just said, Li Moying directly crossed his arms as he shifted his sight, putting on an uncooperative look.","“Alright, stop being unreasonable! No matter how you argue it’s no use, up to you to believe or not!”","“You.....” Huang Yueli almost threw up blood from anger! She had not expected Li Moying to use such a lowly trick!","Where was the Continent’s number one top expert, cold and merciless, overbearing and resolute? What was the difference between this behaviour and those small young boys who laid on the ground throwing a tantrum to ask for sweets?","He actually threw the target back at her and said she was being unreasonable??","Huang Yueli gave him a ferocious stare, “Alright, you’re really difficult to deal with! Don’t you dare to regret using this kind of attitude on me! The matter that happened that year, I’m sure you’re not the only one who knows about it! If I want to know, I will definitely be able to find it out! I want to see how you are going to keep it from me for my entire lifetime!”","Huang Yueli finished up and turned around walking away angrily!","Li Moying watched her departing figure and his expression slowly sunk down. Who was it who tried to expose the secret which he had tried ways and means to hide it? Could it be that trying to keep it from Huang Yueli was really impossible?","Now, Li’er had already said this so what should he do so that she could stop pursuing this topic.....","The night breeze grazed past that sea of Vermilion Cinnabar flowers causing undulated billowing.","Li Moying looked at the beautiful scenery in front of him but he had no heart to admire it as his brows were tightly knitted together."]},{"number":1683,"title":"Chapter 1683 - The truth back then (6)","paragraphs":["Ever since Huang Yueli and Li Moying quarrelled that day, the both of them entered into a cold war.","Or perhaps it could be put in this way, it was Huang Yueli who started this cold war on her own.","Li Moying knew that he was in the wrong and had been finding ways and means to please his little fiancée. Not only did he enquired solicitously about her well-being, delivering food and drinks over, he also adapted to her interests and tidied up the armament furnace and armament refining room which she had used that year as well as sending various high levelled herbs, as though it was free, to her.","However, Huang Yueli totally ignored him and every single time she saw him, it was always neither hot nor cold. Although it wasn’t to the extent of totally ignoring him, but that chilly cold gaze always made Li Moying’s back turn chilly.","But no matter how many times she rolled her eyes at him, he continued to persevere as his daily task was to please his little fiancée.","This scene made everyone in Levitation Sword Palace extremely surprised.","Sixteen years ago, towards Grandmaster Huang, Sovereign saw, listened and obeyed to everything she said using ways and means to please her. But he was after all the number one top exponent and his character was domineering and overbearing so even if he was chasing after his beloved woman, he would not lower himself that badly.","Whoever knew that the minute the both of them had reincarnated, their way of interaction had changed to this?","Many attendants thought they were dreaming. Was this really their invincible and unexcelled Sovereign?","The Four Great Guardians were actually very clear on what happened. In actual fact, after the fight between Huang Yueli and Li Moying had happened, he immediately sent for them.","Originally Blue Profound Sect had been without a leader for the past sixteen years so even if it were subordinates who were loyal towards Li Moying, they would inevitably slack as they no longer revered and feared Li Moying’s commands in the same way as that year.","But after that day, everyone realised that even though he had changed a shell, he was still that powerful unexcelled number one top expert, who still left everyone revere him totally, not daring to have any bit of resistance!","Those things which Cang Ning Yue had said behind his back were found out very quickly. Li Moying was mad with fury and almost struck her to death on the spot. Later it was Cang Po Yu who stood out to plead for mercy and Li Moying was worried that if Cang Ning Yue suddenly died, it would cause Huang Yueli’s suspicion hence he forcibly spared her life.","But Cang Ning Yue was stripped of the Guardian position and even sent to the punishment hall.","Even Cang Po Jun didn’t know what Cang Ning Yue had experienced there, only knowing that after her return, she had completely restrained herself, not daring to say a single word more. Usually she would just shrink herself and hide in one corner, totally not having the past haughtiness that she had.","All these were secretly done with Li Moying hiding it from Huang Yueli.","But although Huang Yueli didn’t witness it with her own eyes, she still knew what was going on and at the same time, she grew even more indignant.","This man.... creating so many matters out, wasn’t trying to hide it making it more conspicuous??","Did he really treat her as an idiot! She must definitely investigate clearly on what had happened!","Alas, with Cang Ning Yue as a precedence, the other three guardians were even more tight lipped and as they were afraid that they would unintentionally be wormed out facts by her, when they met her, they didn’t even dared to let out a single fart as they remained silent throughout the entire duration.","As for the ordinary attendants in Levitation Sword Palace, Huang Yueli managed to try her Piercing Sky Eye and controlled two of them in an attempt to make them tell the truth.","However ordinary attendants’ knowledge towards this matter was limited and no matter how Huang Yueli asked, she only knew that Mu Chengying was devastated that year after her self-explosion and had always been cooping himself up in Levitation Sword Palace. Later on... Cang Po Jun announced that Sovereign was going into long term closed door cultivation."]},{"number":1684,"title":"Chapter 1684 - Li’er, don’t be angry (1)","paragraphs":["It was till this day when Cang Po Jun brought back Li Moying to Levitation Sword Palace with great fanfare did they realise that their Sovereign wasn’t in closed door cultivation but had been reborn!","Huang Yueli was certain that these two attendants had already told them everything that they knew.","But wasn’t this version exactly the same as the rumours in the entire Soaring Heavens Continent?","If what she wanted was to find out about these, would she need to go question them?","Looked like Li Moying had maintained absolute secrecy that year, other than the few trusted aides beside him, practically no one else knew what had happened.....","To find out the truth, she could only start from himself and his Four Great Guardians.","This was cumbersome.","Ten over days had passed and Huang Yueli still hadn’t thought of any ideas. Of course she was also not appeased and still remained indifferent towards Li Moying.","Finally, even Luo Jiyun sensed the uncommon atmosphere in Levitation Sword Palace as he hurried over to Huang Yueli’s side to mediate.","“Lil Sister-in-law, long time no see, how have you been recently? I’m here to visit you.....”","“Stop the crap, did your Eldest Senior Brother send you here?”","Luo Jiyun just entered the room and met with Huang Yueli’s rolled eyes as he was instantly stuck in his shell.","“Ughh, ha ha, how is that possible? Of course it’s not. I miss lil Sister-in-law so I’m here to pay you a visit.....” Luo Jiyun’s head was filled with sweat. He had not expected to be exposed the minute he reached this place, almost coming to light.","Luckily before he came over, Li Moying had already analysed the possible scenarios and the corresponding methods to deal with it so he was able to react in time and immediately denied it.","Huang Yueli evidently didn’t believe his words as her brows rose and said, “Fine, since you’re not the traitor sent over by Li Moying, then later you’re not allowed to mention anything related to him. Otherwise I’ll send you off immediately!”","Another sweat dripped down from Luo Jiyun’s forehead. This scenario was something that even his Eldest Senior Brother didn’t teach him! If he wasn’t able to mention a single word, how was he supposed to mediate?","He wondered what begrudging thing had his Eldest Senior Brother done to actually make lil Sister-in-law so angry to this extent! Surely it couldn’t be that he was with another woman and was caught by lil Sister-in-law right?","If it really was this, then who on earth should he help?","Luo Jiyun immediately replied, “Won’t mention, won’t mention! I promise that I won’t mention! Sister-in-law you’ve really mistaken me. I’m just here to have a chat with you. You said this before that no matter what problems we meet in Blue Profound Sect, we can seek your help!”","Huang Yueli then nodded her head and said, “Then have a seat!”","She let someone serve them tea and snacks and asked, “How is it, these few days, have you and Mo Yi the rest got used to staying in Blue Profound Sect?”","Luo Jiyun gave a bitter smile and said, “Got used to.... I’m still alright but Brother Mo Yi and the others aren’t in very good condition.....”","Luo Jiyun had obtained the rights to become a direct disciple and adding on to the fact that he was Li moying’s Junior Brother in South Sky Region, hence he was specially permitted to stay in Levitation Sword Palace.","Every single disciple or attendant in Levitation Sword Palace were totally loyal towards Li Moying hence their attitude towards Luo Jiyun was very good as well. Plus the fact that Luo Jiyun’s physique and innate talent were not bad so he quickly adjusted to Blue Profound Sect’s lifestyle.","But it wasn’t the same for Mo Yi and the others.","Even though they were inner disciples but Blue Profound Sect was Soaring Heavens Continent’s number one Sacred Land! Even the most ordinary outer disciple had at least seven grade upper innate talent."]},{"number":1685,"title":"Chapter 1685 - Li’er, don’t be angry (2)","paragraphs":["Whereas Mo Yi and the others were at most sixth grade talent. When they were in Celestial Light Sect, they were considered to have top rated innate talent but in Blue Profound Sect where the strong roamed around like clouds, that was just too pathetic.","These Blue Profound Sect’s disciples naturally wouldn’t be used to seeing that. Based on their low innate talents yet still able to become inner disciples? And the minute they joined the Sect, they were able to learn so many high levelled cultivation methods?","Because of this, many disciples picked against Mo Yi and the others in the open and in the dark, not forgetting mocking and ridicule. The Shadow Guards knew they couldn’t match up hence they didn’t rebuke at all, only working hard and silently cultivating on their own.","What was worse was that according to Blue Profound Sect’s regulations, lowered levelled disciples could issue challenges towards high levelled disciples and the latter weren’t allowed to reject.","The number of challenges they received were endless and as they weren’t allowed to reject, but their ability was far worse off than those challenges so practically every single time they would lose for sure. Not to mention losing a huge amount of fortune and time, they would also get injured frequently.","Luo Jiyun told these to Huang Yueli and later on, he hemmed and hawed as he said, “Lil Sister-in-law, you see... isn’t Brother Mo Yi and the others a little too pitiful? Can we.... Can we get them over to Levitation Sword Palace?”","Huang Yueli took a glance at him and shook her head, “No, we can’t.”","Luo Jiyun was a little disappointed, “But every time I visit Brother Mo Yi and the others, they always end up in a miserable state from the bullying! If this carries on, I’m afraid that not only would they be unable to cultivate and advance, they might even end up getting seriously injured and affect their future cultivation! Actually it really isn’t Brother Mo Yi and the other’s fault for not working hard, but their innate talent and physique is originally not as good as the others so no matter how they work hard, it’s of no use!”","Huang Yueli put down the teacup as she stared at Luo Jiyun and said slowly, “Really? Do you really think in this way? Since their innate talent couldn’t match up to the others then no matter how hard they tried, it is useless?”","“Ughh, isn’t... isn’t it like this? You and Eldest Senior Brother.... Ughh, pui pui pui, I didn’t mention him, didn’t mention him! What I mean to say was that, lil Sister-in-law, isn’t your innate talent outstanding as well hence your cultivation speed is that fast?”","Luo Jiyun casually mentioned “Eldest Senior Brother” three words and immediately received two large eye rolls from Huang Yueli.","In order to stop her from sending him off, he immediately changed his sentence at first instance.","Huang Yueli gave a hmph and said, “I indeed have outstanding luck but not every ninth stage realm peerless top exponents relied on innate talent to succeed, there are some whose innate talent were not very good. For example the leader of the Four Great Guardians Cang Po Jun, when he first started off, he only had fourth grade talent.”","“Huh?? How is that possible??” Luo Jiyun’s eyes immediately turned wide with total disbelief, “Sir Po Jun has preeminent strength and so many ninth grade talented practitioners cannot even be compared to him, how could he possible only have fourth grade talent?”","Huang Yueli said, “This is very common. Your inborn innate talent is merely the starting point but that doesn’t mean to say how far it would lead you to. Real strong exponents do not rely only on outstanding innate talent. Most importantly, they must have enough perseverance and courage, not giving up any chance at all! Innate talent and physique might be hard to change but there’s still chances to improve it.”","“Ah? Really? Innate talent can be raised?”","Huang Yueli nodded, “That’s right, otherwise why would so many people fight head over tails to join the Seven Sacred Lands? It’s just because the Seven Sacred Lands had enough inheritances and resources, even to improve a practitioner’s innate talent and physique! As long as they work hard, they will be able to do anything.”"]},{"number":1686,"title":"Chapter 1686 - Li’er, don’t be angry (3)","paragraphs":["Huang Yueli thought about it for a moment and said, “Help me pass this message to the Shadow Guard brothers that they have a very good opportunity in front of them. Every year end, Blue Profound Sect would enter into a year-end assessment for outer disciples and the content is to climb the Sect’s rear mountain cliff’s Sky Ascension Stairs.”","She paused for a moment, “That’s right, you have to go as well! Direct disciples must all partake in the assessment!”","Luo Jiyun went into a blank as he asked curiously, “Sky Ascension Stairs? What’s that?”","Huang Yueli’s lips curled upwards mysteriously, “There’s no point for me to tell you now, you’ll find out by then. I can only say that since it’s named the Sky Ascension Stairs, that as what the name means, to climb up naturally is as difficult as ascending to the sky.....”","Luo Jiyun anxiously spoke out, “What? Lil Sister-in-law, don’t scare me!”","Huang Yueli rolled her eyes at him, “I’m not scaring you! There are many assessments in Seven Sacred Lands and every one of it is filled with extreme danger which would lead to loss of one’s life easily! But the more difficult the assessment, the minute you pass through it, the more rewards you will obtain! Sky Ascension Stairs assessment rewards are something which is worth everyone to take the risk.”","“Luo Jiyun asked, “Really? What kind of rewards are there?”","Huang Yueli replied, “I heard that the top twenty practitioners in this assessment would obtain a chance to cultivate in the Swordbath Pool.”","“Swordbath Pool? What place is that?” He asked in a daze.","Huang Yueli was speechless, “You don’t even know about this! Seven Sacred Lands all have the historical remains left behind from ancient times, which could aid in lifting the practitioners’ innate talents and physiques under their wings! Otherwise why would they keep on producing so many talents under their wings and how would they have the cheek to be known as the Sacred Land? Swordbath pool is an early historical remains of Blue Profund Sect and also one of the best Seven Great Historical Remains with the best effect in raising innate talents. Moreover those with lower innate talents would get better effects after taking a soak in it.”","Luo Jiyun’s face immediately revealed an overjoyed expression. “There’s such a good thing around! I must immediately tell Brother Mo Yi and the others! I also want to register and take part in it!”","Huang Yueli added, “There are plenty of chances to enter the Swordbath Pool in Blue Profound Sect but most chances come from ranking in terms of absolute power so Mo Yi and the others might not be able to rank up in those events. But the Sky Ascension Stairs assessment are auto adjusted based on the practitioner’s innate talent and is the best opportunity which they have.”","“Pass the message to them, if they aren’t able to grasp such a good opportunity, that would mean that they totally don’t have the conviction to become a top rated practitioner! They also need not stay on to be humiliated in Blue Profound Sect, they might as well return back to South Sky Region earlier! In Celestial Light Sect, they could at least muddle along to be an Elder or something, why bother to stay here!”","Huang Yueli made it sound very harsh but not one sentence were empty words.","Those who were able to become ninth stage realm practitioners indeed had eighth grade talent and above and it was extremely rare and more so based on one’s conviction and perseverance to keep on seeking breakthroughs in life and death occasions, lastly surpassing those talented practitioners to reach the peak.","Luo Jiyun’s cold sweat was trickling down.","“Yes, yes, I know. I will definitely bring these words to them! And I will also work hard, to prepare for the assessment!”","Huang Yueli then nodded her head satisfactorily as she picked up the tea cup once again.","Luo Jiyun also took a mouthful of tea as she looked at Huang Yueli’s expression and said, “That’s right, Sister-in-law, there’s another matter... do you know that after Li Lingchuan and Murong Fei had been brought over to Blue Profound Sect, Eldest Senior Brother... ughh! How were they dealt with?”"]},{"number":1687,"title":"Chapter 1687 - Li’er, don’t be angry (4)","paragraphs":["Luo Jiyun almost said the wrong thing again but luckily Huang Yueli was attracted by the content of his words, hence she totally didn’t notice that he had mentioned about “someone” again.”","“I’m not sure, what happened to them now?” Huang Yueli shook her head.","She naturally knew that Li Moying had brought these two fellows back and absolutely would not spare their lives. There was probably a much more miserable state waiting for them.","However as she entered a cold war the minute she and Li Moying reached Levitation Sword Palace hence regarding this matter, she wouldn’t go and ask him about it.","Luo Jiyun saw that she was hooked and finally heaved a sigh of relief. At the same time he recalled the tricks and standard method which Li Moying had imparted to him before he sent him over.","“.... First tell your sister-in-law about Mo Yi and the others to lower her defence and after she has got into a congenial chat with you, then mention about Li Lingchuan and the others to prove that I’m helping her take care of those people who had bullied her. After this matter is done, she should be feeling much better so take the opportunity to put in a few words for me, and you won’t be chased away!”","Wise and brilliant Sovereign was carefully pondering over his fiancée’s thoughts.","Luo Jiyun was left in the clouds and fog from listening to him and it was until now when he totally couldn’t help but submit to him.","He was indeed Soaring Heavens Continent’s number one top exponent! This kind of set pattern was done in such a winding and complicated method...","“Why? Is there something which isn’t apt to talk about?” Huang Yueli saw that he was in a daze and wrinkled her forehead.","Luo Jiyun immediately regained his sensed and hurriedly replied, “Not that it’s not apt to talk about but I only feel that Eldest Senior.... Ughh! Just that their end was a little too miserable!”","“I heard that, Murong Fei was sent by Eld.... Cough cough.... Transferred to the one of the Seven Sacred Lands Sky Devil Sect’s Elders to be a concubine. I heard that that Elder is already nine hundred over years old and so old that all his teeth have almost dropped out. But yet he was still very prone to sexual attractions and he had at least three to four hundred wives and concubines in his residence! To think that Third Senior Sister had so many young, handsome and peerless talents chasing after her but now she ended up in this state, sigh... after all we are Senior and Junior sister and brother relationship so I’m feeling a little.....”","Huang Yueli looked at Luo Jiyun’s uncomfortable look as her lips twitched.","Sky Devil Sect’s Elder... surely it couldn’t be that old lecher Wei Dakai right?","That fellow had always had a bad reputation. Not only was he a lecher, he had obviously been collecting virgins with outstanding reputation to cultivate a kind of allotment and patching evil skill. All those young ladies who fell into his devil claws all suffered miserably, worse off living than dead!","Murong Fei was not only beautiful, she was also an eighth grade talented genius. This kind of best quality stuff, even Wei Dakai found it hard to get. So she would imagine that if Murong Fei was at his place, she would be “pampered” very much!","Looking at Luo Jiyun’s innocent look, Huang Yueli naturally wouldn’t be so silly to tell him the truth behind.","Apparently, even Li Moying didn’t tell him the exact truth, merely avoiding the heavy topic and mentioned it lightly saying that he married Murong Fei to someone as a concubine.","If this soft hearted child knew that they were so vicious in their handlings, he would probably faint from shock.....","Huang Yueli then asked curiously, “Alright I understand her situation now, then how about Li Lingchuan?”","Hearing this question, Luo Jiyun was slightly puzzled as he frowned slightly.","“Speaking of Li Lingchuan, I find it strange! By right, he had personally plotted to murder El.... Ughh.... many things and even poured dirty water onto El... ughh.... poured dirty water to put the blame on others so by right he should end up in a worse off state! But Eldest Senior Brother only sent him to the rear mountain to be a hard labourer for Elder Quan who was responsible for refining pills.”"]},{"number":1688,"title":"Chapter 1688 - Li’er, don’t be angry (5)","paragraphs":["Luo Jiyun really couldn’t think it through since when had his Eldest Senior Brother became so merciful? To actually let the main culprit off so easily?","If it was said that Luo Jiyun was still feeling sympathetic towards Murong Fei that Senior Sister, then towards Li Lingchuan, he totally could not feel any sympathy as he couldn’t wait to slap this scum who had plotted his Eldest Senior Brother multiple times to death!","Huang Yueli however nodded her head while pondering over this.","“Oh.... So it’s like this.....”","Blue Profound Sect’s Alchemy Hall’s Elder Quan was a veteran eighth ranked Pill Master. Although he didn’t have Liu Buyan’s miraculous skills, but his competence was profound and he had been established for a long time.","Only problem was as he was passionate about researching various new prescriptions, even prescribing various poisons to the extent of being smitten. Every single time a new medication was refined successfully, he would always find someone to test the effects of it. These kinds of medication testing slaves were mostly slaves bought from various slave markets.","These slaves were mostly ordinary people who weren’t even practitioners, not to mention outstanding high levelled practitioners with outstanding innate talent but unfortunately all of Elder Quan’s prescriptions were all pinpointed towards high levelled practitioners. In this way, there was no way to test out the actual effect of the medication.","With Li Lingchuan this eighth grade talent as a medication slave, Elder Quan would be elated!","Following that, he would definitely be even more loyal towards Li Moying.","“He indeed is the man who I, Huang Yueli, had chosen. Indeed vicious, merciless and black-bellied.... Heh heh, I like....” Huang Yueli mumbled to herself as she gave a sly smile exposing her sharp little tiger fangs.","Luo Jiyun’s curiosity had reached the peak as he couldn’t help but leaned over to ask, “Lil Sister-in-law, you know what’s going on right? Quickly tell me, what is Eldest Senior Brother trying to do?”","Huang Yueli heard that and lightly grazed him with a sight, “Why? You really want to know?”","Luo Jiyun nodded his head hard, “Of course, I’m curious to death! Lil Sister-in-law, please tell me!”","Huang Yueli gave a slight smile, “Then alright.... I won’t tell you on purpose!”","Luo Jiyun’s smile which had just surfaced instantly froze on his face, “AH—? Wh... WHY?”","Huang Yueli spoke chillingly, “When you first entered the door, what did I tell you? Hmm? As long as you mentioned that stinky man’s name, I will immediately make you leave! Tell me how many times have you mentioned his name earlier? Hmm? Still not going to hurry and scram?”","Luo Jiyun’s face immediately appeared a dazed expression as his eyes turned wide, as though he didn’t hear her clearly.","It took quite a while before he managed to react and plead with a bitter face, “Lil Sister-in-law, how could you be like this? I really didn’t do it intentionally and not purposely mentioned... mentioning about ‘someone’...”","Huang Yueli gave a cold humpf, “Who cares if you’re intentional or unintentional, you can leave now!”","Luo Jiyun hurriedly added, “Lil Sister-in-law, don’t be in a hurry to chase me away, just let me say two more sentences, just two more sentences!”","Huang Yueli’s big bright eyes swept towards him, “Two sentences is it? Then just say!”","Luo Jiyun had originally thought that Eldest Senior Brother’s plan was really useful and lil Sister-in-law had really acted out according to his plans. After hearing him talk about Mo Yi and Li Lingchuan’s news, he was about to enter the most important stage next!","Whoever knew that Huang Yueli actually tore down the bridge after crossing it. She treated him to tea to find out the news and after hearing it all, she immediately swept him out of her door!"]},{"number":1689,"title":"Chapter 1689 - Too hard on himself (1)","paragraphs":["How could it turn out like this?","The routine he leant was obviously not meant to be like this?","How could lil Sister-in-law now go according to the standard pattern to throw out her tiles? This was an obvious violation!","Luo Jiyun really wanted to cry but had no tears but Huang Yueli was so black bellied and so sinister, he totally could not beat her! Arguing with her was the most unwise thing to do under this Heavens.","He could only grasp onto the last “two sentences” chance, attempting to plead for Eldest Senior Brother.","“Lil Sister-in -law, Eldest Senior Brother said he really didn’t lie to you, his heartfelt feelings are something which heaven and earth can prove, he... AH—!”","Luo Jiyun spoke quickly as he tried to grasp onto time to speak a few more sentences but whoever knew that he had just started when Huang Yueli’s right hand waved and a surging burst of Profound Energy gushed towards him!","Although Luo Jiyun’s cultivation was a little higher by a few levels than Huang Yueli’s but Huang Yueli’s innate talent and combat experience was much higher than him by a far chunk.","If they really started to cross hands, Luo Jiyun was totally not her match and in an instant, he was thrown out of the door like a bag of trash!","After a resounding ‘bam’ on the ground, the door shut tightly in front of him.","Huang Yueli’s sweet melodious voice drifted out from inside, “You’re done with two sentence, Junior Brother Luo, have a safe journey and I won’t be seeing you off!”","Luo Jiyun hurriedly pounced over to knock on the door, “Lil Sister-in-law, don’t.... don’t be like this! Let me say a few more sentences! Eldest Senior Brother he really.... aiyo!”","Luo Jiyun’s fist had just reached the door when he sensed an irresistible powerful force coming from the door and he hadn’t even had time to stabilize his body while retreating and directly flew out as he fell onto the flower bed at the entrance.","“Eldest Senior Brother, why am I in such a miserable state.... Not only did Lil Sister-in-law not listen to me finish my words, she also set up an unknown mechanism at the door which sent me flying in an instance...”","Luo Jiyun climbed up from the mud with an ashen face as he turned around and went to look for his Eldest Senior Brother to complain tearfully.","Huang Yueli’s mechanism was mainly set up for defence and its offensive attack wasn’t strong at all hence he wasn’t really hurt, only falling head first into the mud which had just recently been set with fertilizers so not only was he filthy from head to toe, that smell.... Don’t mention just how horrible it was!","Luo Jiyun ran all the way and almost every Levitation Sword Palace’s disciples who he passed by all raised their eyebrows as they looked at him.","Li Moying looked at his sorry state and silently sighed.","“Jiyun, it’s been hard on you. Your Sister-in-law is not biased against you but she’s simply too angry! You’d better not go find her recently and just like what your Sister-in-law said, it’s best that you go into closed door cultivation during this period of time to prepare for the Sky Ascension Stairs assessment! I will personally give you some pointers with regards to cultivation.”","To be able to get Soaring Heavens Continent’s number one top exponent’s personal teaching this was something which every young practitioner in the entire Continent had dreamt of!","Luo Jiyun instantly forgot all his troubles as he left happily.","Li Moying’s inner heart grew even graver.","He knew clearly that Luo Jiyun took on the punishment for him and Li’er’s anger had still not dissipated. Moreover she had seen through his plot to make use of Luo Jiyun in an attempt to mediate for them hence she intentionally taught the both of them a lesson.","He had not expected that even Luo Jiyun could not lower Li’er’s defence... looked like she was set on finding out the truth!","Could it be that, he really needed to tell her.....","No way!","This thought had just surfaced and it was thoroughly refuted by Li Moying!","If he told her the truth, she would definitely.... No, unless he was about to die, otherwise he would never tell her the truth!","Since that’s the case then there would only be one way..."]},{"number":1690,"title":"Chapter 1690 - Too hard on himself (2)","paragraphs":["Another few days went by but Huang Yueli and Li Moying’s relationship did not ease up at all.","Levitation Sword Palace’s atmosphere grew tenser and tenser and every disciple and attendants in the palace were all shaking with fear and trepidation, deeply worried that if they were careless for that one second, they would anger Grandmaster Huang and affect their Sovereign who was on the verge of exploding.","In the past, everyone hoped to get the chance to get closer to Sovereign, even if it was just to take a look at his handsome countenance, it was an extremely glorious matter to them.","But now the minute they heard that the Sovereign was appearing, everyone ran faster away than the rabbits!","It really was because Li Moying’s recent temper was too terrifying. Even his most trusted Eldest Guardian Cang Po Jun was faulted at every turn daily thus being berated badly, not to mention other people.","Whereas Cang Po Jun knew that he had done something wrong and as the Eldest Guardian, right after Sovereign had instructed multiple times to not reveal the secret, yet it was emitted to future Sovereigness’s ears the minute he turned his head so regarding this matter, he could not escape censure.","So everyday there were plenty of people who would intentionally or unintentionally go over to visit Huang Yueli in an attempt to make the two of them reconcile.","Alas, Huang Yueli had set her heart on this, absolutely not giving in at all!","It was another dark nightfall and Huang Yueli was cultivating alone in her room.","Her cultivation had also increased swiftly when she was in the Cloudy Qilin Mystic Region. Although it had not improved as exaggeratedly as Li Moying, Cloudy Qilin Clan’s genius, but she had already advanced into fifth stage realm peak and after a long time of stabilization, she would be able to breakthrough to sixth stage realm anytime.","Just as she congealed her breathing and senses to concentrate on cultivating, her room door suddenly came a series of knocking sounds.","“Lil Sister-in-law! Lil Sister-in-law! Are you there? Something bad has happened!”","Luo Jiyun was shouting outside her door with a hint of sobbing tone mixed in his voice.","Huang Yueli’s cultivation was interrupted but before she could start to get upset, she could tell that there was something wrong with his tone and immediately she turned anxious and jumped right up from her bed, running over to open the door.","“What’s the matter? It’s so late already, what on earth has happened?”","Luo Jiyun was panting hard to catch his breath as he panted heavily and pointed his finger towards the night sky.","“Lil.... Lil Sister-in-law, cough cough, have you forgotten? Tonight... tonight is full moon’s night.....”","Huang Yueli raised her head and a full moon shone brightly in their eyes and her complexion immediately turned pale!","That’s right, no wonder she had been in a daze for the entire day, somewhat feeling that something was ill at ease with the feeling that she seemed to have forgotten about something important... so today was full moon’s night!","She actually.... forgot about such an important matter!","Huang Yueli turned around and sped towards Li Moying’s bedroom!","As she was running, she kept blaming herself in her heart.","Tonight was full moon’s night, such an important matter like this and she had forgotten about it totally! It was all because of her only caring about the cold war with Li Moying and forgetting to pay attention to the condition of his body!","Speaking of that, Li Moying’s Soul Detachment Illness all relied on Liu Buyan’s prescription and it was already totally unable to be suppressed. Every time it acted up, the reaction would be more intense than the previous time!","But as long as she was beside him, it would be suppressed very quickly and if it wasn’t for that, he would.....","Hence, she wasn’t able to pinpoint if the current Li Moying’s state was considered to be turning for the better or for the worse.","But she was very sure on one point, and that was every single full moon’s night, she must stay by Li Moying’s side securely, no exceptions for that even if the two of them were in the middle of a cold war!"]},{"number":1691,"title":"Chapter 1691 - Too hard on himself (3)","paragraphs":["Huang Yueli had just turned into the corridor when she saw a blinding flash in the sky, ripping the silence of the dark night.","That bolt of lightning carried a shocking amount of enormous energy as it directly struck in the open sky above Levitation Sword Palace.","A loud sound rang as ten thousand swords clashed!","Levitation Sword Palace’s sword array was originally a thunder attributed ancient array and right now under the invigoration of powerful electric currents, each sword flew up straight into the sky as it refracted the electric currents which kept on raining down in the sky as the clashing whizzed with a cold murderous aura!","Huang Yueli saw that and pursed her lips as she ran even faster than before.","A large number of disciples had already gathered in Levitation Sword Palace’s front courtyard and everyone wore a shocked and surprised expression.","On seeing Huang Yueli coming over, the disciples all naturally split up a path for her.","Huang Yueli flew nearer and saw Li Moying had already been surrounded by electric currents with a pair of lightning wings and his wings had already expanded over ten feet as his entire body hovered in mid-air. His good looking face was layered with iciness and aloofness, radiating a greenish purple glint and in his sharp eyes, lightning flashed and every single time someone met his eyes, it made that person start shaking with fear and trepidation.","His thunder region was much more powerful than before and the electric currents were closely distributed around the surroundings and it was very hard to find any gaps which could fit in.","Outside the thunder region, Cang Po Jun, Cang Po Yu and Cang Po Hun as well as Li Moying’s three other trusted Elders had already surrounded him in an attempt to pacify him, or were trying to find a way to suppress the explosive energy from his body.","However, Li Moying’s current destructive power was just too shockingly huge and it had even surpassed his past life’s peak condition. Although all the six practitioners who were present were all ninth stage realm peak Sky Chart’s strong exponents, but in front of Li Moying’s thunder region, they were totally unable to withstand a single blow from him as all of them were struck till their faces turned ashen, some even sustaining serious internal injury.","“Big Brother, I... I can’t hold on any longer.... Sovereign is just too powerful.... didn’t they say he had just entered the ninth stage realm and had not even reached his past life’s potential? Why is he this powerful?” Cang Po Hun was sent flying once again by the electric currents as his face was filled with bruises and he clutched the injured area on his chest as he couldn’t help but throw up a mouthful of blood.","Cang Po Jun’s condition wasn’t in any better state than his as his expression was totally gloomy.","“I heard from Master Luo that Sovereign’s Soul Detachment Illness had started fifteen years ago and it would act up every full moon’s night. When it acts up, he would practically be in a state where he lost all his senses but his potential would rise rapidly reaching to ninth stage realm peak!”","“What the ghost, this is ninth stage realm peak potential? I’m also in ninth stage realm peak, but why am I still being beaten until my teeth have all fallen out?” Cang Po Hun couldn’t help himself as he was about to spill vulgarities.","Cang Po Jun shook his head and said, “How can Sovereign’s ninth stage realm peak be the same as yours? Moreover, according to Master Luo’s interpretation, as Sovereign’s cultivation keeps increasing, the destructive power of his Soul Detachment Illness would keep increasing as well. It could be said that every single time it would get stronger and stronger...”","Cang Po hun wanted to spew vulgarities again, “Damnit, that in this case every single time Sovereign would act up once and every single time it acts up, it would be more powerful than before? He’s only in ninth stage realm first level now and already so abnormally strong. By the time he reaches ninth stage realm peak, wouldn’t he be able to strike us all to ash when we meet face to face?”","“Po Hun, mind your words! How can you speak of Sovereign’s right and wrongs?” Cang Po Jun frowned in displeasure as he barked at him harshly.","Cang Po Hun also realised that he had said the wrong things and hurriedly shut his mouth.","However after he was sent flying once again, he still couldn’t help but started grumbling once again."]},{"number":1692,"title":"Chapter 1692 - Too hard on himself (4)","paragraphs":["“This really is.... really is too ridiculously strong! What should we do next? How long will Sovereign act up until? If this went on for too long, I’m afraid that Levitation Sword Palace’s Sword Array would be damaged by him!”","Cang Po Hun’s words weren’t gibberish because right on top of everyone’s heads, ten thousand long swords kept on hacking at the electric currents giving off a horrifying murderous aura causing shocking electric currents retractions which probably the entire Soaring Heavens Continents was able to see.","Such a huge commotion from Blue Profound Sect, they wondered what the other large powerhouses would think when they saw this?","But this matter was no longer something on Cang Po Jun and the other’s minds.","The most important matter now was how to make Li Moying resume back to normality as soon as possible.","Cang Po Jun said, “Levitation Sword Palace’s Sword Array is passed down since ancient times and in the past, it even had resistance against tenth stage realm practitioners who joined hands to attack it so how could it be so easily broken! What is of urgency right now is to hurry up and think of an idea to let Sovereign calm down. Master Luo mentioned that the ability that Sovereign is displaying right now is not his actual ability but obtained via burning his life source. The longer it drags on, the more damage it would cause to his body! It might even cause his cultivation to drop.”","Hearing this, everyone apparently became extremely nervous.","“Then... then what should we do?”","“We can’t even pass ten miles near to Sovereign and if we went near him, we probably hadn’t even touched the corner of his sleeve and we will be struck into ash!”","“But this cannot drag on, otherwise, shall we join hands and risk our lives to head up?”","Just as everyone was bearing a look which faced death with equanimity, preparing to risk their lives, Cang Po Yu suddenly spoke out.","“Wait a minute, everyone don’t be hasty!”","“Second Brother, do you have an idea??” Cang Po Hun went up close with a joyous look.","Everyone knew that Cang Po Yu was Blue Profound Sect’s strategist and when Li Moying wasn’t around, he contributed his ideas for various matters.","Cang Po Yu muttered, “It’s actually now considered a method... but I’d very much like to know that when Master Luo and the others were in the Sect, whenever they met Sovereign acting up, how did they handle this? Theoretically speaking, everyone in their Sect along with the Elders added up, they shouldn’t be stronger than any one of us but they actually could pacify Sovereign for so many years?”","Can Po Hun said, “What’s so strange about that. Hadn’t Big Brother already said that whenever Sovereign acts up, his might would rise according to his cultivation and in the past, he shouldn’t be this powerful right?”","Cang Po Yu shook his head, “You can put it in this way. Since this is a process of gradually strengthening up, and Sovereign who had already broke through to ninth stage realm, then the past few times he acted up should at least be eighth stage realm so his might would definitely be very shocking...”","When he said that, it caused the rest to delve into deep thoughts.","Everyone present were stunned but after thinking through this for a mere couple of seconds, everyone expressed their reconciliation towards this.","“That’s right, what Guardian Yu said is correct!”","“Looks like in order to pacify Sovereign, there should be some tactic involved and we cannot just go head on.”","“Master Luo would definitely know something, hurry go get him over here to question him!”","Cang Po Hun was extremely anxious, “That’s right, quickly go grab that little brat for interrogation, strange, where did he go? Why can’t we even see his shadow?”","Cang Po Jun said, “When Master Luo heard that Sovereign’s illness acted up, he just told me a few simple words and ran off!”","“Ran off? That’s his Eldest Senior Brother!” Cang Po Hun’s eyes popped out.","Cang Po Jun was indifferent, “Then what should we do? He’s only in the sixth stage realm and if he were to head up here, he’d probably be long dead. I’ll go get something to look for him...”"]},{"number":1693,"title":"Chapter 1693 - Too hard on himself (5)","paragraphs":["Cang Po Jun’s words had not ended when he heard a burst of flustered shuffling of footsteps behind him.","For someone to come over at this kind of timing, it was definitely some matter of urgency.","The few of them hurriedly turned around and gazed at the person approaching.","On one look, Cang Po Hun cried out in shock, “Grandmaster Huang, you.... why have you come here?”","Cang Po Jun also bore a face of shock as he immediately stepped upwards to comfort her, “Grandmaster Huang, this isn’t a place which you should stay at. This subordinate knows that Sovereign is in trouble and you must be very worried but this place is simply too dangerous but your cultivation is no longer the same as in your past life. If you get hurt accidentally, how should this subordinate explain to Sect Master.....”","He persuaded her earnestly and halfway through his sentence, he saw Huang Yueli doing a special step as her figure was swift like a hurricane and in no time, she had reached them.","“Stop the nonsense, there’s no time, move aside quickly!”","Huang Yueli seemed as though she didn’t hear his advice as she went around him, thinking of continuing to move forward.","Cang Po Jun didn’t expect her to not stop at all, just charging straight to meet her doom and he was so scared that he hurried over to pull her back, “Grandmaster Huang, you.... please don’t be rash! You can’t go over to that side!”","Alas, his reaction was still too slow as Huang Yueli’s Agility Dance Steps was a God Realm cultivation method which was best at evasion. Cang Po Jun had momentarily been distracted and was passed by easily by her as she slipped past the defence lock and with a flash, her slender figure in the white flowing dress headed straight into the thunder region with no second thoughts.","“Heavens! Grandmaster Huang, quickly come back!”","“Danger! The Sovereign has now lost his consciousness and don’t recognise anyone at all!”","“What should we do? She... she’s already gone in! It’s.... it’s too late!”","No one had expected this situation to happen and basically no one was able to stop her in time.","In that instance, everyone who was present had a complexion which flushed much paler than a dead person!","Who didn’t knew that Huang Yueli’s existence in Li Moying’s heart was much more important than his own life by a thousand hundred times and usually if Huang Yueli suffered a slight injury, he would fly into a rage to murder that person who hurt her!","Now they actually didn’t manage to keep a tight rein on her, allowing her to dash into the thunder region! She would probably end up being struck to death by Sovereign personally!","By the time Sovereign regained his consciousness, that result.... It was simply something which no one dared to imagine!","Cang Po Jun swiftly clenched his teeth, “What are you still hesitating for? Everyone let’s move up! We must try our utmost best to resist the thunder region, even if we are seriously injured, we must still try to get Grandmaster Huang out! I’ll countdown from three, everyone be prepared! Three, Two.....”","Cang Po Jun was really about to faint!","Sovereign having such an illness with symptoms which was like a ticking bomb on his, wasn’t it all because of that year.... For Grandmaster Huang...","Now Huang Yueli was still acting like this! Forget about the usual cold war with Sovereign, but when something happened, she was actually this irrational. Did she think that she was still that year’s Young Palace Lord from Mythical Flame Palace with exceptional ability?","Her cultivation was only at fifth stage realm and that would be equivalent to sending herself to her doom!","The current scenario was already very messy and she actually came to add more trouble!","“...–!”","“Wa... Wait a minute, all of you don’t... don’t be rash! St...stop please!”","Just as the few of them were about to risk their lives to save her, Luo Jiyun who was left behind by Huang Yueli had finally managed to chase up to them.","He ran over in a most urgent manner but his speed simply could not be compared to Huang Yueli.","Cang Po Jun and the others ignored his cries because the situation was just too urgent and if they were late by just one breath, Huang Yueli could possibly be struck into dregs!"]},{"number":1694,"title":"Chapter 1694 - Too hard on himself (6)","paragraphs":["As the circumstances were dire, Luo Jiyun couldn’t care about anything else as he speedily rushed upwards to block himself in front of everyone.","Cang Po Jun and the others almost crashed into him and all of them bore an angry look.","“What on earth are you trying to do? Why did you suddenly rush out like that?”","“Master Luo, we’re on our way to save someone! Haven’t you seen that Grandmaster Huang is almost about to die?”","“Quick, ignore him, let’s grab hold of time!”","On seeing everyone about to rush over again, Luo Jiyun quickly shouted out, “Don’t go in, Sister-in-law rushed in to save people! Everyone please be assured, as long as Sister-in-law is here, she can settle this easily so all of you need not be so agitated and so nervous, just wait a little while and you’ll know!”","Everyone’s actions took a pause as they gazed towards him in doubt.","Luo Jiyun saw that they were finally listening to what he was saying as he hurriedly gave a cough and speedily explained.","“Brother Guardians, you need not be so nervous. Don’t think that Eldest Senior Brother looked so terrifying right now as though he really doesn’t recognise anyone but he’s still able to recognise Sister-in-law! He will absolutely not hurt Sister-in-law so rest your heart!”","Cang Po Hun frowned, apparently still not believing in him, “Are you certain? This matter cannot be based on mere guessing! Sovereign really doesn’t recognise anyone at all! The few of us Guardians have been by his side for at least twenty years but hadn’t he also just punched us madly earlier?”","Cang Po Jun added, “When Sovereign is conscious, of course he wouldn’t bear to hurt even one finger of Grandmaster Huang, but now it’s totally different!”","Luo Jiyun wanted to add something more when he suddenly heard Cang Po Yu giving off a “Huh”.","Everyone turned their heads towards him.","Cang Po Yu pointed to the centre of the thunder region and said in a deep voice, “Grandmaster’s moves are really not simple, she actually ran over so quickly to the thunder region’s centre and also precisely evaded every single bolt of lightning not sustaining any injuries at all.... this is something that even I can’t achieve.....”","“What? So fast? Finished, finished, we’re all finished, we really can’t make it in time!” Cang Po Hun gave an anguished wail as his face flushed so white that it was scary!","He could also predict that by tomorrow, the miserable state of him being skinned alive with all his tendons pulled out!","Can Po Jun also had the same terrible expression but when he took a careful look at the thunder region’s centre, he gave an astonished expression.","Luo Jiyun simply said complacently, “See that? It’s exactly what I said! Sister-in-law she is indeed alright! Although Eldest Senior Brother is unconscious, but in the inner depths of his heart, he will never forget that Lil Sister-in-law is the most important person to him, even more important than his own life!”","By this time, Cang Po Hun had also seen the situation in the thunder region’s centre as well as he said in disbelief, “It’s actually..... actually true! Grandmaster Huang has already reached Sovereign’s side, this.... shouldn’t she have been electrocuted by now? She’s actually really alright?? Is Sovereign conscious or unconscious?”","Everyone had the same question on their minds as they watched this scene silently. They deeply felt in their hearts that no matter how much time had passed, the two of them had already experienced the test of reincarnation but Huang Yueli’s place in Li Moying’s heart was getting deeper and deeper.","Luo Jiyun finally completely relaxed.","He smiled and said, “Alright, now we’ll depend on Lil Sister-in-law! In the past when we were in South Sky Region, no matter how badly Eldest Senior Brother acted up, as long as Lil Sister-in-law is around, he would be cured immediately! Take a careful look, he’s about to.....”"]},{"number":1695,"title":"Chapter 1695 - Too hard on himself (7)","paragraphs":["Luo Jiyun spoke in a light tone as his heart already had a conclusion, feeling that his own mission was already completed and all they had to do was to wait till Lil Sister-in-law and Eldest Senior Brother perform some hot scene then they could officially end their job.","Cang Po Jun and the others had no choice but to admit that Luo Jiyun knew the situation clearer than them so they all believed his words and followed his vision as their eyes grew wide, putting all their concentration into the thunder region’s centre.","But whoever knew that the few of them kept staring at Huang Yueli and Li Moying for half a day but they didn’t see the predicted scene where the electric currents stopped. On the contrary, when Huang Yueli hugged Li Moying’s waist and said a few words, Li Moying’s expression suddenly underwent a change!","Immediately following that, Huang Yueli was thrown aside by him.","The thunder in the sky kept on landing down and this time, it was even more intense than before!","Every single palace in Levitation Sword Palace were built with extremely solid ninth tier material and was impenetrable but under this kind of rampaging electricity shocks repeated torture, minute cracks started to appear.","Cang Po Jun and the others were too near to them and as they were caught unaware, they were suddenly struck by a fluctuating strong gush of energy in their faces and every single one of them without any exception were all sent flying, as they suffered blue black all over once again.","Cang Po Jun climbed up from the ground and rubbed his bruised back and immediately started clamouring.","“Master Luo, are you telling a lie to humour us? Didn’t you say that when Grandmaster Huang is here, everything will be resolved? I think instead of resolving it, the situation took a turn for the worse instead!”","Luo Jiyun’s cultivation was the weakest and so he suffered the worst when he fell.","Not only did he break three rubs, his internal injury was also very serious as he spat out several mouthfuls of blood in mid-air when he was flying out.","He forcibly propped up his body as he sat up a little and looked towards the thunder region.","Under blinding bluish purple electric currents, Huang Yueli’s lucid and elegant little face was filled with a shocked and speechless expression, apparently unable to accept this truth as well.","But she merely hesitated for a moment and immediately got up as she tried her best to go near to Li Moying once again.","However, Li Moying totally didn’t give her any chance to go near him. In that pair of cold and stern profound pupils, no feelings could be detected as only soul stirring electric currents kept flickering.","Huang Yueli merely got nearer by a few steps and was quaked away by him.","Moreover, every single time he avoided her, the intensity of the electric currents would increase by another fold, as it’s destructive power became even more shocking!","The ringing of thunder and sword clashing sounds penetrated each other mutually and resounded together as the sky above Levitation Sword Palace became louder and louder, the vibration from the ground became more and more intense!","As though the entire sword array would explode any time!","Luo Jiyun was completely dazed by this scene as well, so much that he had even forgotten about the pain caused by the heavy injuries on his body as his eyes popped out wide while staring straight ahead, at the same time shaking his head as he kept muttering to himself.","“Impossible.... It shouldn’t be.... How did it turn out to be in this way? This had never happened before?”","Cang Po Hun cried out in exasperation, “Now you’re saying that it’s impossible and shouldn’t be! What should we do now! Just look at Sovereign’s current state, his expression has already turned green. This Profound Energy exhaustion simply means he’s over drafting his life! He originally already couldn’t live for much longer.....”","“Shut your mouth!” Cang Po Jun suddenly opened his mouth and stopped him in a harsh tone.","Cang Po Hun abruptly realised that he had said the wrong thing and immediately shut his mouth."]},{"number":1696,"title":"Chapter 1696 - Too hard on himself (8)","paragraphs":["Luckily, Luo Jiyun was already in a frenzy and totally didn’t notice what Cang Po Hun said, only caring about tangling with himself.","“Why did it become like this? I really didn’t lie to you all! In the past as long as Lil Sister-in-law is here, she has never failed! Moreover she only needed the time to burn one incense stick and would be able to make Eldest Senior Brother quieten down. Why is it that today.....”","Cang Po Hun met Cang Po Jun’s berating gaze as he hung his head low.","But very quickly, he couldn’t endure the silence and said, “What should we do now? Sovereign’s condition looks really too dangerous and I feel that anytime he might possibly... possibly.....”","The crowd threw their alarmed and worried gazes together at the same time towards the thunder region.","Cang Po Hun frowned, “This is difficult, earlier we already couldn’t suppress Sovereign when his illness acted up. Now.... I reckon that even if we joint hands together, we might be turned into charcoal.....”","Everyone present was Li Moying’s most loyal subordinate and no one would care only about saving their own skins and were most willing to sacrifice themselves for their Sovereign!","But now the problem was no matter how willing they were to give up their lives, they weren’t able to stop Li Moying even for a little bit!","Such a feeling of utter helplessness shrouded everyone, making them feel a deep sense of despondency.","Cang Po Hun’s heart was burning with anxiety, “But, surely we can’t allow Sovereign to just continue acting up like this right? The amount of Profound Energy that he is exhausting is increasing.... I’m afraid that he will not be able to hang on until dawn before he, he.... moreover, since he had never acted up this seriously before, then.....no one knows if he will totally stop when dawn breaks or not.....”","Cang Po Jun clenched his teeth and said, “All of you don’t move, let me go in first! If I can make Sovereign stop for just a moment, then you will have a chance to control him!”","“Brother Po Jun, you... what are you trying to do??” Cang Po Hun cried out in alarm!","Wanting to stop Li Moying in this state was something which Cang Po Jun couldn’t possibly do!","The only way is to self-explode.....","“No way, Big Brother, you cannot do this!” Cang Po Hun instantly reacted and jumped out to top him.","Cang Po Jun spoke with a grave expression, “Then how? Do you have any alternative ways?”","“No, but.....”","But he could not bear to witness Cang Po Jun, whom he treated like his own sibling, to self-explode like this!","Just as the both of them were in a deadlock, Cang Po Yu walked over and spoke with a deep voice, “Big Brother, don’t be so rash.”","Cang Po Jun frowned, “Even you also cannot differentiate the severity of the situation? From the moment we started to be a Guardian, we vowed to Heaven that we would be able to give up everything for Sovereign!”","Cang Po Yu shook his head and said, “If there is really such a need, I naturally wouldn’t stop Big Brother, but.... it hasn’t reached that moment yet!”","Cang Po Jun looked at him puzzledly, “What do you mean?”","Cang Po Yu pointed towards the thunder region and said, “Haven’t you noticed it already? Although Sovereign kept pushing Grandmaster Huang away refusing to let her go near him, but Grandmaster Huang is still in good condition! If it was anyone else who was standing so near such a powerful thunder attributed region, even if Sovereign didn’t intentionally attack that person, he would have turned into a charred corpse by now!”","Hearing what he said, everyone then realised that the situation really wasn’t as bad as what they had imagined."]},{"number":1697,"title":"Chapter 1697 - Too hard on himself (9)","paragraphs":["Huang Yueli was right in the centre of the thunder region with an anxious and panic stricken expression as she followed behind Li Moying rightly. She was just short of hugging his legs to plead, totally like a pitiful little fox which was cruelly abandoned.","However, no matter how pitiful she looked, no one could overlook the fact that there was not even a slight sign of injury on her.","Cang Po Jun and the others were tongue tied when they saw this, “This.... what situation is this considered as?”","Luo Jiyun’s twisted face due to the pain finally surfaced a smile, “I said this before, as long as Sister-in-law is here, there wouldn’t be any issue right?”","No one had any free time to answer him as everyone stared intently at the duo standing in the centre of the thunder region.","This..... was really considered ok?","...","Standing in the centre of the thunder region, Huang Yueli was even more anxious than others by a hundred times.","She simply couldn’t understand just what happened today?","Originally she had hurried over smoothly and when she ran over next to Li Moying’s side, she discovered that although he seemed a little weak, but in totality his situation was still alright as she secretly heaved a sigh of relief, thinking that she only needed to pacify him.","Whoever knew that just when she was about to pull the man over to force a kiss on him, even before her fingers had reached his robe, he actually casted her aside immediately.","Initially, Huang Yueli thought that Li Moying had done that unintentionally or perhaps he had not noticed that she was here hence she intentionally rerouted to his front preparing to give him a hug filled with love.","But this wasn’t of any use at all.","Li Moying’s electric current filled eyes grazed past her slightly with a pained expression beneath his eyes and immediately following that, his brows furrowed tightly and he flicked his sleeves as he pushed her aside once again!","“Hey—!”","Huang Yueli was caught off guard and was thrown aside once again as her butt landed on the ground once again.","This time, Huang Yueli was certain that this man had definitely seen her clearly but yet he still pushed her aside!","Just what was going on? Surely it cannot be that while this man’s Soul Detachment Illness was acting up, he still remembered the cold war between them and was still angry, still acting tsundere right??","What was wrong with him? Did he need to be so childish! And like he was throwing rubbish, mercilessly casting her aside without any thoughts!","Huang Yueli’s expression turned slightly green.","If it was usual times, she who was pampered rotten by him might just sneer and Li Moying like that. But now in this situation, looking at Li Moying’s face which was turning paler by the second, there was no indignance in her heart, only heartache.","Huang Yueli climbed up from the ground once again and got close to Li Moying.","She used her pitiful large eyes in an attempt to soften this man.","“Moying, you... don’t be angry anymore alright, I won’t quarrel with you, ok? You must be feeling terrible right now, your head is painful, you are totally lethargic but yet cannot stop right? Relax a little and be obedient, let me give you a kiss and.....”","“Argh—!”","Huang Yueli’s eyes grew wide as she could not believe that she had once again been casted aside yet again!","Although this time, Li Moying had put in extra attention to the amount of strength hence she didn’t fall down, but.... he had still pushed her aside!","Huang Yueli was so angry that she stomped her feet crying in anxiety and indignance, “Li Moying! Can you stop using your own body as a joke! Is this time to be angry with me now? Do you know how terrible your face looks right now? If this carries on, your body will definitely not be able to take it!”"]},{"number":1698,"title":"Chapter 1698 - Too hard on himself (10)","paragraphs":["However, Li Moying didn’t have any reaction, not even looking her straight in the eyes.","On the contrary, the surrounding thunder attributed energy which gathered around him became even more condensed and even more powerful! Surging thunder attributed Profound Energy kept on gushing towards him!","Bursting sounds of electricity continued crackling in the sky.","Huang Yueli could tell distinctively that with each strike of lightning landing in the sky, Li Moying’s complexion turned miserably pale at a visible speed.","His complexion was originally very fair but at this moment, he became even paler to the extent of almost becoming transparent as the greenish veins under his skin all seemed to be surfacing.","Huang Yueli didn’t have any time to consider what was wrong with him as she hurriedly pounced over once again.","In the end.... she was still casted aside.","Huang Yueli climbed up once again and on seeing Li Moying’s thunder wings spreading out once again as he gradually floated into the sky, she was flustered and exasperated as she rushed over to grab his heels, tugging him downwards onto the ground.","Li Moying repeated the same tricks, wanting to cast her aside once again.","However, Huang Yueli had made enough preparations this time round as she gathered all the Profound Energy in her hands to resist against Li Moying’s thunder attribute Profound Energy, insisting on grabbing onto him and refusing to loosen her grip.","“Li Moying, how long are you going into a frenzy for! Are you tired of living? Please regain a little bit of your consciousness, do you really not recognise who I am anymore??”","A severe emotionless pair of eyes swept past her face coldly as the profound dark pupils flashed past a cold glint.","“Let go!”","Following Li Moying’s gloomy voice, Huang Yueli felt the impact emitting from her hands abruptly raising in one straight line up! Bursts of exploding thunder attributed energy were emitted into her body, as though it was going to break her wrists into several segments!","Huang Yueli frowned in pain, her fingers had already turned pale and crooked from the pain but she still refused to loosen her grip.","“I won’t let go.. Moying, you... you come down, hear.... Did you hear me?!”","Huang Yueli’s cultivation was too far apart from Li Moying’s and although she had already tried her fullest to resist against it, but she still had no way to go up against such an overbearing thunder attributed Profound Energy from flooding in as it charged against her meridians.","She sensed a turbulence in her chest as though she would throw up blood any second and when she spoke, her teeth were chattering non-stop.","Li Moying’s mind was extremely disorderly and all the electric currents which gathered on him seemed to have struck onto the top of his head. That kind of pain which kept on emitting from the soul made him totally unable to reflect and could only follow his instinct to keep on venting, as though this was the only way for him to lessen his pain.","But when his vision fell onto Huang Yueli’s pained expression on her face, his heart suddenly jolted!","An indescribable sourish feeling gushed up in his heart.","Li Moying’s body shook and he subconsciously retracted the Profound Energy which he had diverged totally out of his own instincts.","Even though his mind was groggy and messed up, but he just didn’t want to make this young lass’ face have that kind of painful expression.","The pressure on Huang Yueli’s hand suddenly lessened.","Her heart leapt with joy as she thought that her persistence had finally yielded effects and Li Moying had finally regained consciousness, recognising who she was.","She hurriedly said, “Moying, alright, alright.... I know you feel very terrible so right now, keep your thunder wings and land on the ground.... Slowly.....”","She was saying that carefully as she continued to tug Li Moying downwards while observing the expression on his face carefully, prepared to use her skills as a female lecher to lay her claws on him."]},{"number":1699,"title":"Chapter 1699 - Too hard on himself (11)","paragraphs":["Li Moying followed her movement and slowly descended a little.","But suddenly, his brows creased vigorously as an intense pain shot right from his head!","Li Moying clutched his head with both hands as he moaned out, “ARGH.....”","Huang Yueli’s expression changed abruptly as she cried out in anxiety and worry, “Moying, what’s wrong? Quick.....”","However, Li Moying’s pained expression was becoming clearer by the minute as he hugged his head with might and the cold sweat on his forehead kept dripping, followed by the increasing intensity of the Profound Energy from his body!","Powerful matchless thunder attributed Profound Energy was injected suddenly from Huang Yueli’s arm, charging right into her meridians causing her expression to turn white immediately!","The crowd outside the thunder region all cried out in shock when they saw that!","“No good! Grandmaster Huang’s expression doesn’t bode well, it looks like she’s suffered internal injury!”","“How could this be? Master Luo, haven’t you said that Sovereign will definitely not hurt Grandmaster Huang?”","“We’re done for this time round, what should we do?”","Just as everyone was at a loss, Huang Yueli’s expression slowly resumed back to normal.","She sensed that right after that burst of sudden charge, Li Moying seemed to have detected that something was not right and gradually controlled his rampaging Profound Energy.","Although he was still moaning while hugging his head, under such a miserable situation, he was still trying his best to control himself not to hurt his beloved woman.","Huang Yueli looked at his green-white countenance and bit her lips and she decided to press her luck!","Her right hand waved and several pieces of Immortal Binding Rope flew out, coiling it onto Li Moying’s body and in an instance, Li Moying was tied up securely by the ropes, rendering him immovable.","Huang Yueli took the chance to retract her hands, pulling him towards the ground!","She was very clear that no matter how secure the Immortal Binding Rope was, it couldn’t possibly be able to bind a peerless top expert like Li Moying, so she could only take advantage of the fact that he wasn’t paying attention to slightly control him for a few breaths of time.","But this bit of time should be enough!","Taking the instance where Li Moying had lost his balance, Huang Yueli tipped her toes slightly and jumped up as her arms wrapped around his neck and leaned in towards his face!","This was really a forced kiss!","The few outside the thunder region were completely shocked and Cang Po Hun couldn’t even say a single word as he stuttered, “This, this, this.... what is Grandmaster Huang doing? She’s too, too, too..... too anxious already.....”","Luo Jiyun explained with slight embarrassment, “Every single time they must do this, as long as... ughh, they’ve kissed, Eldest Senior Brother would return back to normal....”","“But.....” Cang Po Hun stared at the duo and his brows creased slightly, “Are you certain? Sovereign seems as though he will rather die than to comply?”","This scene, no matter how they looked at it, it was especially awkward...","Huang Yueli had completely thrown her face away as she directly played the role of an evil sheep pouncing towards the wolf, preparing to lay Li Moying down.","But she had totally not expected that when she was about to reach that pale thin lips, Li Moying suddenly turned his head away to avoid her kiss, causing her to kiss his face instead.","Huang Yueli was stunned but immediately stretched out her hand to grab Li Moying’s chin in an attempt to turn his face back.","However, Li Moying refused to go according to her wishes as he even grabbed on to her slender waist, hoping to pull her off from him.","Huang Yueli was so angry that she couldn’t help but pinched him secretly as she retorted angrily, “What is this? Just let me kiss you once, will you die!? Your innocence has long been ruined in This Lady’s hands, still pretending to be some chaste upright man!”"]},{"number":1700,"title":"Chapter 1700 - Too hard on himself (12)","paragraphs":["Li Moying’s tightly creased brows seemed to sooth a little as his dazed sight gradually gathered, meeting her pair of large eyes which seemed to be brimming with tears.","“Don’t.... no.... just.... just a little more.....”","Li Moying slowly pushed out these few words as his deep voice held a trembling tone, as though his breath was floating.","If it wasn’t for the fact that Huang Yueli was so close to him, she totally couldn’t hear what he was saying.","Huang Yueli plastered up to him urgently and asked anxiously, “What are you saying? Wait for a while?? Do you know that you’re about to lose your life! How long are you going into a frenzy for??”","When Li Moying heard that crisp and anxious voice, smelled the sweet and familiar fragrance, his mind regained clear headedness for that one instance, recalling the matter which he kept on reminding himself before he acted up...","“Just... just a little more.... let me.... me recall.... recall the matters..... in the past.....”","Li Moying said intermittently.","Huang Yueli was originally slightly dazed but not too long later, a thought arose in her mind. That shocking guess made her tremble violently.","Surely not.... Impossible right...","“You.... speak clearly! What are you trying to do? What matters in the past? What you’re saying, surely it’s not... the matters in our past lives?”","Li Moying looked at her deeply as his panting became even more severe.","“Just wait.... Wait a moment more... I am about... about to recall.....”","His voice became softer and the surrounding thunder attributed energy became even more uncontrollable as the entire Levitation Sword Palace rang with continuous lightning strikes as it started to shake!","For a moment, Huang Yueli felt her entire body turning chilly, even her heart was about to stop.","“You.... you actually.... for this kind of thing! Damn it! I really deserve to die!”","Huang Yueli finally understood why Li Moying insisted on holding on like that, refusing to let her control his illness!","Because it was only when his Soul Detachment Illness acted up will he regain his memories, recalling what happened in his past life! He was so insistent on holding on, only to regain more memories of their past!","Thinking of this, Huang Yueli’s inner heart’s self-blame had reached the limit.","She recalled the reason why she was in a cold war with Li Moying for this period of time, which was because she suspected Li. Moying for not telling her what happened in their past lives! Li Moying had tried to explain to her numerous times but she wouldn’t believe in his explanation, insisting that it was because Li Moying was lying to her!","She had even set a last ultimatum to this man that if he still refused to divulge what happened in his past life after she self-exploded, then she would break off the engagement with him!","Whereas now, Li Moying didn’t care if he was expending his life source just to force himself to recall the matters which happened in his past life, wasn’t it exactly because of the threat which she had said to him?","It seemed that he really couldn’t remember what happened in his past life, and not lying to her! Whereas the petty her actually kept on suspecting the man who loved her deeply, even forcing him to take this half dead step!","Huang Yueli was feeling both guilty and heartache as the rim of her eyes suddenly turned red.","“Moying, stop thinking! Stop thinking already! I don’t want to know already!”","She choked as she tried her best to hug the man’s neck, pleading with him.","However, Li Moying insistently moved his head aside, “No... No way, I have to.... have to recall!”","Huang Yueli’s head was buried in his chest as she missed the deep scheming glint in Li Moying’s eyes."]}]);
